window.KMD=window.KMD||{};KMD.content={"subs":[{"id":"init","title":"Module load, probe & device init","short":"How the driver comes alive","tag":"both","color":"#6e7781","purpose":"<p>The driver is a Linux <strong>kernel module</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/module\">kernel module</a>) called <code>mali_kbase</code>. Loading it registers a <strong>platform driver</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/platform-driver\">platform driver</a>). When the kernel finds a matching GPU node in the <strong>device tree</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/device-tree\">device tree</a>) it calls the driver's <code>probe</code> function. Probe builds one <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/266\"><code>struct kbase_device</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@1083\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:1083\">mali_kbase_defs.h:1083</a>)</span>, the object that represents one GPU, by running an ordered table of init steps.</p>\n<p>The design is <strong>table-driven</strong>. Instead of a long function with many <code>goto</code> error labels, each step is an entry <code>{init, term, err_mes}</code> in an array:</p>\n<ul><li><code>dev_init[]</code> for the device: <span class=\"inref\">JM table</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c@215\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:215\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:215</a>)</span> and <span class=\"inref\">CSF table</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c@279\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c:279\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c:279</a>)</span>.</li><li><code>context_init[]</code> for each context (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/context\">Contexts (per-process GPU state)</a>).</li></ul>\n<p>If step <em>i</em> fails, every earlier step's <code>term</code> runs in reverse order (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1446\"><code>kbase_device_term_partial()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c@284\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:284\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:284</a>)</span>).</p>","how":"<ol><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2113\"><code>kbase_driver_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@6238\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6238\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6238</a>)</span> registers the platform driver (<span class=\"inref\">platform_driver_register()</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@6251\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6251\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6251</a>)</span>).</li><li>The kernel matches the DT <code>compatible</code> string against <span class=\"inref\">kbase_dt_ids</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@6216\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6216\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6216</a>)</span> and calls <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2107\"><code>kbase_platform_device_probe()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@5954\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5954\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5954</a>)</span>.</li><li>Probe allocates the device (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1450\"><code>kbase_device_alloc()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c@72\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c:72\">device/mali_kbase_device.c:72</a>)</span>) and calls <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1448\"><code>kbase_device_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c@299\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:299\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:299</a>)</span> (JM) or <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1427\"><code>kbase_device_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c@361\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c:361\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c:361</a>)</span> (CSF). These walk <code>dev_init[]</code>.</li><li>Important steps, in order:<ul><li>IRQ lookup (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1927\"><code>kbase_get_irqs()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@479\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:479\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:479</a>)</span>) and register mapping (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2066\"><code>registers_map()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@4514\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4514\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4514</a>)</span>).</li><li>Clocks and regulators (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2072\"><code>power_control_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@4654\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4654\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4654</a>)</span>).</li><li>IRQ install (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1478\"><code>kbase_device_early_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c@487\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c:487\">device/mali_kbase_device.c:487</a>)</span>).</li><li>Address-space bookkeeping (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2122\"><code>kbase_ctx_sched_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c@46\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:46\">mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:46</a>)</span>) and memory (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2488\"><code>kbase_mem_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@198\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:198\">mali_kbase_mem.c:198</a>)</span>).</li><li>Hardware counters (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwcnt\">Hardware performance counters</a>).</li><li>The backend late init, which powers up the GPU (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1438\"><code>kbase_backend_late_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c@56\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:56\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:56</a>)</span>).</li><li>debugfs and sysfs.</li><li>Finally <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1472\"><code>kbase_device_misc_register()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c@443\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c:443\">device/mali_kbase_device.c:443</a>)</span>, which creates <code>/dev/maliN</code>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>CSF only:</strong> the MCU firmware is <em>not</em> loaded during probe. It is loaded the first time a process opens the device (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1430\"><code>kbase_device_firmware_init_once()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c@469\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c:469\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c:469</a>)</span>). See <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/open\">Userspace opens the device and creates a context</a>.</li></ol>\n<p>Removal is the mirror image: <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2104\"><code>kbase_platform_device_remove()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@5911\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5911\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5911</a>)</span> → <code>kbase_device_term()</code>.</p>","locking":"<ul><li><code>kbase_probe_mutex</code> (a file-static mutex in <code>mali_kbase_core_linux.c</code>) serializes probe (<span class=\"inref\">mutex_lock(&amp;kbase_probe_mutex)</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@5977\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5977\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5977</a>)</span>). It only exists on kernels ≥ 5.3.</li><li><code>kbdev-&gt;fw_load_lock</code> makes the one-time firmware load race-free when several processes open the device at once (<span class=\"inref\">lock taken here</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c@473\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c:473\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c:473</a>)</span>).</li></ul>","talks":"<p>Almost every other subsystem plugs into the init table: <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/platform\">Platform integration (DT, clocks, regulators, memory groups)</a>, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwaccess\">Register access, GPU properties &amp; interrupts</a>, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mem\">Memory management</a>, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/ctxsched\">Address-space scheduling</a>, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a>, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwcnt\">Hardware performance counters</a>, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/trace\">Tracing, debugfs &amp; debug aids</a> and <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/uapi\">Userspace interface (fops, ioctl, mmap, sysfs)</a>. On CSF it also includes <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csffw\">CSF firmware &amp; host interface</a> (<code>kbase_csf_early_init</code>/<code>kbase_csf_late_init</code>).</p>","debug":"<ul><li>Each init step has an error message string. A failing probe prints <code>\"&lt;message&gt; error = &lt;errno&gt;\"</code> from <span class=\"inref\">this dev_err</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c@314\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:314\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:314</a>)</span>.</li><li><code>-EPROBE_DEFER</code> (for example a regulator that is not ready yet) is not treated as a failure; the kernel retries probe later (<span class=\"inref\">EPROBE_DEFER branch</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@5982\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5982\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5982</a>)</span>).</li><li>On success the kernel log shows <code>Probed as mali0</code>.</li></ul>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[266,"The per-GPU object. Most driver state hangs off it."],[144,"One row of the init table."],[232,"Register window and IRQs found by the platform."]],"fns":[[[2113],""],[[2107],""],[[1448],""],[[1427],""],[[1438],""],[[1414],""],[[1472],""],[[1430],""],[[2104],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"When is the CSF firmware image loaded?","o":["In module_init","In probe","On the first open() of /dev/maliN","On the first job submission"],"a":2,"e":"<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1938\"><code>kbase_open()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@738\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:738\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:738</a>)</span> calls <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1430\"><code>kbase_device_firmware_init_once()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c@469\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c:469\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_csf.c:469</a>)</span>, which loads the firmware only if <code>csf.firmware_inited</code> is false.</p>"},{"q":"Step 7 of <code>dev_init[]</code> fails. What runs?","o":["Nothing; the module stays half-initialized","The term functions of steps 6..0, in reverse order","All term functions in the table","Only step 7's term function"],"a":1,"e":"<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1446\"><code>kbase_device_term_partial()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c@284\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:284\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:284</a>)</span> walks <code>while (i-- &gt; 0)</code> and calls <code>dev_init[i].term</code>.</p>"},{"q":"Which call makes <code>/dev/mali0</code> appear?","o":["kbase_sysfs_init","kbase_device_misc_register","platform_driver_register","kbase_open"],"a":1,"e":"<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1472\"><code>kbase_device_misc_register()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c@443\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c:443\">device/mali_kbase_device.c:443</a>)</span> registers a misc character device.</p>"}],"locks":[]},{"id":"platform","title":"Platform integration (DT, clocks, regulators, memory groups)","short":"Glue between the generic driver and a specific SoC","tag":"both","color":"#8250df","purpose":"<p>The same driver runs on many <strong>SoCs</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/soc\">SoC</a>). Anything SoC-specific lives behind a small set of hooks:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Device tree properties:</strong> registers, interrupts, clocks, <code>operating-points-v2</code>, <code>power-policy</code>, <code>firmware-name</code> and so on. They are documented in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/arm,mali-midgard.yaml\"><code>Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/arm,mali-midgard.yaml</code></a>.</li><li><strong>Platform callbacks:</strong> <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/227\"><code>struct kbase_pm_callback_conf</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_config.h@164\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_config.h:164\">mali_kbase_config.h:164</a>)</span> (power on/off, suspend, runtime PM) and <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/226\"><code>struct kbase_platform_funcs_conf</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_config.h@52\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_config.h:52\">mali_kbase_config.h:52</a>)</span> (init/term and per-context hooks). The default <code>devicetree</code> platform supplies <span class=\"inref\">pm_callbacks</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/devicetree/mali_kbase_runtime_pm.c@271\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/devicetree/mali_kbase_runtime_pm.c:271\">platform/devicetree/mali_kbase_runtime_pm.c:271</a>)</span>. <code>MALI_PLATFORM_NAME</code> (<a class=\"cfgref\" href=\"#/config/CONFIG_MALI_PLATFORM_NAME\"><code>CONFIG_MALI_PLATFORM_NAME</code></a>) selects which <code>platform/&lt;name&gt;/</code> directory is compiled.</li><li><strong>Memory group manager (MGM):</strong> a separate kernel module (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/base/arm/memory_group_manager/memory_group_manager.c\"><code>drivers/base/arm/memory_group_manager/memory_group_manager.c</code></a>) through which every physical GPU page is allocated (<code>mgm_alloc_page</code>). If none is supplied the driver falls back to the built-in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_native_mgm.c\"><code>mali_kbase_native_mgm.c</code></a>.</li><li><strong>Priority control manager (PCM):</strong> optional; lets the platform cap the GPU scheduling priority a process may ask for.</li></ul>","how":"<ul><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2072\"><code>power_control_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@4654\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4654\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4654</a>)</span> gets the regulators (<span class=\"inref\">regulator_get_optional</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@4698\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4698\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4698</a>)</span>) and clocks (<span class=\"inref\">of_clk_get</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@4730\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4730\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4730</a>)</span>).</li><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1907\"><code>kbasep_platform_device_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_config.c@26\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_config.c:26\">mali_kbase_config.c:26</a>)</span> calls the platform's <code>platform_init_func</code>, if one exists.</li><li>Power on/off ends up in the platform callbacks. For example <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3109\"><code>pm_callback_power_on()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/devicetree/mali_kbase_runtime_pm.c@77\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/devicetree/mali_kbase_runtime_pm.c:77\">platform/devicetree/mali_kbase_runtime_pm.c:77</a>)</span> enables the clocks and regulators on the reference devicetree platform.</li><li>The MGM is looked up from DT in <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1478\"><code>kbase_device_early_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c@487\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c:487\">device/mali_kbase_device.c:487</a>)</span> / the memory group manager init (see <code>mgm_dev</code>). Physical pages are then allocated through <code>kbdev-&gt;mgm_dev-&gt;ops.mgm_alloc_page</code> in <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2734\"><code>kbase_mem_alloc_page()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c@267\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c:267\">mali_kbase_mem_pool.c:267</a>)</span>.</li><li><strong>PBHA</strong> (Page-Based Hardware Attributes) settings from DT are applied by <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pbha.c\"><code>mali_kbase_pbha.c</code></a>.</li></ul>","locking":"<p>Platform callbacks are called with the PM lock or <code>hwaccess_lock</code> held by the <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a> code; see each callback's comment in <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/227\"><code>struct kbase_pm_callback_conf</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_config.h@164\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_config.h:164\">mali_kbase_config.h:164</a>)</span>.</p>","talks":"<p><a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a> calls the power callbacks, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mem\">Memory management</a> allocates through the MGM, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/dvfs\">DVFS, devfreq &amp; thermal (IPA)</a> uses the clocks/regulators found here, and <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/init\">Module load, probe &amp; device init</a> runs <code>power_control_init</code> early.</p>","debug":"<p>If probe fails with <code>Power control initialization failed</code>, check the DT <code>clocks</code>/<code><em>-supply</code> properties. <code>vexpress</em></code> platforms use the fake platform device (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_platform_fake.c\"><code>mali_kbase_platform_fake.c</code></a>) for systems without DT.</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[227,""],[226,""],[382,"MGM instance; <code>ops</code> holds allocation callbacks"],[381,""]],"fns":[[[2072],""],[[2073],""],[[1907],""],[[2734],""],[[3109],""],[[3110],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"Which component actually hands out physical pages for GPU memory?","o":["The GPU firmware","The memory group manager's mgm_alloc_page","dma_alloc_coherent in probe","The MMU"],"a":1,"e":"<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2734\"><code>kbase_mem_alloc_page()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c@267\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c:267\">mali_kbase_mem_pool.c:267</a>)</span> calls <code>kbdev-&gt;mgm_dev-&gt;ops.mgm_alloc_page</code>.</p>"},{"q":"Where does the driver find the GPU's clocks?","o":["Hard-coded in Kconfig","Device tree, via of_clk_get","From the firmware","From sysfs"],"a":1,"e":"<p><span class=\"inref\">power_control_init uses of_clk_get</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@4730\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4730\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4730</a>)</span>.</p>"}],"locks":[]},{"id":"hwaccess","title":"Register access, GPU properties & interrupts","short":"Talking to the hardware: registers, IRQs, GPU ID","tag":"both","color":"#cf222e","purpose":"<p>The GPU is controlled through <strong>memory-mapped registers</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/mmio\">MMIO</a>). This driver does not use raw offsets everywhere. Registers are named by <strong>enums</strong> (e.g. <code>GPU_CONTROL__GPU_ID</code>), and a per-GPU-version <strong>register map</strong> turns each enum into an address and an access-width/permission flag. The map is built in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hw_access/regmap/mali_kbase_regmap_jm.c\"><code>hw_access/regmap/mali_kbase_regmap_jm.c</code></a> / <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hw_access/regmap/mali_kbase_regmap_csf.c\"><code>hw_access/regmap/mali_kbase_regmap_csf.c</code></a> for each architecture version. The site's <a href=\"#/registers\">register reference</a> is generated from those files.</p>\n<p>Accessors: <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1502\"><code>kbase_reg_read32()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hw_access/backend/mali_kbase_hw_access_real_hw.c@39\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hw_access/backend/mali_kbase_hw_access_real_hw.c:39\">hw_access/backend/mali_kbase_hw_access_real_hw.c:39</a>)</span>, <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1505\"><code>kbase_reg_write32()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hw_access/backend/mali_kbase_hw_access_real_hw.c@117\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hw_access/backend/mali_kbase_hw_access_real_hw.c:117\">hw_access/backend/mali_kbase_hw_access_real_hw.c:117</a>)</span> and their 64-bit forms. With <code>CONFIG_MALI_NO_MALI</code> the same API is implemented by a software model (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hw_access/backend/mali_kbase_hw_access_model_linux.c\"><code>hw_access/backend/mali_kbase_hw_access_model_linux.c</code></a>).</p>\n<p>At probe time the driver reads the GPU's ID and feature registers into <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/294\"><code>struct kbase_gpu_props</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_gpuprops_types.h@228\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_gpuprops_types.h:228\">mali_kbase_gpuprops_types.h:228</a>)</span> (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2263\"><code>kbase_gpuprops_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_gpuprops.c@279\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_gpuprops.c:279\">mali_kbase_gpuprops.c:279</a>)</span>). It also applies <strong>hardware workarounds</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/hw-issue\">HW issue / workaround</a>) listed in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_base_hwconfig_issues.h\"><code>mali_base_hwconfig_issues.h</code></a>.</p>","how":"<p><strong>Interrupts.</strong> The GPU has three interrupt sources, JOB, MMU and GPU, wired as three IRQ lines or as one shared line.</p>\n<ul><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/136\"><code>kbase_install_interrupts()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c@448\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:448\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:448</a>)</span> requests them.</li><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/129\"><code>kbase_get_interrupt_handler()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c@180\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:180\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:180</a>)</span> picks either the per-line handlers or <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/128\"><code>kbase_combined_irq_handler()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c@164\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:164\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:164</a>)</span>.</li><li>Every handler follows the same pattern:<ul><li>Take <code>hwaccess_lock</code>.</li><li>Return <code>IRQ_NONE</code> if the GPU is powered off (<span class=\"inref\">check</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c@49\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:49\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:49</a>)</span>).</li><li>Read the <code>*_IRQ_STATUS</code> register.</li><li>Dispatch:</li><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/124\"><code>kbase_job_irq_handler()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c@41\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:41\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:41</a>)</span> → <code>kbase_job_done</code> (JM) / <code>kbase_csf_interrupt</code> (CSF)</li><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/125\"><code>kbase_mmu_irq_handler()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c@76\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:76\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:76</a>)</span> → <code>kbase_mmu_interrupt</code></li><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/126\"><code>kbase_gpuonly_irq_handler()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c@111\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:111\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:111</a>)</span> → <code>kbase_gpu_interrupt</code></li></ul></li><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1437\"><code>kbase_gpu_interrupt()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_hw_jm.c@61\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_hw_jm.c:61\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_hw_jm.c:61</a>)</span> / <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1434\"><code>kbase_gpu_interrupt()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_hw_csf.c@88\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_hw_csf.c:88\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_hw_csf.c:88</a>)</span> handle power-transition-done, cache-clean-done, reset-completed and GPU faults.</li></ul>","locking":"<ul><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_device::hwaccess_lock\"><code>kbase_device::hwaccess_lock</code></a> is an IRQ-safe spinlock and the most used lock in the driver. It protects hardware-facing state (job slots, AS registers, power state). It is held in every top-half IRQ handler.</li><li>Register-history tracking for debugging (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_regs_history_debugfs.c\"><code>mali_kbase_regs_history_debugfs.c</code></a>) has its own lock.</li></ul>","talks":"<p>Every subsystem that touches hardware goes through this layer: <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a> (power registers), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mmu\">GPU MMU: page tables, flushes, faults</a> (AS registers), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/jm\">Job Manager back-end (JD / JS / job slots)</a> (job slot registers), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csffw\">CSF firmware &amp; host interface</a> (doorbells, MCU control), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwcnt\">Hardware performance counters</a>.</p>","debug":"<ul><li>debugfs <code>regs_history</code> shows recent register accesses (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_regs_history_debugfs.c\"><code>mali_kbase_regs_history_debugfs.c</code></a>).</li><li>sysfs <code>gpuinfo</code> prints the decoded GPU name/ID.</li><li>With <code>CONFIG_MALI_DEBUG</code> + real HW, <code>kbase_validate_interrupts</code> tests IRQ wiring at probe (<span class=\"inref\">call site</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c@78\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:78\">device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c:78</a>)</span>).</li></ul>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[294,""],[232,""]],"fns":[[[1502],""],[[1505],""],[[136],""],[[124],""],[[125],""],[[126],""],[[1437],""],[[1434],""],[[2263],""],[[1516],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"An IRQ fires while the GPU is powered off. What does the JOB IRQ handler return?","o":["IRQ_HANDLED","IRQ_NONE","It resets the GPU","IRQ_WAKE_THREAD"],"a":1,"e":"<p>See <span class=\"inref\">the early return</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c@52\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:52\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:52</a>)</span>. The IRQ line may be shared with other devices, so the handler must not claim it.</p>"},{"q":"How does the driver know the address of <code>GPU_CONTROL__GPU_ID</code>?","o":["A #define offset","A per-architecture register map built at probe","Device tree","It asks the firmware"],"a":1,"e":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;regmap.regs[...]</code> is filled by the <code>kbase_regmap_v*_init</code> functions.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_device::hwaccess_lock"]},{"id":"uapi","title":"Userspace interface (fops, ioctl, mmap, sysfs)","short":"Everything userspace can call","tag":"both","color":"#0969da","purpose":"<p>Userspace talks to the driver through the character device <code>/dev/maliN</code>. Its <strong>file operations</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/fops\">file_operations</a>) are in <span class=\"inref\">kbase_fops</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@2308\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:2308\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:2308</a>)</span>:</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>fop</th><th>handler</th><th>purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>open</td><td><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1938\"><code>kbase_open()</code></a></td><td>create a <code>kbase_file</code>; on CSF load firmware once</td></tr><tr><td>unlocked_ioctl</td><td><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1995\"><code>kbase_ioctl()</code></a></td><td>all commands ([[page:ioctls</td><td>ioctl reference]])</td></tr><tr><td>mmap</td><td><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2002\"><code>kbase_mmap()</code></a></td><td>map GPU memory, CSF user I/O pages, tracking page into the process</td></tr><tr><td>read</td><td><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1996\"><code>kbase_read()</code></a></td><td>JM: completed-atom events; CSF: error/event notifications</td></tr><tr><td>poll</td><td><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1998\"><code>kbase_poll()</code></a></td><td>wait for events</td></tr><tr><td>release</td><td><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1939\"><code>kbase_release()</code></a></td><td>tear down the context</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>The ABI is defined in <code>include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/</code>. ioctl numbers use type <code>KBASE_IOCTL_TYPE</code> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ioctl.h@38\" title=\"include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ioctl.h:38\">include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ioctl.h:38</a>)</span> (0x80). The ABI (\"UK\") version is negotiated first by <a class=\"ioref\" href=\"#/ioctl/KBASE_IOCTL_VERSION_CHECK\"><code>KBASE_IOCTL_VERSION_CHECK</code></a> (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1921\"><code>kbase_api_handshake()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@365\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:365\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:365</a>)</span>).</p>","how":"<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1995\"><code>kbase_ioctl()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@1815\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1815\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1815</a>)</span> is a large <code>switch</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Before a context exists</strong>, only four ioctls are accepted:</p>\n<ul><li><code>VERSION_CHECK</code></li><li><code>SET_FLAGS</code></li><li><code>KINSTR_PRFCNT_ENUM_INFO</code>/<code>_SETUP</code></li><li><code>GET_GPUPROPS</code></li></ul>\n<p>Everything else first calls <code>kbase_file_get_kctx_if_setup_complete()</code> and gets <code>-EPERM</code> if setup is not complete (<span class=\"inref\">check</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@1859\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1859\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1859</a>)</span>).</p>\n<p>Each case uses a helper macro that copies the argument struct in and/or out and checks its size and direction at compile time:</p>\n<ul><li><code>KBASE_HANDLE_IOCTL</code> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@1732\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1732\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1732</a>)</span> (no argument)</li><li><code>KBASE_HANDLE_IOCTL_IN</code> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@1742\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1742\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1742</a>)</span> (copy in)</li><li><code>KBASE_HANDLE_IOCTL_OUT</code> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@1757\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1757\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1757</a>)</span> (copy out)</li><li><code>KBASE_HANDLE_IOCTL_INOUT</code> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@1773\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1773\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1773</a>)</span> (copy in and out)</li></ul>\n<p>The perf-counter reader (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwcnt\">Hardware performance counters</a>) and the timeline stream (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/trace\">Tracing, debugfs &amp; debug aids</a>) return <strong>separate file descriptors</strong>, each with its own fops/ioctls.</p>\n<p><strong>sysfs</strong> attributes are created by <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2102\"><code>kbase_sysfs_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@5871\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5871\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5871</a>)</span>; see the <a href=\"#/interfaces\">interfaces page</a> for the full generated list (power_policy, core_mask, gpuinfo, js_timeouts, csg_scheduling_period, …).</p>","locking":"<p><code>kfile-&gt;setup_state</code> is an atomic used as a small state machine (NEED_CTX → CTX_IN_PROGRESS → COMPLETE) so two threads cannot create a context on the same fd (<span class=\"inref\">atomic_cmpxchg</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@692\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:692\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:692</a>)</span>).</p>","talks":"<p>It dispatches to <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/context\">Contexts (per-process GPU state)</a>, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mem\">Memory management</a>, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/jm\">Job Manager back-end (JD / JS / job slots)</a> or <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csf\">CSF queues, groups &amp; scheduler</a>/<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/kcpu\">KCPU queues, sync objects &amp; tiler heap</a>, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwcnt\">Hardware performance counters</a> and <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/trace\">Tracing, debugfs &amp; debug aids</a>.</p>","debug":"<p>Build with dynamic debug and enable <code>mali_kbase_core_linux.c</code> messages: each ioctl logs <code>Enter ioctl &lt;fn&gt;</code> / <code>Return &lt;n&gt; from ioctl &lt;fn&gt;</code> from the handler macros.</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[268,"Per-open-file state; owns the context after SET_FLAGS"],[421,""],[504,""],[506,""]],"fns":[[[1938],""],[[1939],""],[[1995],""],[[2002],""],[[1997],""],[[1998],""],[[1921],""],[[1940],""],[[1916],""],[[1920],""],[[2102],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"A process calls MEM_ALLOC right after open(), before SET_FLAGS. Result?","o":["Works, with a default context","-EPERM","-EINVAL","The kernel creates the context implicitly"],"a":1,"e":"<p>No context exists yet, so <span class=\"inref\">kbase_ioctl returns -EPERM</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@1859\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1859\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1859</a>)</span>.</p>"},{"q":"What does KBASE_HANDLE_IOCTL_INOUT do besides calling the handler?","o":["Takes hwaccess_lock","copy_from_user before and copy_to_user after, with size checks","Powers up the GPU","Nothing"],"a":1,"e":"<p>See <code>KBASE_HANDLE_IOCTL_INOUT</code> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@1773\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1773\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:1773</a>)</span>: <code>BUILD_BUG_ON</code> on size/direction, then copy in, call, copy out.</p>"}],"locks":[]},{"id":"context","title":"Contexts (per-process GPU state)","short":"kbase_context: one per open file","tag":"both","color":"#1a7f37","purpose":"<p>A <strong>context</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/context\">context (kctx)</a>) is the kernel's view of one GPU client, normally one process. It owns:</p>\n<ul><li>a private <strong>GPU virtual address space</strong> (its own page tables, <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/251\"><code>struct kbase_mmu_table</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@321\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:321\">mali_kbase_defs.h:321</a>)</span>)</li><li>memory regions and zones (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mem\">Memory management</a>)</li><li>per-context page pools</li><li>on JM: atoms and job-scheduler state; on CSF: queues, groups, KCPU queues and tiler heaps</li></ul>\n<p>Contexts are created by <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/483\"><code>kbase_create_context()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_jm.c@171\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_jm.c:171\">context/backend/mali_kbase_context_jm.c:171</a>)</span> / <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/470\"><code>kbase_create_context()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c@117\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c:117\">context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c:117</a>)</span> when userspace issues <code>SET_FLAGS</code>, and destroyed by <code>kbase_destroy_context</code> on close.</p>","how":"<p>Creation walks the <code>context_init[]</code> table (<span class=\"inref\">CSF</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c@88\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c:88\">context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c:88</a>)</span>, <span class=\"inref\">JM</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_jm.c@129\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_jm.c:129\">context/backend/mali_kbase_context_jm.c:129</a>)</span>):</p>\n<ul><li>common init (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/487\"><code>kbase_context_common_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c@132\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c:132\">context/mali_kbase_context.c:132</a>)</span>)</li><li>page pools (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/492\"><code>kbase_context_mem_pool_group_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c@297\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c:297\">context/mali_kbase_context.c:297</a>)</span>)</li><li>evictable memory shrinker (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2632\"><code>kbase_mem_evictable_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c@788\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:788\">mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:788</a>)</span>)</li><li>page-table root (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/494\"><code>kbase_context_mmu_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c@308\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c:308\">context/mali_kbase_context.c:308</a>)</span>)</li><li>region tracker / VA zones (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2851\"><code>kbase_region_tracker_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.c@961\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.c:961\">mali_kbase_reg_track.c:961</a>)</span>)</li><li>sticky resources and JIT</li><li>backend-specific: JM <code>kbase_jd_init</code>/<code>kbasep_js_kctx_init</code>; CSF <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/580\"><code>kbase_csf_ctx_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@1644\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:1644\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:1644</a>)</span></li><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/488\"><code>kbase_context_add_to_dev_list()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c@209\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c:209\">context/mali_kbase_context.c:209</a>)</span></li></ul>\n<p>Flags such as <code>KCTX_COMPAT</code> (32-bit process) and <code>KCTX_FORCE_SAME_VA</code> are kept in <code>kctx-&gt;flags</code> and read with <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/500\"><code>kbase_ctx_flag()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.h@88\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.h:88\">context/mali_kbase_context.h:88</a>)</span>. 64-bit processes always get <code>KCTX_FORCE_SAME_VA</code> (<span class=\"inref\">set here</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c@147\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c:147\">context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c:147</a>)</span>).</p>","locking":"<p><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_device::kctx_list_lock\"><code>kbase_device::kctx_list_lock</code></a> protects the device's list of contexts. Context teardown first waits for any system suspend to finish (<span class=\"inref\">kbase_pm_context_active_handle_suspend loop</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c@192\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c:192\">context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c:192</a>)</span>).</p>","talks":"<p>A context gets a hardware address space from <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/ctxsched\">Address-space scheduling</a> while it has work on the GPU. <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mem\">Memory management</a> objects belong to it.</p>","debug":"<p>Each context gets a debugfs directory <code>&lt;tgid&gt;_&lt;id&gt;</code> under <code>ctx/</code> with <code>mem_view</code>, <code>mem_zones</code>, <code>mem_allocs</code>, <code>atoms</code> (JM), <code>jit_*</code> and more (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1937\"><code>kbase_file_create_kctx()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@677\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:677\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:677</a>)</span>).</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[272,""],[49,"One row of <code>context_init[]</code>"],[74,""],[214,""]],"fns":[[[470],""],[[483],""],[[471],""],[[484],""],[[487],""],[[494],""],[[1937],""],[[500],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"Which flag do all 64-bit processes get, making GPU VA = CPU VA by default?","o":["KCTX_COMPAT","KCTX_FORCE_SAME_VA","KCTX_INFINITE_CACHE","KCTX_DYING"],"a":1,"e":"<p><span class=\"inref\">kbase_create_context</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c@147\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c:147\">context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c:147</a>)</span> sets it when <code>!is_compat</code>.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_device::kctx_list_lock"]},{"id":"mem","title":"Memory management","short":"Regions, zones, physical pages, imports, JIT","tag":"both","color":"#bf8700","purpose":"<p>The GPU reads and writes ordinary system RAM through its own MMU. The driver therefore has to track two things:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>GPU virtual address ranges</strong>: <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/319\"><code>struct kbase_va_region</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.h@665\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.h:665\">mali_kbase_mem.h:665</a>)</span> objects, kept in red-black trees (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/rbtree\">red-black tree</a>) per <strong>zone</strong> (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/332\"><code>struct kbase_reg_zone</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.h@172\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.h:172\">mali_kbase_reg_track.h:172</a>)</span>, zones are listed in <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/331\"><code>enum kbase_memory_zone</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.h@141\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.h:141\">mali_kbase_reg_track.h:141</a>)</span>).</li><li><strong>Physical backing</strong>: <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/315\"><code>struct kbase_mem_phy_alloc</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.h@349\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.h:349\">mali_kbase_mem.h:349</a>)</span>, an array of page addresses (<code>pages[]</code>, <code>nents</code> valid) of a given type (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/312\"><code>enum kbase_memory_type</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.h@276\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.h:276\">mali_kbase_mem.h:276</a>)</span>):<ul><li><code>NATIVE</code>: allocated by kbase</li><li><code>IMPORTED_UMM</code>: dma-buf</li><li><code>IMPORTED_USER_BUF</code>: pinned user pages</li><li><code>ALIAS</code></li><li><code>RAW</code></li></ul></li></ul>\n<p>A region points to its backing twice, <code>cpu_alloc</code> and <code>gpu_alloc</code>. They are normally the same object.</p>\n<p>Key ideas:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>SAME_VA:</strong> for 64-bit processes the GPU VA equals the CPU VA. The GPU mapping is created inside <code>mmap()</code> (<a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/memalloc\">GPU memory allocation and mapping into the GPU address space</a>).</li><li><strong>Commit vs. reserve:</strong> <code>va_pages</code> is reserved address space; <code>commit_pages</code> are physically backed. <strong>Growable</strong> regions get more pages on GPU page faults (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mmu\">GPU MMU: page tables, flushes, faults</a>).</li><li><strong>Page pools</strong> (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/256\"><code>struct kbase_mem_pool</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@544\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:544\">mali_kbase_defs.h:544</a>)</span>) cache zeroed pages. Each context pool falls back to the device pool (<code>next_pool</code>), which falls back to the kernel via the memory group manager (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2751\"><code>kbase_mem_pool_alloc_pages()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c@699\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c:699\">mali_kbase_mem_pool.c:699</a>)</span>, <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2734\"><code>kbase_mem_alloc_page()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c@267\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c:267\">mali_kbase_mem_pool.c:267</a>)</span>). Pools exist for small (4 KB) and large (2 MB) pages and per <strong>memory group</strong>.</li><li><strong>JIT</strong> (\"just-in-time\") memory: driver-managed allocations reused between jobs (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2542\"><code>kbase_jit_allocate()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@3132\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:3132\">mali_kbase_mem.c:3132</a>)</span>, <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2543\"><code>kbase_jit_free()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@3382\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:3382\">mali_kbase_mem.c:3382</a>)</span>).</li><li><strong>Eviction:</strong> userspace can mark memory as discardable (<code>BASE_MEM_DONT_NEED</code>). A shrinker then frees it under memory pressure (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2632\"><code>kbase_mem_evictable_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c@788\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:788\">mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:788</a>)</span>).</li><li><strong>Imports:</strong> dma-buf (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2644\"><code>kbase_mem_umm_map()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c@1314\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:1314\">mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:1314</a>)</span>) and user buffers (the <code>kbase_user_buf_*</code> state machine, e.g. <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2570\"><code>kbase_user_buf_from_empty_to_gpu_mapped()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@4416\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:4416\">mali_kbase_mem.c:4416</a>)</span>).</li><li><strong>Aliases:</strong> one region made of slices of other regions (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2650\"><code>kbase_mem_alias()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c@1724\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:1724\">mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:1724</a>)</span>).</li><li><strong>Page migration</strong> (optional, <a class=\"cfgref\" href=\"#/config/CONFIG_MALI_PAGE_MIGRATION\"><code>CONFIG_MALI_PAGE_MIGRATION</code></a>): lets the kernel move GPU pages (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_migrate.c\"><code>mali_kbase_mem_migrate.c</code></a>).</li></ul>","how":"<p>See <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/memalloc\">GPU memory allocation and mapping into the GPU address space</a> for the full walk. In short:</p>\n<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2628\"><code>kbase_mem_alloc()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c@295\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:295\">mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:295</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2515\"><code>kbase_check_alloc_flags()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@2062\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:2062\">mali_kbase_mem.c:2062</a>)</span> / <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2517\"><code>kbase_check_alloc_sizes()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@2182\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:2182\">mali_kbase_mem.c:2182</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2862\"><code>kbase_ctx_alloc_free_region()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.c@1380\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.c:1380\">mali_kbase_reg_track.c:1380</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2513\"><code>kbase_alloc_phy_pages()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@2000\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:2000\">mali_kbase_mem.c:2000</a>)</span> (→ <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2506\"><code>kbase_alloc_phy_pages_helper()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@1226\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:1226\">mali_kbase_mem.c:1226</a>)</span> → pools) → either a cookie (SAME_VA) or <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2491\"><code>kbase_gpu_mmap()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@334\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:334\">mali_kbase_mem.c:334</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3021\"><code>kbase_mmu_insert_pages()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@2932\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:2932\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:2932</a>)</span>.</p>\n<p>Freeing: <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2502\"><code>kbase_mem_free()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@1036\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:1036\">mali_kbase_mem.c:1036</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2501\"><code>kbase_mem_free_region()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@966\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:966\">mali_kbase_mem.c:966</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2492\"><code>kbase_gpu_munmap()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@487\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:487\">mali_kbase_mem.c:487</a>)</span>.</p>\n<p>Growing and shrinking an existing region: <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2655\"><code>kbase_mem_commit()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c@2130\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:2130\">mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:2130</a>)</span>.</p>","locking":"<ul><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_context::reg_lock\"><code>kbase_context::reg_lock</code></a> (taken with <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2518\"><code>kbase_gpu_vm_lock()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c@2292\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c:2292\">mali_kbase_mem.c:2292</a>)</span>) protects the context's region trees and allocations. Most memory functions assert it.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_mem_pool::pool_lock\"><code>kbase_mem_pool::pool_lock</code></a> protects one pool.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_context::jit_evict_lock\"><code>kbase_context::jit_evict_lock</code></a> protects JIT and eviction lists.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_mmu_table::mmu_lock\"><code>kbase_mmu_table::mmu_lock</code></a> (see <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mmu\">GPU MMU: page tables, flushes, faults</a>) is taken <em>inside</em> <code>reg_lock</code> when page tables change.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_page_metadata::migrate_lock\"><code>kbase_page_metadata::migrate_lock</code></a> protects per-page migration metadata.</li></ul>","talks":"<p>Calls into <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mmu\">GPU MMU: page tables, flushes, faults</a> for every mapping change and uses <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/platform\">Platform integration (DT, clocks, regulators, memory groups)</a>'s memory group manager for pages. Used by <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/uapi\">Userspace interface (fops, ioctl, mmap, sysfs)</a> (ioctls/mmap), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/jm\">Job Manager back-end (JD / JS / job slots)</a> (external resources, JIT soft jobs), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/kcpu\">KCPU queues, sync objects &amp; tiler heap</a> (JIT/import commands), and <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csffw\">CSF firmware &amp; host interface</a> (firmware memory).</p>","debug":"<ul><li>debugfs per context: <code>mem_view</code> (dump GPU memory), <code>mem_zones</code>, <code>mem_allocs</code>, <code>mem_profile</code>.</li><li>debugfs per device: <code>mem_pool_size</code> / <code>mem_pool_max_size</code>.</li><li><code>gpu_memory</code> (debugfs) lists per-process usage (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_gpu_memory_debugfs.c\"><code>mali_kbase_gpu_memory_debugfs.c</code></a>).</li></ul>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[319,""],[315,""],[332,""],[331,"Enum of zones"],[256,""],[257,""],[311,""],[323,"A physical address with a large-page tag in the low bits"],[317,""]],"fns":[[[2628],""],[[2513],""],[[2506],""],[[2491],""],[[2492],""],[[2502],""],[[2655],""],[[2651],""],[[2650],""],[[2751],""],[[2734],""],[[2667],""],[[2833],""],[[2827],""],[[2542],""],[[2543],""],[[2518],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"For a SAME_VA allocation, what does MEM_ALLOC return in <code>gpu_va</code>?","o":["The final GPU address","A cookie that userspace passes to mmap() as the offset","A physical address","0"],"a":1,"e":"<p>See <span class=\"inref\">the cookie path</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c@452\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:452\">mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:452</a>)</span>. The real GPU VA is chosen when <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2666\"><code>kbasep_reg_mmap()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c@2698\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:2698\">mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:2698</a>)</span> calls <code>kbase_gpu_mmap(…, vma-&gt;vm_start, …)</code>.</p>"},{"q":"A context pool is empty. Where do pages come from next?","o":["The firmware","The device-wide pool (next_pool), then the kernel via mgm_alloc_page","dma_alloc_coherent","Failure"],"a":1,"e":"<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2751\"><code>kbase_mem_pool_alloc_pages()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c@699\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c:699\">mali_kbase_mem_pool.c:699</a>)</span> tries <code>pool-&gt;next_pool</code>, then <code>kbase_mem_alloc_page()</code>.</p>"},{"q":"Which lock must be held to walk a context's region rbtree?","o":["hwaccess_lock","kctx-&gt;reg_lock (kbase_gpu_vm_lock)","pm.lock","mmu_hw_mutex"],"a":1,"e":"<p><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_context::reg_lock\"><code>kbase_context::reg_lock</code></a>.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_context::reg_lock","kbase_mem_pool::pool_lock","kbase_context::jit_evict_lock","kbase_page_metadata::migrate_lock"]},{"id":"mmu","title":"GPU MMU: page tables, flushes, faults","short":"Translating GPU virtual to physical","tag":"both","color":"#953800","purpose":"<p>Each context has its own <strong>page table</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/page-table\">page table</a>) in the AArch64-style 4-level format (levels 0–3, <code>MIDGARD_MMU_TOPLEVEL</code> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@100\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:100\">mali_kbase_defs.h:100</a>)</span>..<code>MIDGARD_MMU_BOTTOMLEVEL</code> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@102\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:102\">mali_kbase_defs.h:102</a>)</span>, 512 entries per table, <code>KBASE_MMU_PAGE_ENTRIES</code> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.h@28\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.h:28\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.h:28</a>)</span>). The driver writes these tables in normal RAM. The GPU walks them when a context is bound to one of the hardware <strong>address spaces</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/as\">address space (AS)</a>).</p>\n<p>The PTE format code is in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_mode_aarch64.c\"><code>mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_mode_aarch64.c</code></a> (an ops table <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/261\"><code>struct kbase_mmu_mode</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@645\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:645\">mali_kbase_defs.h:645</a>)</span>, e.g. <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3093\"><code>entry_set_ate()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_mode_aarch64.c@140\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_mode_aarch64.c:140\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_mode_aarch64.c:140</a>)</span>). The register-level commands (UPDATE, LOCK, UNLOCK, FLUSH) are in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_hw_direct.c\"><code>mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_hw_direct.c</code></a>.</p>","how":"<p><strong>Inserting pages:</strong> <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3021\"><code>kbase_mmu_insert_pages()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@2932\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:2932\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:2932</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3019\"><code>mmu_insert_pages_no_flush()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@2686\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:2686\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:2686</a>)</span>:</p>\n<ol><li>Walk down from the top-level page directory (PGD).</li><li>Allocate missing levels with <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3012\"><code>mmu_insert_alloc_pgds()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@2336\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:2336\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:2336</a>)</span>.</li><li>Write the leaf entries (ATEs).</li><li>Flush: <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3010\"><code>mmu_flush_invalidate_insert_pages()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@2117\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:2117\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:2117</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3082\"><code>kbase_mmu_hw_do_flush()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_hw_direct.c@502\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_hw_direct.c:502\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_hw_direct.c:502</a>)</span>. If the context currently has no AS there is nothing to flush.</li></ol>\n<p><strong>Binding a context to an AS:</strong> <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3024\"><code>kbase_mmu_update()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@3017\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:3017\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:3017</a>)</span> → <code>mmu_mode-&gt;update</code> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3074\"><code>kbase_mmu_hw_configure()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_hw_direct.c@321\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_hw_direct.c:321\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_hw_direct.c:321</a>)</span> writes <code>TRANSTAB</code>, <code>MEMATTR</code> and <code>TRANSCFG</code>, then issues <code>AS_COMMAND_UPDATE</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Faults:</strong></p>\n<ul><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2967\"><code>kbase_mmu_interrupt()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c@301\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c:301\">mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c:301</a>)</span> / <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2952\"><code>kbase_mmu_interrupt()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_csf.c@360\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_csf.c:360\">mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_csf.c:360</a>)</span> (IRQ context) read the fault address and status, then queue <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3004\"><code>kbase_mmu_page_fault_worker()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@1230\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:1230\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:1230</a>)</span> or <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3051\"><code>kbase_mmu_bus_fault_worker()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@4838\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:4838\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:4838</a>)</span>.</li><li>The page-fault worker either <strong>grows</strong> a growable region (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3003\"><code>page_fault_try_alloc()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@1077\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:1077\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:1077</a>)</span>, then inserts the pages) or <strong>kills</strong> the context's GPU work (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2964\"><code>kbase_mmu_report_fault_and_kill()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c@103\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c:103\">mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c:103</a>)</span> / <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2949\"><code>kbase_mmu_report_fault_and_kill()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_csf.c@195\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_csf.c:195\">mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_csf.c:195</a>)</span>).</li><li>Fault decoding helpers: <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_faults_decoder.c\"><code>mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_faults_decoder.c</code></a>.</li></ul>\n<p>On CSF the firmware itself (MCU) has an address space, <code>MCU_AS_NR</code>, with page tables in <code>kbdev-&gt;csf.mcu_mmu</code>.</p>","locking":"<ul><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_mmu_table::mmu_lock\"><code>kbase_mmu_table::mmu_lock</code></a> protects one page table.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_device::mmu_hw_mutex\"><code>kbase_device::mmu_hw_mutex</code></a> serializes MMU hardware commands with AS assignment.</li><li><code>hwaccess_lock</code> is also needed for AS register writes (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3024\"><code>kbase_mmu_update()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@3017\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:3017\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:3017</a>)</span> asserts both).</li></ul>","talks":"<p>Called by <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mem\">Memory management</a> (map/unmap), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/ctxsched\">Address-space scheduling</a> (bind AS), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/reset\">GPU reset &amp; fault recovery</a> (restore AS after reset), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csffw\">CSF firmware &amp; host interface</a> (MCU tables). Faults feed <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/jm\">Job Manager back-end (JD / JS / job slots)</a>/<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csf\">CSF queues, groups &amp; scheduler</a> (kill jobs/groups).</p>","debug":"<ul><li>debugfs <code>as_fault</code> per AS (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_as_fault_debugfs.c\"><code>mali_kbase_as_fault_debugfs.c</code></a>).</li><li>The kernel log prints the decoded fault, e.g. <code>\"Unhandled Page fault in AS…\"</code> with the access type and source ID.</li><li>An MMU dump of a context can be mapped with <code>BASE_MEM_MMU_DUMP_HANDLE</code> (<span class=\"inref\">mmap case</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c@2818\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:2818\">mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:2818</a>)</span>).</li></ul>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[251,""],[261,""],[216,"AS slot (JM version)"],[95,"AS slot (CSF version)"],[250,""]],"fns":[[[3021],""],[[3019],""],[[3031],""],[[3024],""],[[3074],""],[[3082],""],[[3004],""],[[3003],""],[[2967],""],[[2952],""],[[3045],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"How many levels does the GPU page table have here?","o":["2","3","4 (levels 0..3)","5"],"a":2,"e":"<p><code>MIDGARD_MMU_TOPLEVEL</code> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@100\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:100\">mali_kbase_defs.h:100</a>)</span> = 0 and <code>MIDGARD_MMU_BOTTOMLEVEL</code> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@102\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:102\">mali_kbase_defs.h:102</a>)</span> = 3.</p>"},{"q":"A GPU translation fault hits a region without the GROWABLE flag. What happens?","o":["Pages are allocated","The fault is reported and the context's work is killed","The GPU is reset","Ignored"],"a":1,"e":"<p><span class=\"inref\">&#x27;Memory is not growable&#x27;</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@1470\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:1470\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:1470</a>)</span> → <code>kbase_mmu_report_fault_and_kill</code>.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_mmu_table::mmu_lock","kbase_device::mmu_hw_mutex"]},{"id":"ctxsched","title":"Address-space scheduling","short":"Giving contexts one of the few hardware AS slots","tag":"both","color":"#57606a","purpose":"<p>The GPU has only a few hardware address spaces (<code>nr_hw_address_spaces</code>, typically 8–16). Contexts may far outnumber them. <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c\"><code>mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c</code></a> hands out AS numbers using a <strong>refcount</strong> per context:</p>\n<ul><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2126\"><code>kbase_ctx_sched_retain_ctx()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c@107\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:107\">mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:107</a>)</span>: if the refcount goes 0→1, find an AS (prefer the context's previous AS, so no reprogramming is needed). If the slot previously held a different context, unbind that context and program the MMU for the new one (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3024\"><code>kbase_mmu_update()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c@3017\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:3017\">mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c:3017</a>)</span>).</li><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2128\"><code>kbase_ctx_sched_release_ctx()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c@179\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:179\">mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:179</a>)</span>: when the refcount reaches 0 the AS is marked free but stays programmed. A later retain can reuse it cheaply.</li></ul>","how":"<p>Callers: on JM the job scheduler (<code>kbasep_js_schedule_ctx</code>), on CSF the scheduler when it places a group on a CSG slot (<span class=\"inref\">program_csg_slot</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@2903\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:2903\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:2903</a>)</span>). After a GPU reset every AS is re-programmed by <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2131\"><code>kbase_ctx_sched_restore_all_as()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c@236\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:236\">mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:236</a>)</span>.</p>","locking":"<p>Retain requires both <a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_device::mmu_hw_mutex\"><code>kbase_device::mmu_hw_mutex</code></a> and <a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_device::hwaccess_lock\"><code>kbase_device::hwaccess_lock</code></a> (<span class=\"inref\">asserts</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c@111\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:111\">mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:111</a>)</span>).</p>","talks":"<p>Between <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/jm\">Job Manager back-end (JD / JS / job slots)</a>/<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csf\">CSF queues, groups &amp; scheduler</a> (who need the GPU) and <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mmu\">GPU MMU: page tables, flushes, faults</a> (which programs AS registers).</p>","debug":"<p>Timeline events <code>TL_KBASE_CTX_ASSIGN_AS</code> / <code>UNASSIGN_AS</code> record every assignment (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/trace\">Tracing, debugfs &amp; debug aids</a>).</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[266,"See <code>as_free</code>, <code>as_to_kctx[]</code>, <code>nr_hw_address_spaces</code>"]],"fns":[[[2126],""],[[2128],""],[[2131],""],[[2122],""],[[2132],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"A context's refcount drops to 0. What happens to its AS?","o":["Page tables are freed","It is marked free in as_free but stays programmed for cheap reuse","The GPU is reset","Nothing at all"],"a":1,"e":"<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2128\"><code>kbase_ctx_sched_release_ctx()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c@179\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:179\">mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:179</a>)</span> sets the bit in <code>as_free</code>; <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2126\"><code>kbase_ctx_sched_retain_ctx()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c@107\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:107\">mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:107</a>)</span> prefers <code>kctx-&gt;as_nr</code> later.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_device::mmu_hw_mutex","kbase_device::hwaccess_lock"]},{"id":"jm","title":"Job Manager back-end (JD / JS / job slots)","short":"Atoms → job slots (older GPUs)","tag":"JM","color":"#d4a72c","purpose":"<p>On <strong>JM GPUs</strong> userspace submits <strong>atoms</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/atom\">atom</a>). An atom is a job chain address plus requirements and up to two dependencies. Three layers process them:</p>\n<ol><li><strong>JD (job dispatcher)</strong>, <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c\"><code>mali_kbase_jd.c</code></a>: parses atoms (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2296\"><code>kbase_jd_submit()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c@1008\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c:1008\">mali_kbase_jd.c:1008</a>)</span>, <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2295\"><code>jd_submit_atom()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c@711\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c:711\">mali_kbase_jd.c:711</a>)</span>), resolves dependencies, runs <strong>soft jobs</strong> (CPU-side work such as fence waits and JIT alloc, <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_softjobs.c\"><code>mali_kbase_softjobs.c</code></a>) and completes atoms (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2292\"><code>kbase_jd_done_nolock()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c@526\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c:526\">mali_kbase_jd.c:526</a>)</span>).</li><li><strong>JS (job scheduler)</strong>, <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c\"><code>mali_kbase_js.c</code></a>: per job slot and priority, keeps lists of contexts that have runnable atoms (<code>ctx_list_pullable</code>). It picks the next context (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2384\"><code>kbase_js_sched()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c@2947\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c:2947\">mali_kbase_js.c:2947</a>)</span>) and pulls atoms from it (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2379\"><code>kbase_js_pull()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c@2567\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c:2567\">mali_kbase_js.c:2567</a>)</span>).</li><li><strong>Backend</strong>, <code>backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_*.c</code>: a two-entry <strong>ringbuffer</strong> per slot (current and next), a per-atom state machine (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/210\"><code>enum kbase_atom_gpu_rb_state</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/jm/mali_kbase_jm_defs.h@284\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/jm/mali_kbase_jm_defs.h:284\">jm/mali_kbase_jm_defs.h:284</a>)</span>), register writes (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/147\"><code>kbase_job_hw_submit()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c@119\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:119\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:119</a>)</span>), IRQ completion (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/150\"><code>kbase_job_done()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c@288\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:288\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:288</a>)</span>), and soft/hard stop on timeouts (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_js_backend.c\"><code>backend/gpu/mali_kbase_js_backend.c</code></a>).</li></ol>\n<p>Atom life cycle (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/445\"><code>enum kbase_jd_atom_state</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/jm/mali_base_jm_kernel.h@411\" title=\"include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/jm/mali_base_jm_kernel.h:411\">include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/jm/mali_base_jm_kernel.h:411</a>)</span>): <code>UNUSED → QUEUED → IN_JS → HW_COMPLETED → COMPLETED</code>.</p>","how":"<p>See <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/submit_jm\">Submitting work and completion: Job Manager GPUs</a>. Submit:</p>\n<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2296\"><code>kbase_jd_submit()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c@1008\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c:1008\">mali_kbase_jd.c:1008</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2295\"><code>jd_submit_atom()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c@711\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c:711\">mali_kbase_jd.c:711</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2357\"><code>kbasep_js_add_job()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c@1488\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c:1488\">mali_kbase_js.c:1488</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2384\"><code>kbase_js_sched()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c@2947\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c:2947\">mali_kbase_js.c:2947</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2312\"><code>kbase_jm_kick()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jm.c@65\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jm.c:65\">mali_kbase_jm.c:65</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/208\"><code>kbase_backend_slot_update()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c@861\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c:861\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c:861</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/147\"><code>kbase_job_hw_submit()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c@119\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:119\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:119</a>)</span>.</p>\n<p>The last step writes <code>JS_HEAD_NEXT</code>, <code>JS_CONFIG_NEXT</code> and then <code>JS_COMMAND_NEXT = START</code>.</p>\n<p>Completion:</p>\n<p>IRQ → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/150\"><code>kbase_job_done()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c@288\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:288\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:288</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/213\"><code>kbase_gpu_complete_hw()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c@1217\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c:1217\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c:1217</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2383\"><code>kbase_js_complete_atom()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c@2891\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c:2891\">mali_kbase_js.c:2891</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2299\"><code>kbase_jd_done()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c@1406\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c:1406\">mali_kbase_jd.c:1406</a>)</span> → worker <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2297\"><code>kbase_jd_done_worker()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c@1153\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c:1153\">mali_kbase_jd.c:1153</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2292\"><code>kbase_jd_done_nolock()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c@526\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c:526\">mali_kbase_jd.c:526</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2222\"><code>kbase_event_post()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_event.c@162\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_event.c:162\">mali_kbase_event.c:162</a>)</span> → userspace <code>read()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Timeouts:</strong> an hrtimer (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/225\"><code>timer_callback()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_js_backend.c@74\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_js_backend.c:74\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_js_backend.c:74</a>)</span>) counts ticks per running atom:</p>\n<ul><li>after <code>soft_stop_ticks</code> it soft-stops the atom</li><li>after <code>hard_stop_ticks</code> it hard-stops it</li><li>after <code>gpu_reset_ticks</code> it resets the GPU</li></ul>\n<p>These are tunable through sysfs <code>js_timeouts</code>.</p>","locking":"<ul><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_jd_context::lock\"><code>kbase_jd_context::lock</code></a> (<code>kctx-&gt;jctx.lock</code>) covers JD state per context.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbasep_js_kctx_info::ctx.jsctx_mutex\"><code>kbasep_js_kctx_info::ctx.jsctx_mutex</code></a> covers per-context JS state.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbasep_js_device_data::queue_mutex\"><code>kbasep_js_device_data::queue_mutex</code></a> and <a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbasep_js_device_data::runpool_mutex\"><code>kbasep_js_device_data::runpool_mutex</code></a> cover global JS state.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_device::hwaccess_lock\"><code>kbase_device::hwaccess_lock</code></a> covers slot ringbuffers and register writes, and is held in the IRQ handler.</li></ul>\n<p>Documented order (outermost first, from the comment in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/jm/mali_kbase_js_defs.h\"><code>jm/mali_kbase_js_defs.h</code></a>): <code>queue_mutex</code> → <code>jsctx_mutex</code> → <code>runpool_mutex</code> → <code>hwaccess_lock</code>.</p>","talks":"<p>Uses <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/ctxsched\">Address-space scheduling</a> for AS, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a> for keeping the GPU powered (<code>kbase_pm_context_active</code> when the first context becomes active), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mem\">Memory management</a> for external resources/JIT, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/reset\">GPU reset &amp; fault recovery</a> on timeouts.</p>","debug":"<p>debugfs <code>atoms</code> per context (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd_debugfs.c\"><code>mali_kbase_jd_debugfs.c</code></a>); sysfs <code>js_timeouts</code>, <code>js_scheduling_period</code>, <code>js_softstop_always</code>, <code>serialize_jobs</code>; <code>kinstr_jm</code> gives userspace a stream of atom state changes (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_kinstr_jm.c\"><code>mali_kbase_kinstr_jm.c</code></a>).</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[213,""],[214,""],[218,""],[219,""],[445,"Atom life-cycle enum"],[210,"Backend ringbuffer state enum"],[448,"The atom as userspace passes it"]],"fns":[[[2296],""],[[2295],""],[[2357],""],[[2384],""],[[2379],""],[[2312],""],[[208],""],[[147],""],[[150],""],[[213],""],[[2299],""],[[2297],""],[[2292],""],[[2222],""],[[2917],""],[[160],""],[[161],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"Which register write actually starts a job on a JM slot?","o":["JS_HEAD_NEXT","JS_CONFIG_NEXT","JS_COMMAND_NEXT = JS_COMMAND_START","JOB_IRQ_CLEAR"],"a":2,"e":"<p><span class=\"inref\">kbase_job_hw_submit</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c@235\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:235\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:235</a>)</span>. The HEAD and CONFIG writes only prepare the slot.</p>"},{"q":"Why does kbase_jd_done hand off to a worker instead of finishing inline?","o":["To save stack space","It is called from IRQ context under a spinlock; completion takes mutexes and may sleep","The GPU requires it","For tracing"],"a":1,"e":"<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2299\"><code>kbase_jd_done()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c@1406\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c:1406\">mali_kbase_jd.c:1406</a>)</span> queues <code>kbase_jd_done_worker</code> with <code>kthread_queue_work</code>; the worker takes <code>jctx.lock</code> (a mutex).</p>"},{"q":"What is a 'soft job'?","o":["A job that runs on the GPU at low priority","An atom executed by the CPU in the kernel (fences, JIT, events)","A job that was soft-stopped","A firmware task"],"a":1,"e":"<p>See <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2917\"><code>kbase_process_soft_job()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_softjobs.c@1495\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_softjobs.c:1495\">mali_kbase_softjobs.c:1495</a>)</span>: <code>BASE_JD_REQ_SOFT_*</code> types are handled on the CPU.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_jd_context::lock","kbasep_js_kctx_info::ctx.jsctx_mutex","kbasep_js_device_data::queue_mutex","kbasep_js_device_data::runpool_mutex","kbase_device::hwaccess_lock"]},{"id":"csffw","title":"CSF firmware & host interface","short":"Loading and talking to the MCU firmware","tag":"CSF","color":"#0550ae","purpose":"<p>On <strong>CSF GPUs</strong> a small microcontroller (<strong>MCU</strong>, <a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/mcu\">MCU</a>) inside the GPU runs Arm firmware (<code>mali_csffw.bin</code>, overridable with the <code>fw_name</code> module parameter or the DT <code>firmware-name</code> property). The driver and the firmware talk through <strong>shared memory pages</strong> described by the firmware image:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Global interface</strong> <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/102\"><code>struct kbase_csf_global_iface</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h@266\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h:266\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h:266</a>)</span>: <code>GLB_*</code> registers for global requests (idle timer, protected mode, perf counters, halt…)</li><li>per <strong>CSG</strong> (command stream group slot) <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/101\"><code>struct kbase_csf_cmd_stream_group_info</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h@190\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h:190\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h:190</a>)</span>: <code>CSG_*</code></li><li>per <strong>CS</strong> (command stream) <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/100\"><code>struct kbase_csf_cmd_stream_info</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h@124\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h:124\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h:124</a>)</span>: <code>CS_*</code></li></ul>\n<p>Each interface has an <strong>input page</strong> (driver writes) and an <strong>output page</strong> (firmware writes). Requests follow a <strong>REQ/ACK toggle</strong> protocol (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/req-ack\">REQ/ACK protocol</a>):</p>\n<ol><li>The driver flips a bit in <code>*_REQ</code>.</li><li>It rings a <strong>doorbell</strong> (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/727\"><code>kbase_csf_ring_doorbell()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c@1530\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1530\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1530</a><span class=\"tag t-CSF\">CSF</span> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c@512\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c:512\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c:512</a><span class=\"tag t-CSF\">CSF</span>)</span>).</li><li>The firmware does the work and makes the same bit in <code>*_ACK</code> equal to <code>REQ</code>.</li><li><code>(req ^ ack) &amp; mask</code> therefore means \"request still pending\" (<span class=\"inref\">example</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@3132\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:3132\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:3132</a>)</span>).</li></ol>","how":"<p><strong>Loading</strong> (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/765\"><code>kbase_csf_firmware_load_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c@2391\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:2391\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:2391</a><span class=\"tag t-CSF\">CSF</span> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c@1173\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c:1173\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c:1173</a><span class=\"tag t-CSF\">CSF</span>)</span>):</p>\n<ol><li>Reserve the MCU address space and create its page table.</li><li><code>request_firmware</code>, then check the header magic and version.</li><li>Parse the image entries (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/700\"><code>load_firmware_entry()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c@1022\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1022\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1022</a>)</span>): memory sections, configuration, trace buffers, timeline metadata, core-dump info.</li><li>Set up the shared interface region.</li><li>Load the MMU tables (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/692\"><code>load_mmu_tables()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c@380\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:380\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:380</a>)</span>).</li><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/689\"><code>boot_csf_firmware()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c@331\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:331\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:331</a>)</span>: enable the MCU and wait for its boot interrupt.</li><li>Read the firmware's capabilities (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/706\"><code>parse_capabilities()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c@1227\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1227\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1227</a>)</span>).</li><li>Initialise the scheduler (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1215\"><code>kbase_csf_scheduler_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@6744\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:6744\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:6744</a>)</span>).</li><li>Run the global init (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/747\"><code>global_init_on_boot()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c@1971\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1971\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1971</a><span class=\"tag t-CSF\">CSF</span> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c@810\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c:810\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c:810</a><span class=\"tag t-CSF\">CSF</span>)</span>).</li></ol>\n<p>Accessors: <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/718\"><code>kbase_csf_firmware_csg_input()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c@1435\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1435\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1435</a><span class=\"tag t-CSF\">CSF</span> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c@328\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c:328\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c:328</a><span class=\"tag t-CSF\">CSF</span>)</span>, <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/721\"><code>kbase_csf_firmware_csg_output()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c@1463\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1463\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:1463</a><span class=\"tag t-CSF\">CSF</span> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c@364\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c:364\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_no_mali.c:364</a><span class=\"tag t-CSF\">CSF</span>)</span> and their <code>cs</code>/<code>global</code> equivalents.</p>\n<p>Firmware log and trace buffers: <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_log.c\"><code>csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_log.c</code></a>, <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_trace_buffer.c\"><code>csf/mali_kbase_csf_trace_buffer.c</code></a>. Firmware core dumps: <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_core_dump.c\"><code>csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware_core_dump.c</code></a>.</p>\n<p><strong>MCU power</strong> is a state machine in <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a> (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/350\"><code>kbase_pm_mcu_update_state()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c@940\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:940\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:940</a>)</span>). The firmware is halted and rebooted on suspend/resume and on reset.</p>","locking":"<ul><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_csf_scheduler::interrupt_lock\"><code>kbase_csf_scheduler::interrupt_lock</code></a> (<code>kbase_csf_scheduler_spin_lock</code>) protects shared-page accesses that happen in IRQ context.</li><li><code>fw_load_lock</code> serializes the one-time load.</li></ul>","talks":"<p>Used by <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csf\">CSF queues, groups &amp; scheduler</a> (scheduler programs CSG/CS interfaces), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a> (MCU state), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwcnt\">Hardware performance counters</a> (GLB perf counter requests), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/reset\">GPU reset &amp; fault recovery</a> (reload firmware).</p>","debug":"<p>debugfs <code>fw_traces</code>, <code>fw_trace_enable_mask</code>, <code>fw_core_dump</code>, <code>firmware_config/*</code> entries; module params <code>fw_debug</code>, <code>csf_firmware_boot_timeout_ms</code>.</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[102,""],[101,""],[100,""],[94,""],[86,"One memory section of the firmware image"],[88,""]],"fns":[[[765,898],""],[[700],""],[[692],""],[[689],""],[[706],""],[[747,880],""],[[748,881],""],[[727,864],""],[[718,855],""],[[721,858],""],[[769,902],""],[[766,899],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"The driver flips CSG_REQ bit X and rings the doorbell. How does it know the firmware finished?","o":["An ioctl from userspace","CSG_ACK bit X becomes equal to CSG_REQ bit X","A register in GPU_CONTROL","It sleeps 1 ms"],"a":1,"e":"<p>The REQ/ACK toggle protocol: pending while <code>(req ^ ack) &amp; mask</code> is non-zero.</p>"},{"q":"What is the default firmware file name?","o":["mali_fw.bin","mali_csffw.bin","csf.bin","firmware.elf"],"a":1,"e":"<p><span class=\"inref\">default_fw_name</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c@60\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:60\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c:60</a>)</span>.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_csf_scheduler::interrupt_lock"]},{"id":"csf","title":"CSF queues, groups & scheduler","short":"Command queues scheduled onto firmware slots","tag":"CSF","color":"#0a3069","purpose":"<p>On CSF, userspace builds <strong>command queues</strong> (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/61\"><code>struct kbase_queue</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h@414\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:414\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:414</a>)</span>): ring buffers of GPU commands in its own memory. Queues are bundled into <strong>queue groups</strong> (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/64\"><code>struct kbase_queue_group</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h@575\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:575\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:575</a>)</span>) with a priority. The GPU has a fixed number of <strong>CSG slots</strong>, which the firmware runs concurrently. The kernel's <strong>CSF scheduler</strong> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c\"><code>csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c</code></a>) decides which groups occupy those slots.</p>\n<p>Userspace adds work <em>without any syscall</em>: it writes commands into the ring buffer and updates the insert pointer in its <strong>user I/O pages</strong>. A <strong>doorbell</strong> page (mapped into the process) wakes the firmware. The <code>CS_QUEUE_KICK</code> ioctl is only needed when the kernel must (re)schedule the group.</p>","how":"<p>Setup ioctls:</p>\n<ul><li><code>CS_QUEUE_REGISTER</code> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/544\"><code>kbase_csf_queue_register()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@573\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:573\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:573</a>)</span></li><li><code>CS_QUEUE_GROUP_CREATE</code> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/568\"><code>kbase_csf_queue_group_create()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@1301\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:1301\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:1301</a>)</span></li><li><code>CS_QUEUE_BIND</code> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/548\"><code>kbase_csf_queue_bind()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@698\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:698\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:698</a>)</span>, which returns an mmap cookie for the user I/O pages (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/536\"><code>kbase_csf_alloc_command_stream_user_pages()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@280\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:280\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:280</a>)</span>)</li></ul>\n<p>Kick: <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/555\"><code>kbase_csf_queue_kick()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@899\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:899\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:899</a>)</span> → scheduler kthread <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1214\"><code>kbase_csf_scheduler_kthread()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@6691\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:6691\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:6691</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/615\"><code>kbase_csf_process_queue_kick()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@3355\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:3355\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:3355</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1114\"><code>kbase_csf_scheduler_queue_start()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@1846\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:1846\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:1846</a>)</span>.</p>\n<p><strong>Scheduling</strong> is driven by <strong>ticks</strong> (periodic, period from sysfs <code>csg_scheduling_period</code>, <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1191\"><code>schedule_on_tick()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@5575\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5575\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5575</a>)</span>) and <strong>tocks</strong> (event driven, e.g. a group became idle, <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1190\"><code>schedule_on_tock()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@5529\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5529\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5529</a>)</span>). <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1188\"><code>schedule_actions()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@5339\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5339\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5339</a>)</span> does the work:</p>\n<ol><li>Update idle slots (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1173\"><code>scheduler_handle_idle_slots()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@4637\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:4637\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:4637</a>)</span>).</li><li>Rotate for fairness (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1175\"><code>scheduler_rotate()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@4704\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:4704\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:4704</a>)</span>).</li><li>Choose the groups (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1183\"><code>scheduler_prepare()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@5005\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5005\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5005</a>)</span>).</li><li>Program the slots (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1167\"><code>scheduler_apply()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@4215\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:4215\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:4215</a>)</span>). Groups are placed with <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1141\"><code>program_csg_slot()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@2855\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:2855\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:2855</a>)</span>, which writes the CSG interface and calls <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1112\"><code>program_cs()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@1737\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:1737\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:1737</a>)</span> for each bound queue.</li></ol>\n<p>Group states (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/55\"><code>enum kbase_csf_group_state</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h@171\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:171\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:171</a>)</span>):</p>\n<ul><li><code>RUNNABLE</code></li><li><code>IDLE</code></li><li><code>SUSPENDED</code></li><li><code>SUSPENDED_ON_IDLE</code></li><li><code>SUSPENDED_ON_WAIT_SYNC</code></li><li><code>FAULT_EVICTED</code></li><li><code>TERMINATED</code></li></ul>\n<p>Slot states: <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/56\"><code>enum kbase_csf_csg_slot_state</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h@203\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:203\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:203</a>)</span>.</p>\n<p><strong>Interrupts</strong> from the firmware arrive on the JOB IRQ line → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/606\"><code>kbase_csf_interrupt()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@3074\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:3074\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:3074</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/599\"><code>process_csg_interrupts()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@2713\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:2713\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:2713</a>)</span> (<code>SYNC_UPDATE</code>, <code>IDLE</code>, progress timer, faults) → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/598\"><code>process_cs_interrupts()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@2584\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:2584\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:2584</a>)</span> (per-queue faults, tiler out-of-memory).</p>","locking":"<ul><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_csf_scheduler::lock\"><code>kbase_csf_scheduler::lock</code></a> (mutex) protects scheduler state and is held in most scheduler functions.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_csf_scheduler::interrupt_lock\"><code>kbase_csf_scheduler::interrupt_lock</code></a> (spinlock, <code>kbase_csf_scheduler_spin_lock</code>) protects state touched in IRQ context.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_csf_context::lock\"><code>kbase_csf_context::lock</code></a> (<code>kctx-&gt;csf.lock</code>) protects a context's queues and groups.</li><li>Kicks use <code>pending_gpuq_kick_queues_lock</code> (<span class=\"inref\">spin_lock</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@920\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:920\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:920</a>)</span>).</li></ul>","talks":"<p>Uses <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csffw\">CSF firmware &amp; host interface</a> interfaces, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/ctxsched\">Address-space scheduling</a> for AS, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a> (MCU on/off, GPU idle/sleep), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mem\">Memory management</a> (queue buffers, suspend buffers), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/kcpu\">KCPU queues, sync objects &amp; tiler heap</a> (sync waits), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/reset\">GPU reset &amp; fault recovery</a> (on timeouts/faults).</p>","debug":"<p>debugfs <code>scheduling_timer_enabled</code>, <code>scheduling_timer_kick</code>, <code>scheduler_state</code>, per-context <code>groups</code>, <code>active_groups</code>; sysfs <code>csg_scheduling_period</code>, <code>idle_hysteresis_time</code>, <code>fw_timeout</code>; <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/Documentation/csf_sync_state_dump.txt\"><code>Documentation/csf_sync_state_dump.txt</code></a> explains the sync state dump.</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[61,""],[64,""],[74,""],[79,""],[76,""],[55,"Group state enum"],[56,"Slot state enum"]],"fns":[[[544],""],[[568],""],[[548],""],[[555],""],[[1214],""],[[1114],""],[[1191],""],[[1190],""],[[1188],""],[[1141],""],[[1112],""],[[606],""],[[599],""],[[598],""],[[576],""],[[1224],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"Does every GPU command submission on CSF require an ioctl?","o":["Yes, CS_QUEUE_KICK each time","No: userspace writes the ring buffer and rings a mapped doorbell; KICK is only needed for (re)scheduling","Yes, KCPU_QUEUE_ENQUEUE","No, the kernel polls ring buffers"],"a":1,"e":"<p>The user I/O pages and doorbell are mapped into the process (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2688\"><code>kbase_csf_cpu_mmap_user_io_pages()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c@3731\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:3731\">mali_kbase_mem_linux.c:3731</a>)</span>).</p>"},{"q":"What is a 'tock'?","o":["The periodic tick","An event-driven, out-of-cycle scheduling pass","A firmware heartbeat","A reset step"],"a":1,"e":"<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1190\"><code>schedule_on_tock()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@5529\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5529\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5529</a>)</span> runs when, for example, an IDLE interrupt suggests the slot arrangement should change.</p>"},{"q":"Which IRQ line carries CSF firmware interrupts?","o":["GPU","MMU","JOB","A dedicated MCU line"],"a":2,"e":"<p><span class=\"inref\">kbase_job_irq_handler calls kbase_csf_interrupt</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c@66\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:66\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c:66</a>)</span>.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_csf_scheduler::lock","kbase_csf_scheduler::interrupt_lock","kbase_csf_context::lock"]},{"id":"kcpu","title":"KCPU queues, sync objects & tiler heap","short":"CPU-side commands and GPU heaps on CSF","tag":"CSF","color":"#6639ba","purpose":"<p><strong>KCPU queues</strong> (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/123\"><code>struct kbase_kcpu_command_queue</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.h@297\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.h:297\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.h:297</a>)</span>) are command queues executed by the <em>kernel on the CPU</em>. They do work the GPU firmware cannot do itself:</p>\n<ul><li>wait on or signal Linux <strong>dma-fences</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/fence\">dma-fence / sync_file</a>)</li><li>wait on or set <strong>CQS</strong> (cross-queue sync objects in memory)</li><li>map or unmap imported memory</li><li>JIT alloc/free</li><li>suspend a group</li><li>error barriers</li></ul>\n<p>Command types are dispatched in <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/984\"><code>kbase_csf_kcpu_queue_process()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c@2157\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c:2157\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c:2157</a>)</span>.</p>\n<p>The <strong>tiler heap</strong> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_tiler_heap.c\"><code>csf/mali_kbase_csf_tiler_heap.c</code></a>) is growable memory the GPU tiler writes intermediate geometry into. When the firmware reports <em>tiler out-of-memory</em>, the driver adds chunks (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1291\"><code>kbase_csf_tiler_heap_alloc_new_chunk()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_tiler_heap.c@926\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_tiler_heap.c:926\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_tiler_heap.c:926</a>)</span>). A shrinker can reclaim unused chunks (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_tiler_heap_reclaim.c\"><code>csf/mali_kbase_csf_tiler_heap_reclaim.c</code></a>).</p>\n<p><strong>Sync dumps:</strong> <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_sync.c\"><code>csf/mali_kbase_csf_sync.c</code></a> prints what each queue is waiting for, which is invaluable for debugging hangs.</p>","how":"<ul><li>Create: <a class=\"ioref\" href=\"#/ioctl/KBASE_IOCTL_KCPU_QUEUE_CREATE\"><code>KBASE_IOCTL_KCPU_QUEUE_CREATE</code></a> → <code>kbasep_kcpu_queue_new</code>.</li><li>Enqueue: <a class=\"ioref\" href=\"#/ioctl/KBASE_IOCTL_KCPU_QUEUE_ENQUEUE\"><code>KBASE_IOCTL_KCPU_QUEUE_ENQUEUE</code></a> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/987\"><code>kbase_csf_kcpu_queue_enqueue()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c@2551\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c:2551\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c:2551</a>)</span> copies the commands in, prepares each one, and processes the queue.</li><li>Blocked commands resume when their fence or CQS signals. Pending queues are handled from the scheduler kthread (<code>handle_pending_kcpuq_commands</code>).</li><li>Tiler heap: <a class=\"ioref\" href=\"#/ioctl/KBASE_IOCTL_CS_TILER_HEAP_INIT\"><code>KBASE_IOCTL_CS_TILER_HEAP_INIT</code></a> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1288\"><code>kbase_csf_tiler_heap_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_tiler_heap.c@664\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_tiler_heap.c:664\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_tiler_heap.c:664</a>)</span>.</li></ul>","locking":"<ul><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_kcpu_command_queue::lock\"><code>kbase_kcpu_command_queue::lock</code></a> protects one KCPU queue.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_csf_tiler_heap_context::lock\"><code>kbase_csf_tiler_heap_context::lock</code></a> protects a context's tiler heaps.</li></ul>","talks":"<p><a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csf\">CSF queues, groups &amp; scheduler</a> (scheduler thread processes KCPU work, OOM events), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mem\">Memory management</a> (JIT/import), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/jm\">Job Manager back-end (JD / JS / job slots)</a>'s fence helpers are shared with sync_file code.</p>","debug":"<p>debugfs per context <code>kcpu_queues</code>, <code>tiler_heaps</code>, <code>csf_sync</code>; <code>fence_signal_timeout_ms</code> / <code>fence_signal_timeout_enable</code> detect stuck fences.</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[123,""],[122,""],[131,""],[68,""]],"fns":[[[987],""],[[984],""],[[1288],""],[[1291],""],[[1289],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"Who executes a KCPU queue command such as FENCE_WAIT?","o":["The MCU firmware","The kernel driver on the CPU","Userspace","The GPU shader cores"],"a":1,"e":"<p>That is what the K in KCPU stands for: the kernel processes it in <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/984\"><code>kbase_csf_kcpu_queue_process()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c@2157\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c:2157\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c:2157</a>)</span>.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_kcpu_command_queue::lock","kbase_csf_tiler_heap_context::lock"]},{"id":"pm","title":"Power management","short":"Refcounts, policies, power state machines, suspend","tag":"both","color":"#2da44e","purpose":"<p>GPU power management has three layers:</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Demand:</strong> an <em>active count</em> (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2806\"><code>kbase_pm_context_active()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c@50\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c:50\">mali_kbase_pm.c:50</a>)</span> / <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2810\"><code>kbase_pm_context_idle()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c@146\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c:146\">mali_kbase_pm.c:146</a>)</span>, in <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/255\"><code>struct kbase_pm_device_data</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@482\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:482\">mali_kbase_defs.h:482</a>)</span>). Anything that needs the GPU holds a reference.</li><li><strong>Policy:</strong> decides what to power when there is or isn't demand.<ul><li><code>coarse_demand</code> is the default on real HW: power everything while active (<span class=\"inref\">policy list</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_policy.c@38\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_policy.c:38\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_policy.c:38</a>)</span>).</li><li><code>always_on</code>.</li><li>Selectable via sysfs <code>power_policy</code> or DT <code>power-policy</code>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>State machines</strong> in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c\"><code>backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c</code></a>, advanced by <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/369\"><code>kbase_pm_update_state()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c@2268\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:2268\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:2268</a>)</span>:<ul><li>L2 cache (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/360\"><code>kbase_pm_l2_update_state()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c@1433\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:1433\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:1433</a>)</span>)</li><li>shader cores (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/364\"><code>kbase_pm_shaders_update_state()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c@1868\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:1868\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:1868</a>)</span>)</li><li>on CSF, the MCU (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/350\"><code>kbase_pm_mcu_update_state()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c@940\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:940\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:940</a>)</span>)</li></ul></li></ol>\n<p>They write <code>*_PWRON</code>/<code>*_PWROFF</code> registers (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/329\"><code>kbase_pm_invoke()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c@414\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:414\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:414</a>)</span>) and advance on power-transition interrupts.</p>\n<p>Below that, platform callbacks switch clocks and regulators (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/390\"><code>kbase_pm_clock_on()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c@2826\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:2826\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:2826</a>)</span> / <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/391\"><code>kbase_pm_clock_off()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c@2967\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:2967\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:2967</a>)</span>). Linux <strong>runtime PM</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/runtime-pm\">runtime PM</a>) can be used too.</p>","how":"<p>See <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/power\">Power up / power down (runtime)</a>. The active count going 0→1 → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/439\"><code>kbase_pm_update_active()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_policy.c@101\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_policy.c:101\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_policy.c:101</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/282\"><code>kbase_pm_do_poweron()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c@234\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c:234\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c:234</a>)</span>.</p>\n<p><strong>System suspend:</strong> <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2108\"><code>kbase_device_suspend()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@6031\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6031\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6031</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2815\"><code>kbase_pm_suspend()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c@370\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c:370\">mali_kbase_pm.c:370</a>)</span> → <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2813\"><code>kbase_pm_driver_suspend()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c@196\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c:196\">mali_kbase_pm.c:196</a>)</span>:</p>\n<ol><li>Stop scheduling (JM <code>kbasep_js_suspend</code>, CSF <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1224\"><code>kbase_csf_scheduler_pm_suspend()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@7007\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:7007\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:7007</a>)</span>).</li><li>Wait for <code>active_count == 0</code>.</li><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/303\"><code>kbase_hwaccess_pm_suspend()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c@910\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c:910\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c:910</a>)</span>.</li></ol>\n<p>Resume runs in reverse: <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2814\"><code>kbase_pm_driver_resume()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c@334\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c:334\">mali_kbase_pm.c:334</a>)</span>.</p>\n<p><strong>CSF GPU sleep:</strong> when all groups are idle the MCU can be put to sleep without a full power-off (see <code>KBASE_MCU_ON_SLEEP_INITIATE</code> states in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_mcu_states.h\"><code>backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_mcu_states.h</code></a>).</p>","locking":"<ul><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_pm_device_data::lock\"><code>kbase_pm_device_data::lock</code></a> (<code>kbdev-&gt;pm.lock</code>, <code>kbase_pm_lock()</code>) is the PM mutex.</li><li><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_device::hwaccess_lock\"><code>kbase_device::hwaccess_lock</code></a> protects the state machines: <code>kbase_pm_update_state</code> asserts it.</li></ul>","talks":"<p>Every work-submitting subsystem (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/jm\">Job Manager back-end (JD / JS / job slots)</a>, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csf\">CSF queues, groups &amp; scheduler</a>) takes PM references; <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/dvfs\">DVFS, devfreq &amp; thermal (IPA)</a> adjusts frequency while powered; <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/platform\">Platform integration (DT, clocks, regulators, memory groups)</a> callbacks do the physical switching; <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwcnt\">Hardware performance counters</a> is disabled around power transitions; <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/reset\">GPU reset &amp; fault recovery</a> re-runs <code>kbase_pm_init_hw</code>.</p>","debug":"<p>sysfs <code>power_policy</code>, <code>core_mask</code>, <code>pm_poweroff</code>, <code>idle_hysteresis_time</code>, <code>mcu_shader_pwroff_timeout</code>; ktrace records each state transition (<code>KBASE_KTRACE_CODE(PM_*)</code>).</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[255,""],[40,""],[43,""],[32,"L2 state enum (generated from mali_kbase_pm_l2_states.h)"],[33,"MCU state enum (CSF)"]],"fns":[[[2806],""],[[2810],""],[[439],""],[[282],""],[[292],""],[[369],""],[[360],""],[[364],""],[[350],""],[[329],""],[[390],""],[[391],""],[[2815],""],[[2813],""],[[2814],""],[[295],""],[[407],""],[[446],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"What does the default power policy on real hardware do?","o":["Never power off","coarse_demand: power on while there is demand, off when idle","Per-core demand","Firmware decides"],"a":1,"e":"<p><code>all_policy_list[0]</code> is <code>kbase_pm_coarse_demand_policy_ops</code> unless NO_MALI (<span class=\"inref\">list</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_policy.c@38\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_policy.c:38\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_policy.c:38</a>)</span>).</p>"},{"q":"What must reach zero before the GPU can be suspended?","o":["The number of contexts","pm.active_count","The number of AS slots","The MMU refcount"],"a":1,"e":"<p><span class=\"inref\">wait_event(... active_count == 0)</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c@270\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c:270\">mali_kbase_pm.c:270</a>)</span>.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_pm_device_data::lock","kbase_device::hwaccess_lock"]},{"id":"dvfs","title":"DVFS, devfreq & thermal (IPA)","short":"Choosing frequency/voltage; power models","tag":"both","color":"#1b7c83","purpose":"<p><strong>DVFS</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/dvfs\">DVFS</a>) trades performance for power by changing the GPU clock (and voltage). The driver registers with the Linux <strong>devfreq</strong> framework (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/devfreq\">devfreq</a>) in <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/103\"><code>kbase_devfreq_init()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c@602\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c:602\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c:602</a>)</span>:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Operating points</strong> (frequency/voltage pairs, optionally with a core mask) come from DT <code>operating-points-v2</code> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/arm,mali-opp.yaml\"><code>Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/arm,mali-opp.yaml</code></a>).</li><li>devfreq asks <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/91\"><code>kbase_devfreq_status()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c@239\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c:239\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c:239</a>)</span> how busy the GPU was (utilization from <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_metrics.c\"><code>backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_metrics.c</code></a>), then calls <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/88\"><code>kbase_devfreq_target()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c@110\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c:110\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c:110</a>)</span> to switch the clock and regulators.</li><li><strong>IPA</strong> (Intelligent Power Allocation, <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/ipa/mali_kbase_ipa.c\"><code>ipa/mali_kbase_ipa.c</code></a>) provides power models to the thermal framework. It uses a simple static/temperature model (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/ipa/mali_kbase_ipa_simple.c\"><code>ipa/mali_kbase_ipa_simple.c</code></a>) or counter-based models (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/ipa/backend/mali_kbase_ipa_counter_common_csf.c\"><code>ipa/backend/mali_kbase_ipa_counter_common_csf.c</code></a>).</li><li>On CSF, <strong>IPA control</strong> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/ipa_control/mali_kbase_csf_ipa_control.c\"><code>csf/ipa_control/mali_kbase_csf_ipa_control.c</code></a>) shares the firmware's performance counters between IPA and other users.</li><li>The <strong>clock rate trace manager</strong> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_clk_rate_trace_mgr.c\"><code>backend/gpu/mali_kbase_clk_rate_trace_mgr.c</code></a>) notifies listeners (hwcnt, timeline) of frequency changes.</li></ul>","how":"<p>Devfreq work (suspend/resume of devfreq) is serialized on its own workqueue (<code>devfreq_workq</code>, <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/100\"><code>kbase_devfreq_enqueue_work()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c@561\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c:561\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c:561</a>)</span>). Legacy non-devfreq DVFS (<code>CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD_DVFS</code>) calls the platform's <code>kbase_platform_dvfs_event</code> periodically instead.</p>","locking":"<p><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_device::ipa.lock\"><code>kbase_device::ipa.lock</code></a> protects IPA model state. The clock rate trace manager has <a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_clk_rate_trace_manager::lock\"><code>kbase_clk_rate_trace_manager::lock</code></a>.</p>","talks":"<p><a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a> (metrics, power state), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/platform\">Platform integration (DT, clocks, regulators, memory groups)</a> (clocks/regulators), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwcnt\">Hardware performance counters</a>/IPA control (counters), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/trace\">Tracing, debugfs &amp; debug aids</a> (<code>power_gpu_frequency</code> tracepoint).</p>","debug":"<p>debugfs <code>dvfs_utilization</code>, <code>ipa_current_power</code>, <code>ipa_force_fallback_model</code>; sysfs <code>dvfs_period</code>; standard <code>/sys/class/devfreq/*</code> files.</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[37,""],[202,""],[254,""]],"fns":[[[103],""],[[88],""],[[91],""],[[311],""],[[430],""],[[1817],""],[[76],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"Which function does devfreq call to change the GPU frequency?","o":["kbase_devfreq_status","kbase_devfreq_target","kbase_pm_clock_on","kbase_ipa_init"],"a":1,"e":"<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/88\"><code>kbase_devfreq_target()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c@110\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c:110\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c:110</a>)</span> picks the OPP and sets clocks/regulators.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_device::ipa.lock","kbase_clk_rate_trace_manager::lock"]},{"id":"reset","title":"GPU reset & fault recovery","short":"Getting a hung or faulted GPU back","tag":"both","color":"#a40e26","purpose":"<p>When the GPU hangs (job timeout, firmware not responding, MMU command stuck) or reports an unrecoverable error, the driver performs a <strong>soft reset</strong>. It then re-initializes hardware state, restores the address spaces and restarts scheduling. The API is shared by both back-ends (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reset_gpu.h\"><code>mali_kbase_reset_gpu.h</code></a>):</p>\n<pre class=\"snippet\"><code>if (kbase_prepare_to_reset_gpu(kbdev, flags))\n        kbase_reset_gpu(kbdev);</code></pre>\n<p><code>prepare</code> returns false if a reset is already in progress, so concurrent failures produce only one reset. Code that must not run during a reset brackets itself with <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1036\"><code>kbase_reset_gpu_prevent_and_wait()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c@96\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:96\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:96</a>)</span> / <code>kbase_reset_gpu_allow</code>.</p>","how":"<p><strong>JM:</strong></p>\n<ol><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/176\"><code>kbase_reset_gpu()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c@1179\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:1179\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:1179</a>)</span> arms an hrtimer, giving soft-stopped jobs a chance to finish.</li><li>The timer queues <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/170\"><code>kbasep_reset_timeout_worker()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c@878\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:878\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:878</a>)</span>.</li><li>The worker evicts jobs (<code>kbase_backend_reset</code>) and runs <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/407\"><code>kbase_pm_init_hw()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c@3457\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:3457\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:3457</a>)</span>, which issues the soft reset in <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/404\"><code>kbase_pm_do_reset()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c@3331\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:3331\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:3331</a>)</span>.</li><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2131\"><code>kbase_ctx_sched_restore_all_as()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c@236\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:236\">mali_kbase_ctx_sched.c:236</a>)</span> restores the address spaces.</li><li>Jobs are rescheduled.</li></ol>\n<p><strong>CSF:</strong></p>\n<ol><li><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1050\"><code>kbase_reset_gpu()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c@533\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:533\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:533</a>)</span> queues <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1047\"><code>kbase_csf_reset_gpu_worker()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c@450\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:450\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:450</a>)</span>.</li><li>The worker calls <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1046\"><code>kbase_csf_reset_gpu_now()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c@380\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:380\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:380</a>)</span>.</li><li>That evicts groups (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1196\"><code>kbase_csf_scheduler_reset()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@5838\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5838\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:5838</a>)</span>) and calls <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1045\"><code>kbase_csf_reset_gpu_once()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c@285\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:285\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:285</a>)</span>: dump the firmware log, <code>kbase_pm_init_hw</code>, restore the AS, wait for the MCU to reboot.</li><li>Groups that were running get a fatal error reported to userspace. Others are rescheduled.</li></ol>\n<p>Faults that don't need a reset: MMU faults kill only the faulting context's work (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mmu\">GPU MMU: page tables, flushes, faults</a>); CSF queue faults go to <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/594\"><code>handle_fault_event()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@2330\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:2330\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:2330</a>)</span> / <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/596\"><code>cs_error_worker()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@2421\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:2421\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:2421</a>)</span>.</p>","locking":"<p>The reset state is an atomic (<code>hwaccess.backend.reset_gpu</code> on JM, <code>csf.reset.state</code> on CSF); the CSF side also uses an rwsem <code>csf.reset.sem</code> to block hardware access during reset (see <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c\"><code>csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c</code></a>).</p>","talks":"<p>Triggered by <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/jm\">Job Manager back-end (JD / JS / job slots)</a> timeouts, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csf\">CSF queues, groups &amp; scheduler</a>/<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csffw\">CSF firmware &amp; host interface</a> timeouts and fatal errors, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/mmu\">GPU MMU: page tables, flushes, faults</a> stuck commands; uses <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a> (<code>kbase_pm_init_hw</code>), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/ctxsched\">Address-space scheduling</a> (restore AS), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwcnt\">Hardware performance counters</a> (disabled across reset).</p>","debug":"<p>debugfs <code>reset</code> lets you trigger a reset by hand. sysfs <code>reset_timeout</code> sets the JM reset delay. The kernel log shows <code>\"Resetting GPU (allowing up to %d ms)\"</code> and register dumps (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1043\"><code>kbase_csf_debug_dump_registers()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c@225\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:225\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c:225</a>)</span>).</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[],"fns":[[[175],""],[[176],""],[[170],""],[[1048],""],[[1050],""],[[1047],""],[[1046],""],[[1045],""],[[1196],""],[[407],""],[[404],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"Two different paths detect a hang at the same time. How many resets happen?","o":["Two","One: kbase_prepare_to_reset_gpu returns false for the second","Zero","It deadlocks"],"a":1,"e":"<p>See <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/174\"><code>kbase_prepare_to_reset_gpu_locked()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c@1126\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:1126\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c:1126</a>)</span>: it only succeeds if no reset is pending.</p>"}],"locks":[]},{"id":"hwcnt","title":"Hardware performance counters","short":"From GPU counter blocks to profiler tools","tag":"both","color":"#e16f24","purpose":"<p>The GPU has <strong>performance counters</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/hwcnt\">hardware counters</a>) in blocks: front-end, tiler, memory system (L2), and shader cores. The driver layers them so several users can sample at once:</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Backend</strong> (talks to the hardware):<ul><li>JM: <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hwcnt/backend/mali_kbase_hwcnt_backend_jm.c\"><code>hwcnt/backend/mali_kbase_hwcnt_backend_jm.c</code></a> programs <code>PRFCNT_*</code> registers directly.</li><li>CSF: <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hwcnt/backend/mali_kbase_hwcnt_backend_csf.c\"><code>hwcnt/backend/mali_kbase_hwcnt_backend_csf.c</code></a> asks the firmware through the <code>GLB_PRFCNT_*</code> interface.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Context / accumulator</strong> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt.c\"><code>hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt.c</code></a>): enables and disables counting, for example around power transitions (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1667\"><code>kbase_hwcnt_context_disable()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt.c@666\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt.c:666\">hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt.c:666</a>)</span>).</li><li><strong>Virtualizer</strong> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt_virtualizer.c\"><code>hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt_virtualizer.c</code></a>): lets many clients each see \"their own\" counters.</li><li><strong>Clients:</strong> <code>kinstr_prfcnt</code> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_kinstr_prfcnt.c\"><code>mali_kbase_kinstr_prfcnt.c</code></a>) is the userspace API. It is set up by <a class=\"ioref\" href=\"#/ioctl/KBASE_IOCTL_KINSTR_PRFCNT_SETUP\"><code>KBASE_IOCTL_KINSTR_PRFCNT_SETUP</code></a> and returns an fd with its own ioctls (<code>KINSTR_PRFCNT_CMD</code>, <code>GET_SAMPLE</code>, <code>PUT_SAMPLE</code>). IPA is another client.</li></ol>\n<p>There is also a watchdog interface for periodic dumps (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt_watchdog_if_timer.c\"><code>hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt_watchdog_if_timer.c</code></a>).</p>","how":"<p>Userspace: <code>KINSTR_PRFCNT_ENUM_INFO</code> (what counters exist) → <code>KINSTR_PRFCNT_SETUP</code> (fd) → <code>CMD start/stop/sample</code> → <code>GET_SAMPLE</code> reads from a ring buffer mapped with mmap. Dumping goes through <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1765\"><code>kbase_hwcnt_virtualizer_client_dump()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt_virtualizer.c@601\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt_virtualizer.c:601\">hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt_virtualizer.c:601</a>)</span>.</p>","locking":"<p><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_hwcnt_context::state_lock\"><code>kbase_hwcnt_context::state_lock</code></a>, <a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_kinstr_prfcnt_context::lock\"><code>kbase_kinstr_prfcnt_context::lock</code></a>; on CSF the backend coordinates with the scheduler spinlock.</p>","talks":"<p><a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a> (counters must be disabled while powering down), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csffw\">CSF firmware &amp; host interface</a> (CSF backend), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/reset\">GPU reset &amp; fault recovery</a>, <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/dvfs\">DVFS, devfreq &amp; thermal (IPA)</a> (IPA counter models).</p>","debug":"<p>With <code>CONFIG_MALI_PRFCNT_SET_SELECT_VIA_DEBUG_FS</code> (JM only) the counter set can be selected at runtime.</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[177,""],[193,""],[303,""],[157,""]],"fns":[[[1657],""],[[1669],""],[[1667],""],[[1768],""],[[1766],""],[[2483],""],[[2482],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"Why is there a 'virtualizer' layer?","o":["For VMs","So multiple clients can use the single hardware counter resource as if each had it exclusively","To emulate counters","For security"],"a":1,"e":"<p>See the header comment of <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt_virtualizer.h\"><code>hwcnt/mali_kbase_hwcnt_virtualizer.h</code></a>.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_hwcnt_context::state_lock","kbase_kinstr_prfcnt_context::lock"]},{"id":"trace","title":"Tracing, debugfs & debug aids","short":"Seeing what the driver does","tag":"both","color":"#8c959f","purpose":"<p>The driver has several independent observability mechanisms:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>KTrace</strong> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/debug/mali_kbase_debug_ktrace.c\"><code>debug/mali_kbase_debug_ktrace.c</code></a>): a low-overhead in-kernel ring buffer of driver events. Each code is defined in <code>mali_kbase_debug_ktrace_codes.h</code>. It is readable via debugfs and/or ftrace.</li><li><strong>Timeline stream (TL / MIPE)</strong> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/tl/mali_kbase_timeline.c\"><code>tl/mali_kbase_timeline.c</code></a>, <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/tl/mali_kbase_tracepoints.c\"><code>tl/mali_kbase_tracepoints.c</code></a>): a binary event stream for profilers such as Arm Streamline / Performance Studio. Userspace gets an fd through <a class=\"ioref\" href=\"#/ioctl/KBASE_IOCTL_TLSTREAM_ACQUIRE\"><code>KBASE_IOCTL_TLSTREAM_ACQUIRE</code></a> (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3295\"><code>kbase_timeline_io_acquire()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/tl/mali_kbase_timeline_io.c@367\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/tl/mali_kbase_timeline_io.c:367\">tl/mali_kbase_timeline_io.c:367</a>)</span>).</li><li><strong>Linux tracepoints</strong> in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_linux_trace.h\"><code>mali_linux_trace.h</code></a> (<code>mali_job_slots_event</code>, <code>mali_page_fault_insert_pages</code>, …) and <code>power_gpu_frequency</code>, <code>gpu_work_period</code>.</li><li><strong>debugfs:</strong> about 90 entries, all generated on the <a href=\"#/interfaces\">interfaces page</a>. For example <code>mem_view</code>, <code>regs_history</code>, <code>job_fault</code> (JM job fault dump, <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_debug_job_fault.c\"><code>mali_kbase_debug_job_fault.c</code></a>), <code>quirks_*</code>, firmware traces.</li><li><strong>kinstr_jm</strong> (JM): atom state change stream (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_kinstr_jm.c\"><code>mali_kbase_kinstr_jm.c</code></a>).</li><li><strong>GPU metrics</strong> (<code>CONFIG_MALI_TRACE_POWER_GPU_WORK_PERIOD</code>): per-application GPU active periods (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_gpu_metrics.c\"><code>mali_kbase_gpu_metrics.c</code></a>).</li></ul>","how":"<p>Use <code>KBASE_KTRACE_ADD(kbdev, CODE, kctx, info)</code> to add a trace point (see uses in <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/606\"><code>kbase_csf_interrupt()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c@3074\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:3074\">csf/mali_kbase_csf.c:3074</a>)</span>); timeline helpers are macros named <code>KBASE_TLSTREAM_*</code> generated in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/tl/mali_kbase_tracepoints.h\"><code>tl/mali_kbase_tracepoints.h</code></a>.</p>","locking":"<p>KTrace's ring buffer uses an IRQ-safe spinlock (see <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/143\"><code>struct kbase_ktrace</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/debug/mali_kbase_debug_ktrace_defs.h@165\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/debug/mali_kbase_debug_ktrace_defs.h:165\">debug/mali_kbase_debug_ktrace_defs.h:165</a>)</span>); timeline streams use per-stream locks.</p>","talks":"<p>Every subsystem emits trace events; debugfs entries live next to the code they inspect.</p>","debug":"<p>Start with <code>dmesg</code>, then <code>ktrace</code> in debugfs, then a timeline capture. For hangs on CSF, read the sync state dump and firmware log.</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[143,""],[142,""],[373,""],[374,""]],"fns":[[[1392],""],[[3276],""],[[3295],""],[[2082],""],[[3281],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"How does a profiler get the timeline stream?","o":["Reading /proc","KBASE_IOCTL_TLSTREAM_ACQUIRE returns a new fd","ftrace only","sysfs"],"a":1,"e":"<p><a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/3295\"><code>kbase_timeline_io_acquire()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/tl/mali_kbase_timeline_io.c@367\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/tl/mali_kbase_timeline_io.c:367\">tl/mali_kbase_timeline_io.c:367</a>)</span> → <code>anon_inode_getfd(\"[mali_tlstream]\", …)</code>.</p>"}],"locks":[]},{"id":"arbiter","title":"Arbiter, virtualization & protected mode","short":"Sharing the GPU; secure content","tag":"both","color":"#4d2d00","purpose":"<p><strong>Arbiter</strong> (<a class=\"cfgref\" href=\"#/config/CONFIG_MALI_ARBITER_SUPPORT\"><code>CONFIG_MALI_ARBITER_SUPPORT</code></a>, <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/arbiter/mali_kbase_arbiter_pm.c\"><code>arbiter/mali_kbase_arbiter_pm.c</code></a>): when several virtual machines share one GPU, an external <em>arbiter</em> grants the GPU to one VM at a time. The driver runs a VM state machine (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/6\"><code>enum kbase_vm_state</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/arbiter/mali_kbase_arbiter_pm.h@57\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/arbiter/mali_kbase_arbiter_pm.h:57\">arbiter/mali_kbase_arbiter_pm.h:57</a>)</span>): <code>INITIALIZING → … → IDLE/ACTIVE → SUSPEND_PENDING → STOPPED</code>. The arbiter interface is defined in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/include/linux/mali_arbiter_interface.h\"><code>include/linux/mali_arbiter_interface.h</code></a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Protected mode</strong> (<a class=\"term\" href=\"#/glossary/protected-mode\">protected mode</a>): runs work on secure (DRM-protected) buffers that the normal world cannot read.</p>\n<ul><li>Switching is done by a platform <em>protected mode switcher</em> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/include/linux/protected_mode_switcher.h\"><code>include/linux/protected_mode_switcher.h</code></a>).</li><li>Memory comes from the <em>protected memory allocator</em> module (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/base/arm/protected_memory_allocator/protected_memory_allocator.c\"><code>drivers/base/arm/protected_memory_allocator/protected_memory_allocator.c</code></a>).</li><li>On JM the backend ringbuffer has extra states for entering and exiting protected mode (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/206\"><code>kbase_jm_enter_protected_mode()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c@596\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c:596\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c:596</a>)</span>).</li><li>On CSF the firmware enters protected mode for a group on request (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1201\"><code>kbase_csf_scheduler_group_protm_enter()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c@6194\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:6194\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c:6194</a>)</span>), using memory from <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_protected_memory.c\"><code>csf/mali_kbase_csf_protected_memory.c</code></a>.</li></ul>","how":"<p>With the arbiter, PM calls are routed through <code>kbase_arbiter_pm_vm_event</code> (see <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2815\"><code>kbase_pm_suspend()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c@370\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c:370\">mali_kbase_pm.c:370</a>)</span>), and the GPU may be <em>lost</em> (<code>kbase_pm_is_gpu_lost</code>), which many code paths check.</p>","locking":"<p><a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_arbiter_vm_state::vm_state_lock\"><code>kbase_arbiter_vm_state::vm_state_lock</code></a> protects the VM state machine.</p>","talks":"<p><a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/pm\">Power management</a> (suspend/resume become VM events), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/jm\">Job Manager back-end (JD / JS / job slots)</a>/<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csf\">CSF queues, groups &amp; scheduler</a> (protected atoms/groups), <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/reset\">GPU reset &amp; fault recovery</a>.</p>","debug":"<p>debugfs <code>protected_debug_mode</code>; module param <code>gpu_req_timeout</code> (arbiter).</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[[4,""],[6,"VM state enum"]],"fns":[[[62],""],[[49],""],[[206],""],[[1201],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"Is arbiter code compiled by default?","o":["Yes","No: CONFIG_MALI_ARBITER_SUPPORT defaults to n","Only on CSF","Only on JM"],"a":1,"e":"<p>See <a class=\"cfgref\" href=\"#/config/CONFIG_MALI_ARBITER_SUPPORT\"><code>CONFIG_MALI_ARBITER_SUPPORT</code></a> (default n) and <code>arbiter/Kbuild</code> being included only when it is set.</p>"}],"locks":["kbase_arbiter_vm_state::vm_state_lock"]},{"id":"build","title":"Build system & configuration","short":"Kbuild, Kconfig, what gets compiled","tag":"both","color":"#24292f","purpose":"<p>The driver can be built in-tree or out-of-tree:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Kconfig</strong> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kconfig\"><code>Kconfig</code></a>) defines options; the full generated list is on the <a href=\"#/config\">configuration page</a>.</li><li><strong>Kbuild</strong> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild\"><code>Kbuild</code></a>) lists objects. It turns <code>CONFIG_MALI_CSF_SUPPORT</code> into <code>-DMALI_USE_CSF=1/0</code> (<span class=\"inref\">here</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild@97\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild:97\">Kbuild:97</a>)</span>) and includes the per-directory Kbuild files.</li><li><strong>Makefile</strong> (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Makefile\"><code>Makefile</code></a>) supplies defaults for out-of-tree builds (<code>CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD ?= m</code>, …).</li><li>Bazel/Android <code>build.bp</code>/<code>Mconfig</code> files are for Arm's internal build systems.</li><li><code>config/fragment/*.fragment</code> are ready-made Kconfig fragments (debug, no-mali, platforms).</li></ul>\n<p>The <strong>source map</strong> shows, for every <code>.c</code> file, the exact Kbuild condition under which it is compiled. That condition is computed by <code>tools/build_index.py</code> from the Kbuild files.</p>","how":"<p>Typical out-of-tree build: <code>make -C &lt;kernel&gt; M=$PWD/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD=m CONFIG_MALI_CSF_SUPPORT=y …</code> (exact variables are in the Makefile). The resulting module is <code>mali_kbase.ko</code> plus optional <code>memory_group_manager.ko</code>, <code>protected_memory_allocator.ko</code> and KUTF test modules.</p>","locking":"","talks":"","debug":"<p><code>CONFIG_MALI_DEBUG</code> enables asserts (<code>KBASE_DEBUG_ASSERT</code>), extra checks and KUTF; <code>CONFIG_MALI_NO_MALI</code> builds against a software GPU model, useful for learning without hardware.</p>","pitfalls":"","structs":[],"fns":[],"quiz":[{"q":"Where does MALI_USE_CSF come from?","o":["A header #define","Kbuild sets -DMALI_USE_CSF from CONFIG_MALI_CSF_SUPPORT","The firmware","Device tree"],"a":1,"e":"<p><span class=\"inref\">Kbuild</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild@97\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild:97\">Kbuild:97</a>)</span> and the <code>ccflags-y</code> list.</p>"}],"locks":[]},{"id":"tests","title":"KUTF kernel tests","short":"In-kernel unit test framework","tag":"both","color":"#57606a","purpose":"<p><strong>KUTF</strong> (Kernel Unit Test Framework, <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/tests/kutf/kutf_suite.c\"><code>tests/kutf/kutf_suite.c</code></a>) runs test suites inside the kernel and reports results through debugfs. The included tests:</p>\n<ul><li>IRQ latency (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/tests/mali_kutf_irq_test/mali_kutf_irq_test_main.c\"><code>tests/mali_kutf_irq_test/mali_kutf_irq_test_main.c</code></a>)</li><li>clock rate trace (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/tests/mali_kutf_clk_rate_trace/kernel/mali_kutf_clk_rate_trace_test.c\"><code>tests/mali_kutf_clk_rate_trace/kernel/mali_kutf_clk_rate_trace_test.c</code></a>)</li><li>memory group manager integration</li></ul>","how":"<p>Enable <code>CONFIG_MALI_KUTF</code> (needs <code>CONFIG_MALI_DEBUG</code> in the default Makefile flow). Each test module registers suites with <code>kutf_create_application</code>/<code>kutf_create_suite</code>.</p>","locking":"","talks":"<p>Tests call into <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwaccess\">Register access, GPU properties &amp; interrupts</a> (custom IRQ handlers via <code>kbase_set_custom_irq_handler</code>) and <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/dvfs\">DVFS, devfreq &amp; thermal (IPA)</a>.</p>","debug":"","pitfalls":"","structs":[[358,""],[357,""]],"fns":[[[3202],""],[[3200],""]],"quiz":[{"q":"Where do KUTF tests run?","o":["In userspace against /dev/mali0","Inside the kernel, as separate test modules","On the GPU firmware","Only in the NO_MALI model"],"a":1,"e":"<p>They are kernel modules (e.g. <code>kutf.ko</code>, <code>mali_kutf_irq_test.ko</code>) built by <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/tests/Kbuild\"><code>tests/Kbuild</code></a> when <code>CONFIG_MALI_KUTF</code> is set.</p>"}],"locks":[]}],"flows":[{"id":"load","title":"Driver load: module init → probe → HW init → ready","summary":"<p>What happens between <code>insmod mali_kbase.ko</code> and <code>/dev/mali0</code> appearing.</p>","lanes":[["vfs","Linux kernel core"],["core","kbase Linux glue (core_linux)"],["dev","Device / context init"],["plat","Platform (clocks/regulators)"],["pm","Power mgmt"],["hw","GPU hardware"]],"tag":"both","intro":"","dataflow":"<ul><li>**Device tree node → <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/232\"><code>struct kbase_io_resources</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_config.h@445\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_config.h:445\">mali_kbase_config.h:445</a>)</span>:** reg window and IRQs, read by <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1927\"><code>kbase_get_irqs()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@479\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:479\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:479</a>)</span> and <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2066\"><code>registers_map()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@4514\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4514\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:4514</a>)</span>.</li><li><strong>Register window → <code>kbdev-&gt;reg</code>:</strong> an ioremapped address.</li><li><strong>DT clocks and supplies → <code>kbdev-&gt;clocks[]</code>, <code>kbdev-&gt;regulators[]</code>.</strong></li><li>**GPU_ID and feature registers → <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/294\"><code>struct kbase_gpu_props</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_gpuprops_types.h@228\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_gpuprops_types.h:228\">mali_kbase_gpuprops_types.h:228</a>)</span> → a \"prop buffer\":** userspace later reads it with <code>GET_GPUPROPS</code>.</li><li><strong>The init table index <code>i</code>:</strong> the only state needed to undo a partial init.</li></ul>","notes":"","steps":[{"lane":"vfs","to":"core","title":"module_init calls kbase_driver_init","tag":"both","text":"<p>Runs when the module is loaded. Registers the platform driver so the kernel can match it to the GPU's device-tree node.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbase_platform_driver</code>: name <code>\"mali\"</code>, PM ops, the <code>kbase_dt_ids</code> match table.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2113,"name":"kbase_driver_init","line":6238,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":6238,"focus":6238,"lines":["static int __init kbase_driver_init(void)","{","\tint ret;","","#if (KERNEL_VERSION(5, 3, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)","\tmutex_init(&kbase_probe_mutex);","#endif","","#ifndef CONFIG_OF","\tret = kbase_platform_register();","\tif (ret)","\t\treturn ret;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"vfs","title":"Register the platform driver","tag":"both","text":"<p>The kernel walks platform devices. Any node whose <code>compatible</code> matches <code>arm,mali-*</code> triggers probe (asynchronously: <code>PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS</code>).</p>","data":"<p>Match table <span class=\"inref\">kbase_dt_ids</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@6216\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6216\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6216</a>)</span>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2113,"name":"kbase_driver_init","line":6251,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":6248,"focus":6251,"lines":["\tif (ret)","\t\treturn ret;","#endif","\tret = platform_driver_register(&kbase_platform_driver);","#ifndef CONFIG_OF","\tif (ret) {","\t\tkbase_platform_unregister();","\t\treturn ret;","\t}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"vfs","to":"core","title":"Probe: allocate the device","tag":"both","text":"<p>Allocates an empty <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/266\"><code>struct kbase_device</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@1083\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:1083\">mali_kbase_defs.h:1083</a>)</span> and links it to the <code>struct device</code> (<code>dev_set_drvdata</code>).</p>","data":"<p>New <code>kbdev</code> (zeroed), <code>kbdev-&gt;dev = &amp;pdev-&gt;dev</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2107,"name":"kbase_platform_device_probe","line":5961,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":5958,"focus":5961,"lines":["","\tmali_kbase_print_cs_experimental();","","\tkbdev = kbase_device_alloc();","\tif (!kbdev) {","\t\tdev_err(&pdev->dev, \"Allocate device failed\\n\");","\t\treturn -ENOMEM;","\t}",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"dev","title":"kbase_device_init walks dev_init[]","tag":"both","text":"<p>Calls each <code>{init, term}</code> row in order. On error it unwinds rows <code>i-1..0</code>. The CSF version has a different table, with <code>kbase_csf_early_init</code>/<code>late_init</code>.</p>","data":"<p>Loop index <code>i</code> = how far init got.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1448,"name":"kbase_device_init","line":311,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c","start":308,"focus":311,"lines":["","\tfor (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev_init); i++) {","\t\tif (dev_init[i].init) {","\t\t\terr = dev_init[i].init(kbdev);","\t\t\tif (err) {","\t\t\t\tif (err != -EPROBE_DEFER)","\t\t\t\t\tdev_err(kbdev->dev, \"%s error = %d\\n\", dev_init[i].err_mes,","\t\t\t\t\t\terr);","\t\t\t\tkbase_device_term_partial(kbdev, i);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"plat","title":"Find IRQs","tag":"both","text":"<p>Reads the IRQ resources from the platform device: names <code>JOB</code>, <code>MMU</code>, <code>GPU</code>, or a single combined IRQ.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;irqs[]</code>, <code>kbdev-&gt;nr_irqs</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1927,"name":"kbase_get_irqs","line":479,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":479,"focus":479,"lines":["int kbase_get_irqs(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{","\tint result;","\tstruct platform_device *pdev = to_platform_device(kbdev->dev);","","\tkbdev->nr_irqs = 0;","\tresult = get_irqs(kbdev, pdev);","\tif (!result)","\t\treturn result;","","\tif (result)","\t\tdev_err(kbdev->dev, \"Invalid or No interrupt resources\");"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"plat","title":"Map registers","tag":"both","text":"<p>Gets the MEM resource and <code>ioremap</code>s the GPU register window.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;reg_start</code>, <code>kbdev-&gt;reg_size</code>, <code>kbdev-&gt;reg</code> (CPU virtual address of registers).</p>","kind":"call","fn":2066,"name":"registers_map","line":4514,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":4514,"focus":4514,"lines":["int registers_map(struct kbase_device *const kbdev)","{","\t/* the first memory resource is the physical address of the GPU","\t * registers.","\t */","\tstruct platform_device *pdev = to_platform_device(kbdev->dev);","\tstruct resource *reg_res;","\tint err;","","\treg_res = platform_get_resource(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, 0);","\tif (!reg_res) {","\t\tdev_err(kbdev->dev, \"Invalid register resource\\n\");"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"plat","title":"Get clocks & regulators","tag":"both","text":"<p>Looks up up to <code>BASE_MAX_NR_CLOCKS_REGULATORS</code> clocks and regulators from DT, and optionally power domains.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;clocks[i]</code>, <code>kbdev-&gt;regulators[i]</code>, <code>kbdev-&gt;nr_clocks</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2072,"name":"power_control_init","line":4730,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":4727,"focus":4730,"lines":["\t * operating with a partial initialization of clocks.","\t */","\tfor (i = 0; i < BASE_MAX_NR_CLOCKS_REGULATORS; i++) {","\t\tkbdev->clocks[i] = of_clk_get(kbdev->dev->of_node, (int)i);","\t\tif (IS_ERR(kbdev->clocks[i])) {","\t\t\terr = PTR_ERR(kbdev->clocks[i]);","\t\t\tkbdev->clocks[i] = NULL;","\t\t\tbreak;","\t\t}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"hw","title":"Early init: GPU ID, register map, IRQs","tag":"both","text":"<p>Reads <code>GPU_ID</code>, builds the register map for that GPU version, initialises GPU properties, and <strong>installs the IRQ handlers</strong>. From here on the GPU can interrupt the CPU.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;gpu_props</code>, <code>kbdev-&gt;regmap</code>, registered IRQ handlers.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1478,"name":"kbase_device_early_init","line":557,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c","start":554,"focus":557,"lines":["\t\tif (kbdev->pm.arb_vm_state)","\t\t\terr = kbase_arbiter_pm_install_interrupts(kbdev);","\t} else {","\t\terr = kbase_install_interrupts(kbdev);","\t}","#else","\terr = kbase_install_interrupts(kbdev);","#endif",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"dev","title":"Memory subsystem init","tag":"both","text":"<p>Device-wide memory state: the device page pools (small and 2 MB), the memory group manager, and the DMA-buf tracking tree.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;mem_pools</code>, <code>kbdev-&gt;mgm_dev</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2488,"name":"kbase_mem_init","line":198,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c","start":198,"focus":198,"lines":["int kbase_mem_init(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{","\tint err = 0;","\tchar va_region_slab_name[VA_REGION_SLAB_NAME_SIZE];","#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_OF)","\tstruct device_node *mgm_node = NULL;","#endif","","\tKBASE_DEBUG_ASSERT(kbdev);","","\tkbasep_mem_page_size_init(kbdev);",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"pm","title":"Backend late init: first power-up","tag":"both","text":"<p>Initialises PM and reset, then <strong>powers the GPU</strong> for the first time and runs <code>kbase_pm_init_hw</code> (soft reset, apply workarounds).</p>","data":"<p>PM backend state, <code>gpu_powered = true</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1438,"name":"kbase_backend_late_init","line":68,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c","start":65,"focus":68,"lines":["\tif (err)","\t\tgoto fail_reset_gpu_init;","","\terr = kbase_hwaccess_pm_powerup(kbdev, PM_HW_ISSUES_DETECT);","\tif (err)","\t\tgoto fail_pm_powerup;","","\terr = kbase_backend_timer_init(kbdev);","\tif (err)"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_jm.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"hw","title":"Power on + soft reset the GPU","tag":"both","text":"<p>Turns on clocks via platform callbacks, then resets and configures the GPU.</p>","data":"<p>Hardware is now in a known state.</p>","kind":"call","fn":295,"name":"kbase_hwaccess_pm_powerup","line":730,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c","start":727,"focus":730,"lines":["\t/* Power up the GPU, don't enable IRQs as we are not ready to receive","\t * them","\t */","\tret = kbase_pm_init_hw(kbdev, flags);","\tif (ret) {","\t\tkbase_pm_unlock(kbdev);","\t\treturn ret;","\t}","#if MALI_USE_CSF"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"vfs","title":"Create /dev/maliN","tag":"both","text":"<p>Registers a misc character device whose fops are <code>kbase_fops</code>. sysfs attributes were created just before, so udev sees them.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;mdev</code> (miscdevice), device name <code>mali%d</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1472,"name":"kbase_device_misc_register","line":443,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c","start":443,"focus":443,"lines":["int kbase_device_misc_register(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{","\treturn misc_register(&kbdev->mdev);","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"vfs","title":"Probe done","tag":"both","text":"<p>Logs the device name. On CSF the firmware is still not loaded; that happens on first open.</p>","data":"<p>Kernel log: <code>Probed as mali0</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2107,"name":"kbase_platform_device_probe","line":6001,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":5998,"focus":6001,"lines":["\t\tdev_info(kbdev->dev, KBASE_COMPILED_MMAP_MIN_ADDR_MSG);","#endif","","\t\tdev_info(kbdev->dev, \"Probed as %s\\n\", dev_name(kbdev->mdev.this_device));","\t\tif (PAGE_SHIFT != 12)","\t\t\tdev_warn(kbdev->dev, \"Experimental feature: %s with Page Size of %luKiB\",","\t\t\t\t dev_name(kbdev->mdev.this_device), PAGE_SIZE / 1024);","","\t\tkbase_increment_device_id();"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"}]},{"id":"open","title":"Userspace opens the device and creates a context","summary":"<p><code>open()</code> → (CSF: firmware load) → <code>VERSION_CHECK</code> → <code>SET_FLAGS</code> → a ready <code>kbase_context</code>.</p>","lanes":[["user","Userspace (UMD / app)"],["vfs","Linux kernel core"],["core","kbase Linux glue (core_linux)"],["dev","Device / context init"],["fw","MCU firmware"],["mem","Memory mgmt"],["mmu","GPU MMU"]],"tag":"both","intro":"","dataflow":"<ul><li>**File descriptor → <code>struct file</code> → <code>filp-&gt;private_data</code> = <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/268\"><code>struct kbase_file</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@1434\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:1434\">mali_kbase_defs.h:1434</a>)</span>.**</li><li><strong>The process's ABI version (major.minor) → <code>kfile-&gt;api_version</code>:</strong> negotiated by the handshake.</li><li>**Create flags → <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/272\"><code>struct kbase_context</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@1888\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:1888\">mali_kbase_defs.h:1888</a>)</span>:** this holds the MMU root page, VA zones, pools and backend state.</li><li><strong>CSF only: <code>mali_csffw.bin</code> → <code>kbdev-&gt;csf.fw</code> (vmalloc copy) → sections copied into GPU memory and mapped in the MCU AS.</strong></li></ul>","notes":"","steps":[{"lane":"user","to":"vfs","title":"open(\"/dev/mali0\")","tag":"both","text":"<p>VFS calls <code>kbase_fops.open</code>.</p>","data":"<p>inode minor number → which GPU.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1938,"name":"kbase_open","line":738,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":738,"focus":738,"lines":["static int kbase_open(struct inode *inode, struct file *filp)","{","\tstruct kbase_device *kbdev = NULL;","\tstruct kbase_file *kfile;","\tint ret = 0;","","\tkbdev = kbase_find_device((int)iminor(inode));","","\tif (!kbdev)","\t\treturn -ENODEV;","","#if (KERNEL_VERSION(6, 0, 0) > LINUX_VERSION_CODE)"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"dev","title":"Find the device","tag":"both","text":"<p>Maps the minor number to a <code>kbase_device</code> and takes a reference.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev</code> pointer.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1938,"name":"kbase_open","line":744,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":741,"focus":744,"lines":["\tstruct kbase_file *kfile;","\tint ret = 0;","","\tkbdev = kbase_find_device((int)iminor(inode));","","\tif (!kbdev)","\t\treturn -ENODEV;","","#if (KERNEL_VERSION(6, 0, 0) > LINUX_VERSION_CODE)"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"fw","title":"Firmware init (once)","tag":"both","text":"<p>On CSF the first opener loads the MCU firmware. On JM it only loads the optional dummy-job workaround binary.</p>","data":"<p>CSF: <code>kbdev-&gt;csf.firmware_inited</code> becomes true.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1938,"name":"kbase_open","line":757,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":754,"focus":757,"lines":["\t/* Device-wide firmware load is moved here from probing to comply with","\t * Android GKI vendor guideline.","\t */","\tret = kbase_device_firmware_init_once(kbdev);","\tif (ret)","\t\tgoto out;","","\tkfile = kbase_file_new(kbdev, filp);","\tif (!kfile) {"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"fw","title":"CSF: load firmware image","tag":"CSF","text":"<p>Reads the file (default <code>mali_csffw.bin</code>, DT <code>firmware-name</code> or module param <code>fw_name</code>), checks the magic and version, and parses entries.</p>","data":"<p>Firmware bytes → <code>mcu_fw-&gt;data</code>; then one <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/86\"><code>struct kbase_csf_firmware_interface</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h@1415\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:1415\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:1415</a>)</span> per section.</p>","kind":"call","fn":765,"name":"kbase_csf_firmware_load_init","line":2451,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c","start":2448,"focus":2451,"lines":["","#endif /* IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_OF) */","","\tif (request_firmware(&firmware, fw_name, kbdev->dev) != 0) {","\t\tdev_err(kbdev->dev, \"Failed to load firmware image '%s'\\n\", fw_name);","\t\tret = -ENOENT;","\t} else {","\t\t/* Try to save a copy and then release the loaded firmware image */","\t\tmcu_fw->size = firmware->size;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"fw","title":"CSF: boot the MCU","tag":"CSF","text":"<p>Loads the MCU page tables into the MCU AS, enables the MCU and waits for boot. After this the driver reads the firmware's interface and capabilities, starts the scheduler, and sends the global init.</p>","data":"<p>Shared interface pages: <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/102\"><code>struct kbase_csf_global_iface</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h@266\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h:266\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.h:266</a>)</span> + per-CSG/CS info.</p>","kind":"call","fn":765,"name":"kbase_csf_firmware_load_init","line":2559,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c","start":2556,"focus":2559,"lines":["\tif (ret != 0)","\t\tgoto err_out;","","\tboot_csf_firmware(kbdev);","","\tret = parse_capabilities(kbdev);","\tif (ret != 0)","\t\tgoto err_out;",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"core","title":"Allocate kbase_file","tag":"both","text":"<p>Creates the per-fd object in state <code>KBASE_FILE_NEED_CTX</code>. No context yet.</p>","data":"<p><a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/268\"><code>struct kbase_file</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@1434\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:1434\">mali_kbase_defs.h:1434</a>)</span> → <code>filp-&gt;private_data</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1916,"name":"kbase_file_new","line":220,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":220,"focus":220,"lines":["static struct kbase_file *kbase_file_new(struct kbase_device *const kbdev, struct file *const filp)","{","\tstruct kbase_file *const kfile = kmalloc(sizeof(*kfile), GFP_KERNEL);","","\tif (kfile) {","\t\tkfile->kbdev = kbdev;","\t\tkfile->filp = filp;","\t\tkfile->kctx = NULL;","\t\tkfile->api_version = 0;","\t\tatomic_set(&kfile->setup_state, KBASE_FILE_NEED_VSN);","\t}","\treturn kfile;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"user","to":"core","title":"ioctl VERSION_CHECK","tag":"both","text":"<p>Userspace sends its ABI version and the kernel answers with what it supports. JM and CSF have different version numbers.</p>","data":"<p><a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/421\"><code>struct kbase_ioctl_version_check</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_ioctl.h@131\" title=\"include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_ioctl.h:131\">include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_ioctl.h:131</a>)</span> in/out; stored in <code>kfile-&gt;api_version</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1921,"name":"kbase_api_handshake","line":365,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":365,"focus":365,"lines":["static int kbase_api_handshake(struct kbase_file *kfile, struct kbase_ioctl_version_check *version)","{","\tint err = 0;","","\tswitch (version->major) {","\tcase BASE_UK_VERSION_MAJOR:","\t\t/* set minor to be the lowest common */","\t\tversion->minor = min_t(int, BASE_UK_VERSION_MINOR, (int)version->minor);","\t\tbreak;","\tdefault:","\t\t/* We return our actual version regardless if it","\t\t * matches the version returned by userspace -"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"user","to":"core","title":"ioctl SET_FLAGS","tag":"both","text":"<p>Validates the create flags and creates the context.</p>","data":"<p><a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/504\"><code>struct kbase_ioctl_set_flags</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ioctl.h@45\" title=\"include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ioctl.h:45\">include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ioctl.h:45</a>)</span> → <code>create_flags</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1940,"name":"kbase_api_set_flags","line":803,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":800,"focus":803,"lines":["\t * the flags were set.","\t */","\tif (mali_kbase_supports_system_monitor(api_version)) {","\t\terr = kbase_file_create_kctx(kfile, flags->create_flags);","\t} else {","#if !MALI_USE_CSF","\t\tstruct kbasep_js_kctx_info *js_kctx_info = NULL;","\t\tunsigned long irq_flags = 0;","#endif"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"dev","title":"Guard against double creation","tag":"both","text":"<p>An atomic compare-exchange moves NEED_CTX → CTX_IN_PROGRESS, so only one thread proceeds.</p>","data":"<p><code>kfile-&gt;setup_state</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1937,"name":"kbase_file_create_kctx","line":692,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":689,"focus":692,"lines":["\t/* setup pending, try to signal that we'll do the setup,","\t * if setup was already in progress, err this call","\t */","\tif (atomic_cmpxchg(&kfile->setup_state, KBASE_FILE_NEED_CTX, KBASE_FILE_CTX_IN_PROGRESS) !=","\t    KBASE_FILE_NEED_CTX)","\t\treturn -EPERM;","","\tkbdev = kfile->kbdev;",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"dev","title":"kbase_create_context walks context_init[]","tag":"both","text":"<p><code>vzalloc</code>s the context and runs each init step (the JM table differs only in backend rows).</p>","data":"<p>New <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/272\"><code>struct kbase_context</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@1888\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:1888\">mali_kbase_defs.h:1888</a>)</span>: <code>kbdev</code>, <code>api_version</code>, <code>comm</code>, flags (<code>KCTX_COMPAT</code> / <code>KCTX_FORCE_SAME_VA</code>).</p>","kind":"call","fn":470,"name":"kbase_create_context","line":153,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c","start":150,"focus":153,"lines":["\tfor (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(context_init); i++) {","\t\tint err = 0;","","\t\tif (context_init[i].init)","\t\t\terr = context_init[i].init(kctx);","","\t\tif (err) {","\t\t\tdev_err(kbdev->dev, \"%s error = %d\\n\", context_init[i].err_mes, err);",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"mmu","title":"Create the context's page table","tag":"both","text":"<p>Allocates the top-level page directory. The context now has its own GPU virtual address space, not yet bound to any hardware AS.</p>","data":"<p><code>kctx-&gt;mmu.pgd</code> (physical address of level-0 table).</p>","kind":"call","fn":494,"name":"kbase_context_mmu_init","line":308,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c","start":308,"focus":308,"lines":["int kbase_context_mmu_init(struct kbase_context *kctx)","{","\treturn kbase_mmu_init(kctx->kbdev, &kctx->mmu, kctx,","\t\t\t      kbase_context_mmu_group_id_get(kctx->create_flags));","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"mem","title":"Create VA zones","tag":"both","text":"<p>Sets up the SAME_VA, CUSTOM_VA and EXEC_VA (+ CSF FIXED/EXEC_FIXED) zones with their red-black trees.</p>","data":"<p><code>kctx-&gt;reg_zone[]</code> (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/332\"><code>struct kbase_reg_zone</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.h@172\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.h:172\">mali_kbase_reg_track.h:172</a>)</span>).</p>","kind":"call","fn":2851,"name":"kbase_region_tracker_init","line":961,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.c","start":961,"focus":961,"lines":["int kbase_region_tracker_init(struct kbase_context *kctx)","{","\tconst u64 gpu_va_bits = kctx->kbdev->gpu_props.mmu.va_bits;","\tconst u64 gpu_va_limit = (1ULL << gpu_va_bits) >> PAGE_SHIFT;","\tint err;","\tunsigned int i;","","\t/* Take the lock as kbase_free_alloced_region requires it */","\tkbase_gpu_vm_lock(kctx);","","\tfor (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(zones_init); i++) {","\t\terr = zones_init[i].init(kctx, gpu_va_limit);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"dev","title":"CSF: per-context CSF state","tag":"CSF","text":"<p>Queue group table, KCPU queues, tiler heaps, event wait queue, CPU-queue dump support.</p>","data":"<p><code>kctx-&gt;csf</code> (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/74\"><code>struct kbase_csf_context</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h@892\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:892\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:892</a>)</span>).</p>","kind":"call","fn":580,"name":"kbase_csf_ctx_init","line":1644,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c","start":1644,"focus":1644,"lines":["int kbase_csf_ctx_init(struct kbase_context *kctx)","{","\tint err = -ENOMEM;","","\tINIT_LIST_HEAD(&kctx->csf.queue_list);","\tINIT_LIST_HEAD(&kctx->csf.link);","\tatomic_set(&kctx->csf.pending_sync_update, 0);","","\tkbase_csf_event_init(kctx);","","\t/* Mark all the cookies as 'free' */","\tbitmap_fill(kctx->csf.cookies, KBASE_CSF_NUM_USER_IO_PAGES_HANDLE);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"user","title":"Context ready","tag":"both","text":"<p>Creates the per-context debugfs dir and marks setup complete. Every other ioctl now works.</p>","data":"<p><code>kfile-&gt;kctx = kctx</code>, <code>setup_state = KBASE_FILE_COMPLETE</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1937,"name":"kbase_file_create_kctx","line":733,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":730,"focus":733,"lines":["\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \"created base context\\n\");","","\tkfile->kctx = kctx;","\tatomic_set(&kfile->setup_state, KBASE_FILE_COMPLETE);","","\treturn 0;","}","","static int kbase_open(struct inode *inode, struct file *filp)"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"}]},{"id":"memalloc","title":"GPU memory allocation and mapping into the GPU address space","summary":"<p><code>MEM_ALLOC</code> → region + physical pages → (SAME_VA) cookie → <code>mmap()</code> → GPU page table entries → TLB flush.</p>","lanes":[["user","Userspace (UMD / app)"],["core","kbase Linux glue (core_linux)"],["mem","Memory mgmt"],["mmu","GPU MMU"],["hw","GPU hardware"]],"tag":"both","intro":"","dataflow":"<ul><li><strong>Request:</strong> <code>va_pages</code>, <code>commit_pages</code>, <code>extension</code>, <code>flags</code> in <code>union kbase_ioctl_mem_alloc</code>.</li><li><strong>Virtual range:</strong> a <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/319\"><code>struct kbase_va_region</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.h@665\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.h:665\">mali_kbase_mem.h:665</a>)</span> in a zone rbtree.</li><li><strong>Physical pages:</strong> first the context pool, then the device pool, then <code>mgm_alloc_page</code> (the kernel). They are stored as <code>tagged_addr</code> in <code>gpu_alloc-&gt;pages[]</code>.</li><li><strong>SAME_VA:</strong> the region is parked in <code>kctx-&gt;pending_regions[cookie]</code>, and the cookie is returned to userspace.</li><li><strong><code>mmap(offset = cookie)</code>:</strong> the CPU VA chosen by the kernel (<code>vma-&gt;vm_start</code>) becomes the region's GPU VA.</li><li><strong>Page table entries (ATEs):</strong> written into the table pages. The GPU TLB is invalidated through MMU registers, but only if the context currently owns a hardware AS.</li></ul>","notes":"","steps":[{"lane":"user","to":"core","title":"ioctl MEM_ALLOC","tag":"both","text":"<p>Copies in the request. A 64-bit client is forced to SAME_VA (except executable memory when an EXEC_VA zone exists). The CSF variant wraps <code>kbase_api_mem_alloc_ex</code>.</p>","data":"<p><code>union kbase_ioctl_mem_alloc</code> (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/506\"><code>union kbase_ioctl_mem_alloc</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ioctl.h@96\" title=\"include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ioctl.h:96\">include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_ioctl.h:96</a>)</span>).</p>","kind":"call","fn":1946,"name":"kbase_api_mem_alloc","line":989,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":989,"focus":989,"lines":["static int kbase_api_mem_alloc(struct kbase_context *kctx, union kbase_ioctl_mem_alloc *alloc)","{","\tstruct kbase_va_region *reg;","\tu64 flags = alloc->in.flags;","\tu64 gpu_va;","","\t/* Calls to this function are inherently asynchronous, with respect to","\t * MMU operations.","\t */","\tconst enum kbase_caller_mmu_sync_info mmu_sync_info = CALLER_MMU_ASYNC;","","\tif (!kbase_mem_allow_alloc(kctx))"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"mem","title":"kbase_mem_alloc: validate","tag":"both","text":"<p>Rejects invalid flag combinations and sizes.</p>","data":"<p><code>*flags</code>, <code>va_pages</code>, <code>commit_pages</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2628,"name":"kbase_mem_alloc","line":321,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c","start":318,"focus":321,"lines":["\telse","\t\tdev_dbg(dev, \"Keeping requested GPU VA of 0x%llx\\n\", (unsigned long long)*gpu_va);","","\tif (!kbase_check_alloc_flags(*flags)) {","\t\tdev_warn(dev, \"%s called with bad flags (%llx)\", __func__,","\t\t\t (unsigned long long)*flags);","\t\tgoto bad_flags;","\t}",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mem","title":"Pick a zone","tag":"both","text":"<p>SAME_VA, EXEC_VA (GPU-executable) or CUSTOM_VA.</p>","data":"<p><code>enum kbase_memory_zone zone</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2628,"name":"kbase_mem_alloc","line":365,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c","start":362,"focus":365,"lines":["","\t/* find out which VA zone to use */","\tif (*flags & BASE_MEM_SAME_VA)","\t\tzone = SAME_VA_ZONE;","#if MALI_USE_CSF","\t/* fixed va_zone always exists */","\telse if (*flags & (BASE_MEM_FIXED | BASE_MEM_FIXABLE)) {","\t\tif (*flags & BASE_MEM_PROT_GPU_EX) {","\t\t\tzone = EXEC_FIXED_VA_ZONE;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mem","title":"Allocate the region object","tag":"both","text":"<p>Creates a <code>kbase_va_region</code> (not yet inserted into the tree for SAME_VA).</p>","data":"<p><code>reg</code>: <code>start_pfn</code> (0 for SAME_VA until mmap), <code>nr_pages = va_pages</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2628,"name":"kbase_mem_alloc","line":382,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c","start":379,"focus":382,"lines":["\t\tzone = CUSTOM_VA_ZONE;","\t}","","\treg = kbase_ctx_alloc_free_region(kctx, zone, PFN_DOWN(*gpu_va), va_pages);","","\tif (!reg) {","\t\tdev_err(dev, \"Failed to allocate free region\");","\t\tgoto no_region;","\t}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mem","title":"Allocate physical pages","tag":"both","text":"<p>Allocates <code>commit_pages</code> pages for <code>cpu_alloc</code> (and <code>gpu_alloc</code> if separate).</p>","data":"<p><code>reg-&gt;gpu_alloc-&gt;pages[0..nents)</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2513,"name":"kbase_alloc_phy_pages","line":2000,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c","start":2000,"focus":2000,"lines":["int kbase_alloc_phy_pages(struct kbase_va_region *reg, size_t vsize, size_t size)","{","\tKBASE_DEBUG_ASSERT(reg != NULL);","\tKBASE_DEBUG_ASSERT(vsize > 0);","","\t/* validate user provided arguments */","\tif (size > vsize || vsize > reg->nr_pages)","\t\tgoto out_term;","","\t/* Prevent vsize*sizeof from wrapping around.","\t * For instance, if vsize is 2**29+1, we'll allocate 1 byte and the alloc won't fail.","\t */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mem","title":"From the page pools","tag":"both","text":"<p>Prefers 2 MB pages from <code>mem_pools.large[group]</code> if enabled and the size allows, else 4 KB from <code>mem_pools.small[group]</code>.</p>","data":"<p>Pages from the context pool.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2506,"name":"kbase_alloc_phy_pages_helper","line":1274,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c","start":1271,"focus":1274,"lines":["\tif (kbase_is_large_pages_enabled() && nr_left >= NUM_PAGES_IN_2MB_LARGE_PAGE) {","\t\tsize_t nr_lp = nr_left / NUM_PAGES_IN_2MB_LARGE_PAGE;","","\t\tres = kbase_mem_pool_alloc_pages(&kctx->mem_pools.large[alloc->group_id],","\t\t\t\t\t\t nr_lp * NUM_PAGES_IN_2MB_LARGE_PAGE, tp, true,","\t\t\t\t\t\t kctx->task);","","\t\tif (res > 0) {","\t\t\tnr_left -= (size_t)res;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mem","title":"Pool fall-back chain","tag":"both","text":"<p>Context pool → device pool (<code>next_pool</code>) → fresh pages from the kernel.</p>","data":"<p><code>struct page *</code> list.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2751,"name":"kbase_mem_pool_alloc_pages","line":737,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c","start":734,"focus":737,"lines":["\t}","\tkbase_mem_pool_unlock(pool);","","\tif (i != nr_small_pages && pool->next_pool) {","\t\t/* Allocate via next pool */","\t\terr = kbase_mem_pool_alloc_pages(pool->next_pool, nr_small_pages - i, pages + i,","\t\t\t\t\t\t partial_allowed, page_owner);","","\t\tif (err < 0)"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mem","title":"Fresh page from the kernel","tag":"both","text":"<p>Calls the memory group manager, then <code>dma_map_page</code> so CPU caches can be maintained.</p>","data":"<p><code>struct page</code> + DMA address stored in page private.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2734,"name":"kbase_mem_alloc_page","line":282,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c","start":279,"focus":282,"lines":["\telse","\t\tgfp |= kbase_is_page_migration_enabled() ? GFP_HIGHUSER_MOVABLE : GFP_HIGHUSER;","","\tp = kbdev->mgm_dev->ops.mgm_alloc_page(kbdev->mgm_dev, pool->group_id, gfp, pool->order);","\tif (!p)","\t\treturn NULL;","","\tdma_addr = dma_map_page(dev, p, 0, (PAGE_SIZE << pool->order), DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_pool.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"core","title":"SAME_VA: return a cookie","tag":"both","text":"<p>The GPU address isn't known yet. The region waits in <code>pending_regions[]</code> and userspace receives a cookie.</p>","data":"<p><code>gpu_va = cookie &lt;&lt; PAGE_SHIFT</code> (between <code>BASE_MEM_COOKIE_BASE</code> and <code>BASE_MEM_FIRST_FREE_ADDRESS</code>).</p>","kind":"call","fn":2628,"name":"kbase_mem_alloc","line":455,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c","start":452,"focus":455,"lines":["\t\tcookie_nr = find_first_bit(kctx->cookies, BITS_PER_LONG);","\t\tbitmap_clear(kctx->cookies, cookie_nr, 1);","\t\tBUG_ON(kctx->pending_regions[cookie_nr]);","\t\tkctx->pending_regions[cookie_nr] = reg;","","\t\t/* relocate to correct base */","\t\tcookie = cookie_nr + PFN_DOWN(BASE_MEM_COOKIE_BASE);","\t\tcookie <<= PAGE_SHIFT;",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c"},{"lane":"user","to":"core","title":"mmap(fd, offset=cookie)","tag":"both","text":"<p><code>kbase_mmap</code> → <code>kbase_context_mmap</code>. The offset falls in the cookie range.</p>","data":"<p><code>vma-&gt;vm_pgoff</code> = cookie page.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2667,"name":"kbase_context_mmap","line":2846,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c","start":2843,"focus":2846,"lines":["\t}","#endif","\tcase PFN_DOWN(BASE_MEM_COOKIE_BASE)... PFN_DOWN(BASE_MEM_FIRST_FREE_ADDRESS) - 1: {","\t\terr = kbasep_reg_mmap(kctx, vma, &reg, &nr_pages, &aligned_offset);","\t\tif (err != 0)","\t\t\tgoto out_unlock;","\t\t/* free the region on munmap */","\t\tfree_on_close = 1;","\t\tbreak;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mem","title":"Bind CPU VA = GPU VA","tag":"both","text":"<p>Now the GPU mapping is created at the address the kernel chose for the CPU mapping. The cookie is released.</p>","data":"<p><code>reg-&gt;start_pfn = vma-&gt;vm_start &gt;&gt; PAGE_SHIFT</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2666,"name":"kbasep_reg_mmap","line":2742,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c","start":2739,"focus":2742,"lines":["","\t/* adjust down nr_pages to what we have physically */","\t*nr_pages = kbase_reg_current_backed_size(reg);","\tif (kbase_gpu_mmap(kctx, reg, vma->vm_start + *aligned_offset, reg->nr_pages, 1,","\t\t\t   mmu_sync_info) != 0) {","\t\t/* Unable to map in GPU space. */","\t\tdev_err(kctx->kbdev->dev, \"%s:%d\\n\", __FILE__, __LINE__);","\t\terr = -ENOMEM;","\t\tgoto out;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mem","title":"Insert region into the zone tree","tag":"both","text":"<p>The region becomes findable by address (<code>kbase_region_tracker_find_region_enclosing_address</code>).</p>","data":"<p>Region in <code>reg_zone[SAME_VA].reg_rbtree</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2491,"name":"kbase_gpu_mmap","line":358,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c","start":355,"focus":358,"lines":["\tKBASE_DEBUG_ASSERT(kctx != NULL);","\tKBASE_DEBUG_ASSERT(reg != NULL);","","\terr = kbase_add_va_region(kctx, reg, addr, nr_pages, align);","\tif (err)","\t\treturn err;","","\talloc = reg->gpu_alloc;","\tgroup_id = alloc->group_id;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mmu","title":"Insert pages into GPU page tables","tag":"both","text":"<p>Native memory path. Imports use <code>kbase_mmu_insert_pages_skip_status_update</code>; aliases insert each slice.</p>","data":"<p><code>phys[] = kbase_get_gpu_phy_pages(reg)</code>, <code>flags</code> → PTE attributes.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2491,"name":"kbase_gpu_mmap","line":428,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c","start":425,"focus":428,"lines":["\t\t\t\tkbase_get_gpu_phy_pages(reg), kbase_reg_current_backed_size(reg),","\t\t\t\treg->flags & gwt_mask, kctx->as_nr, group_id, mmu_sync_info, reg);","\t\t} else {","\t\t\terr = kbase_mmu_insert_pages(kctx->kbdev, &kctx->mmu, reg->start_pfn,","\t\t\t\t\t\t     kbase_get_gpu_phy_pages(reg),","\t\t\t\t\t\t     kbase_reg_current_backed_size(reg),","\t\t\t\t\t\t     reg->flags & gwt_mask, kctx->as_nr, group_id,","\t\t\t\t\t\t     mmu_sync_info, reg);","\t\t}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.c"},{"lane":"mmu","to":"mmu","title":"Walk / allocate page-table levels","tag":"both","text":"<p>For each run of pages: find the lowest existing table, allocate missing levels (2 MB pages map at level 2), then write ATEs.</p>","data":"<p>New PGD pages; <code>dirty_pgds</code> bitmap of touched levels.</p>","kind":"call","fn":3019,"name":"mmu_insert_pages_no_flush","line":2773,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c","start":2770,"focus":2773,"lines":["\t\t\t/* Allocate new pgds for all missing levels from the required level","\t\t\t * down to the lowest valid pgd at insert_level","\t\t\t */","\t\t\terr = mmu_insert_alloc_pgds(kbdev, mmut, new_pgds, (insert_level + 1),","\t\t\t\t\t\t    cur_level, &pool_grown);","\t\t\tif (err)","\t\t\t\tgoto fail_unlock_free_pgds;","","\t\t\tif (pool_grown)"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c"},{"lane":"mmu","to":"mmu","title":"Write a leaf entry","tag":"both","text":"<p>Encodes physical address + memory attributes + permissions in AArch64 format.</p>","data":"<p>64-bit PTE in a table page.</p>","kind":"call","fn":3093,"name":"entry_set_ate","line":140,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_mode_aarch64.c","start":140,"focus":140,"lines":["static void entry_set_ate(u64 *entry, struct tagged_addr phy, unsigned long flags, int const level)","{","\tif (level == MIDGARD_MMU_BOTTOMLEVEL)","\t\tpage_table_entry_set(entry, as_phys_addr_t(phy) | get_mmu_flags(flags) |","\t\t\t\t\t\t    ENTRY_ACCESS_BIT | ENTRY_IS_ATE_L3);","\telse","\t\tpage_table_entry_set(entry, as_phys_addr_t(phy) | get_mmu_flags(flags) |","\t\t\t\t\t\t    ENTRY_ACCESS_BIT | ENTRY_IS_ATE_L02);","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu_mode_aarch64.c"},{"lane":"mmu","to":"hw","title":"Flush GPU caches/TLB","tag":"both","text":"<p>If the context has an AS, issue the MMU flush/invalidate commands; otherwise nothing needs doing until it is bound.</p>","data":"<p><code>AS_COMMAND</code> / <code>GPU_COMMAND</code> register writes.</p>","kind":"call","fn":3021,"name":"kbase_mmu_insert_pages","line":2951,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c","start":2948,"focus":2951,"lines":["\tif (err)","\t\treturn err;","","\tmmu_flush_invalidate_insert_pages(kbdev, mmut, vpfn, nr, dirty_pgds, mmu_sync_info, false);","","\treturn 0;","}","","KBASE_EXPORT_TEST_API(kbase_mmu_insert_pages);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mem","title":"CPU mapping","tag":"both","text":"<p>Sets up the CPU side of the mapping (page-fault handler <code>kbase_vm_ops</code>).</p>","data":"<p><code>struct kbase_cpu_mapping</code> in <code>alloc-&gt;mappings</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2667,"name":"kbase_context_mmap","line":2910,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c","start":2907,"focus":2910,"lines":["\t} /* default */","\t} /* switch */","","\terr = kbase_cpu_mmap(kctx, reg, vma, kaddr, nr_pages, aligned_offset, free_on_close);","#if defined(CONFIG_MALI_VECTOR_DUMP)","\tif (vma->vm_pgoff == PFN_DOWN(BASE_MEM_MMU_DUMP_HANDLE)) {","\t\t/* MMU dump - userspace should now have a reference on","\t\t * the pages, so we can now free the kernel mapping","\t\t */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c"}]},{"id":"submit_jm","title":"Submitting work and completion: Job Manager GPUs","summary":"<p><code>JOB_SUBMIT</code> → atoms → job scheduler → job-slot registers → IRQ → worker → event → <code>read()</code>.</p>","lanes":[["user","Userspace (UMD / app)"],["core","kbase Linux glue (core_linux)"],["jd","JM: JD + JS"],["be","JM backend / HW access"],["hw","GPU hardware"],["irq","IRQ handlers (top half)"],["wq","Workqueue / kthread (bottom half)"]],"tag":"JM","intro":"","dataflow":"<ul><li><strong>Userspace array of <code>base_jd_atom</code>:</strong> copied one at a time (<code>copy_from_user</code>).</li><li><strong>Atom table:</strong> each one becomes a kernel <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/213\"><code>struct kbase_jd_atom</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/jm/mali_kbase_jm_defs.h@505\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/jm/mali_kbase_jm_defs.h:505\">jm/mali_kbase_jm_defs.h:505</a>)</span> in <code>kctx-&gt;jctx.atoms[atom_number]</code>.</li><li><strong>Dependencies:</strong> atoms linked onto <code>dep_head</code> lists.</li><li><strong>Runnable atoms:</strong> sit in the JS per-slot per-priority trees.</li><li><strong>Picked atoms:</strong> enter the slot ringbuffer (max 2 per slot).</li><li><strong>Job slot registers:</strong> <code>jc</code> (GPU address of the job chain) is written to <code>JS_HEAD_NEXT</code>, the config to <code>JS_CONFIG_NEXT</code>, then <code>START</code> to <code>JS_COMMAND_NEXT</code>.</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong> <code>JOB_IRQ_STATUS</code> bits and the completion code are read from <code>JS_STATUS</code>.</li><li><strong>Event:</strong> <code>katom-&gt;event_code</code> is posted to <code>kctx-&gt;event_list</code>, and <code>read()</code> copies a <code>base_jd_event_v2</code> back to userspace.</li></ul>","notes":"","steps":[{"lane":"user","to":"core","title":"ioctl JOB_SUBMIT","tag":"both","text":"<p>Passes the user pointer, count and stride to JD.</p>","data":"<p><a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/454\"><code>struct kbase_ioctl_job_submit</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/jm/mali_kbase_jm_ioctl.h@195\" title=\"include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/jm/mali_kbase_jm_ioctl.h:195\">include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/jm/mali_kbase_jm_ioctl.h:195</a>)</span>: <code>addr</code>, <code>nr_atoms</code>, <code>stride</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1941,"name":"kbase_api_job_submit","line":839,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":839,"focus":839,"lines":["static int kbase_api_job_submit(struct kbase_context *kctx, struct kbase_ioctl_job_submit *submit)","{","\treturn kbase_jd_submit(kctx, u64_to_user_ptr(submit->addr), submit->nr_atoms,","\t\t\t       submit->stride, false);","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"jd","title":"Copy each atom from userspace","tag":"both","text":"<p>Supports older, smaller atom layouts via <code>stride</code>.</p>","data":"<p><code>struct base_jd_atom user_atom</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2296,"name":"kbase_jd_submit","line":1068,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c","start":1065,"focus":1068,"lines":["\t\t\t/* no seq_nr in v2 */","\t\t\tuser_atom.seq_nr = 0;","\t\t} else {","\t\t\tif (copy_from_user(&user_atom, user_addr, stride) != 0) {","\t\t\t\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev,","\t\t\t\t\t\"Invalid atom address %pK passed to job_submit\\n\",","\t\t\t\t\tuser_addr);","\t\t\t\terr = -EFAULT;","\t\t\t\tbreak;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c"},{"lane":"jd","to":"jd","title":"jd_submit_atom","tag":"both","text":"<p>Takes <code>jctx.lock</code> and initialises the kernel atom.</p>","data":"<p><code>katom = &amp;jctx-&gt;atoms[user_atom.atom_number]</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2296,"name":"kbase_jd_submit","line":1129,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c","start":1126,"focus":1129,"lines":["\t\t\tmutex_lock(&jctx->lock);","\t\t}","\t\tKBASE_TLSTREAM_TL_JD_SUBMIT_ATOM_START(kbdev, katom);","\t\tneed_to_try_schedule_context |= jd_submit_atom(kctx, &user_atom, katom);","\t\tKBASE_TLSTREAM_TL_JD_SUBMIT_ATOM_END(kbdev, katom);","\t\t/* Register a completed job as a disjoint event when the GPU is in a disjoint state","\t\t * (ie. being reset).","\t\t */","\t\tkbase_disjoint_event_potential(kbdev);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c"},{"lane":"jd","to":"jd","title":"Resolve dependencies","tag":"both","text":"<p>If a dependency is still pending, the atom waits on it. If the dependency already failed, the error propagates.</p>","data":"<p><code>katom-&gt;dep[i]</code>, dep lists.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2295,"name":"jd_submit_atom","line":844,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c","start":841,"focus":844,"lines":["","\t\t} else {","\t\t\t/* Atom is in progress, add this atom to the list */","\t\t\tlist_add_tail(&katom->dep_item[i], &dep_atom->dep_head[i]);","\t\t\tkbase_jd_katom_dep_set(&katom->dep[i], dep_atom, dep_atom_type);","\t\t\tqueued = 1;","\t\t}","\t}",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c"},{"lane":"jd","to":"jd","title":"Soft job or GPU job?","tag":"both","text":"<p>Soft jobs (<code>BASE_JD_REQ_SOFT_*</code>) run on the CPU right here. GPU jobs go to the scheduler.</p>","data":"<p><code>katom-&gt;core_req</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2295,"name":"jd_submit_atom","line":975,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c","start":972,"focus":975,"lines":["\t\treturn false;","","\tif (katom->core_req & BASE_JD_REQ_SOFT_JOB) {","\t\tif (kbase_process_soft_job(katom) == 0) {","\t\t\tkbase_finish_soft_job(katom);","\t\t\treturn kbase_jd_done_nolock(katom, true);","\t\t}","\t\treturn false;","\t}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c"},{"lane":"jd","to":"jd","title":"Hand to the job scheduler","tag":"both","text":"<p>The atom enters the context's per-slot priority tree. If the context wasn't runnable before, it is added to the device's pullable list.</p>","data":"<p><code>katom-&gt;status = KBASE_JD_ATOM_STATE_IN_JS</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2295,"name":"jd_submit_atom","line":988,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c","start":985,"focus":988,"lines":["\t\tkatom->status = KBASE_JD_ATOM_STATE_IN_JS;","\t\tdev_dbg(kctx->kbdev->dev, \"Atom %pK status to in JS\\n\", (void *)katom);","","\t\tneed_to_try_schedule_context = kbasep_js_add_job(kctx, katom);","\t\t/* If job was cancelled then resolve immediately */","\t\tif (katom->event_code != BASE_JD_EVENT_JOB_CANCELLED)","\t\t\treturn need_to_try_schedule_context;","","\t\t/* Synchronize with backend reset */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c"},{"lane":"jd","to":"jd","title":"Schedule: pick contexts per slot","tag":"both","text":"<p>For each slot, pop the highest-priority pullable context and make sure it has an AS (<code>kbasep_js_schedule_ctx</code> → <code>kbase_ctx_sched_retain_ctx</code>).</p>","data":"<p>Running context set; <code>kctx-&gt;as_nr</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2384,"name":"kbase_js_sched","line":2978,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c","start":2975,"focus":2978,"lines":["\t\t\tunsigned long flags;","\t\t\tbool context_idle = false;","","\t\t\tkctx = kbase_js_ctx_list_pop_head(kbdev, js);","","\t\t\tif (!kctx) {","\t\t\t\tjs_mask &= ~(1UL << js);","\t\t\t\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \"No kctx on pullable list (s:%u)\\n\", js);","\t\t\t\tbreak;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c"},{"lane":"jd","to":"be","title":"Kick the slot","tag":"both","text":"<p>Pull atoms from the chosen context into the slot ringbuffer.</p>","data":"<p>Slot mask.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2384,"name":"kbase_js_sched","line":3041,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c","start":3038,"focus":3041,"lines":["","\t\t\tkbase_ctx_flag_clear(kctx, KCTX_PULLED);","","\t\t\tif (!kbase_jm_kick(kbdev, 1UL << js)) {","\t\t\t\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \"No more jobs can be submitted (s:%u)\\n\", js);","\t\t\t\tjs_mask &= ~(1UL << js);","\t\t\t}","\t\t\tif (!kbase_ctx_flag(kctx, KCTX_PULLED)) {","\t\t\t\tbool pullable;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c"},{"lane":"be","to":"be","title":"Pull atoms into the ringbuffer","tag":"both","text":"<p>Up to <code>kbase_backend_slot_free()</code> atoms per slot (the hardware has a current and a NEXT register set).</p>","data":"<p><code>kbase_js_pull()</code> → ringbuffer entry.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2312,"name":"kbase_jm_kick","line":76,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jm.c","start":73,"focus":76,"lines":["\t\tunsigned int js = (unsigned int)ffs((int)js_mask) - 1U;","\t\tint nr_jobs_to_submit = kbase_backend_slot_free(kbdev, js);","","\t\tif (kbase_jm_next_job(kbdev, js, nr_jobs_to_submit))","\t\t\tret_mask |= (1U << js);","","\t\tjs_mask &= ~(1U << js);","\t}",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jm.c"},{"lane":"be","to":"be","title":"Per-atom ringbuffer state machine","tag":"both","text":"<p>Handles protected-mode transitions, waits for shader cores to be powered, then marks READY.</p>","data":"<p><code>katom-&gt;gpu_rb_state</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":208,"name":"kbase_backend_slot_update","line":956,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c","start":953,"focus":956,"lines":["","\t\t\t\t/* ***TRANSITION TO HIGHER STATE*** */","\t\t\t\tfallthrough;","\t\t\tcase KBASE_ATOM_GPU_RB_WAITING_FOR_CORE_AVAILABLE:","\t\t\t\tif (katom[idx]->will_fail_event_code) {","\t\t\t\t\tkbase_gpu_mark_atom_for_return(kbdev, katom[idx]);","\t\t\t\t\t/* Set EVENT_DONE so this atom will be","\t\t\t\t\t * completed, not unpulled.","\t\t\t\t\t */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c"},{"lane":"be","to":"hw","title":"Write job slot registers","tag":"both","text":"<p>Writes the job chain address to <code>JS_HEAD_NEXT</code>, then config (cache flush policy, thread priority).</p>","data":"<p><code>katom-&gt;jc</code> (GPU VA of the first job descriptor).</p>","kind":"call","fn":147,"name":"kbase_job_hw_submit","line":138,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c","start":135,"focus":138,"lines":["\tdev_dbg(kctx->kbdev->dev, \"Write JS_HEAD_NEXT 0x%llx for atom %pK\\n\", jc_head,","\t\t(void *)katom);","","\tkbase_reg_write64(kbdev, JOB_SLOT_OFFSET(js, HEAD_NEXT), jc_head);","","\taffinity = kbase_job_write_affinity(kbdev, katom->core_req, js, kctx->limited_core_mask);","","\t/* start MMU, medium priority, cache clean/flush on end, clean/flush on","\t * start"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c"},{"lane":"be","to":"hw","title":"START","tag":"both","text":"<p>The GPU's job manager now walks the job chain in the context's address space.</p>","data":"<p><code>JS_COMMAND_NEXT = JS_COMMAND_START</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":147,"name":"kbase_job_hw_submit","line":235,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c","start":232,"focus":235,"lines":["","\ttrace_sysgraph_gpu(SGR_SUBMIT, kctx->id, kbase_jd_atom_id(kctx, katom), js);","","\tkbase_reg_write32(kbdev, JOB_SLOT_OFFSET(js, COMMAND_NEXT), JS_COMMAND_START);","","\treturn 0;","}","","/**"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c"},{"lane":"hw","to":"irq","title":"Completion interrupt","tag":"both","text":"<p>The JOB IRQ handler reads <code>JOB_IRQ_STATUS</code> under <code>hwaccess_lock</code>.</p>","data":"<p><code>val</code> = done/failed bit per slot.</p>","kind":"call","fn":124,"name":"kbase_job_irq_handler","line":68,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c","start":65,"focus":68,"lines":["\t/* call the csf interrupt handler */","\tkbase_csf_interrupt(kbdev, val);","#else","\tkbase_job_done(kbdev, val);","#endif","","\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","","\treturn IRQ_HANDLED;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c"},{"lane":"irq","to":"be","title":"Process finished slots","tag":"both","text":"<p>For each finished slot, read status/tail, clear the IRQ, complete the head of the ringbuffer, and kick more work.</p>","data":"<p><code>completion_code</code> (e.g. <code>BASE_JD_EVENT_DONE</code> or a fault code).</p>","kind":"call","fn":150,"name":"kbase_job_done","line":447,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c","start":444,"focus":447,"lines":["","\t\t\twhile (nr_done) {","\t\t\t\tif (likely(nr_done == 1)) {","\t\t\t\t\tkbase_gpu_complete_hw(kbdev, i, completion_code, job_tail,","\t\t\t\t\t\t\t      &end_timestamp);","\t\t\t\t\tkbase_jm_try_kick_all(kbdev);","\t\t\t\t} else {","\t\t\t\t\t/* More than one job has completed.","\t\t\t\t\t * Since this is not the last job being"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c"},{"lane":"be","to":"jd","title":"Complete in JS","tag":"both","text":"<p>Updates JS accounting and calls into JD.</p>","data":"<p><code>katom-&gt;event_code</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2383,"name":"kbase_js_complete_atom","line":2919,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c","start":2916,"focus":2919,"lines":["\t\t\t   katom->slot_nr);","","\tKBASE_TLSTREAM_TL_JD_DONE_START(kbdev, katom);","\tkbase_jd_done(katom, katom->slot_nr, end_timestamp, 0);","\tKBASE_TLSTREAM_TL_JD_DONE_END(kbdev, katom);","","\t/* Unblock cross dependency if present */","\tif (x_dep &&","\t    (katom->event_code == BASE_JD_EVENT_DONE ||"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c"},{"lane":"jd","to":"wq","title":"Defer to the job-done worker","tag":"both","text":"<p>We are in IRQ context. The rest runs on the per-context <code>mali_jd/&lt;id&gt;</code> kthread worker.</p>","data":"<p><code>katom-&gt;work</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2299,"name":"kbase_jd_done","line":1440,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c","start":1437,"focus":1440,"lines":["#endif","","\tkthread_init_work(&katom->work, kbase_jd_done_worker);","\tkthread_queue_work(kctx->jctx.job_done_worker, &katom->work);","}","","KBASE_EXPORT_TEST_API(kbase_jd_done);","","void kbase_jd_cancel(struct kbase_device *kbdev, struct kbase_jd_atom *katom)"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"jd","title":"Job-done worker","tag":"both","text":"<p>Removes the atom from JS, may release the context's AS, then completes in JD.</p>","data":"<p>Retained JS state.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2297,"name":"kbase_jd_done_worker","line":1235,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c","start":1232,"focus":1235,"lines":["\tmutex_unlock(&js_kctx_info->ctx.jsctx_mutex);","\tmutex_unlock(&js_devdata->queue_mutex);","\t/* kbase_jd_done_nolock() requires the jsctx_mutex lock to be dropped */","\tkbase_jd_done_nolock(katom, false);","","\t/* katom may have been freed now, do not use! */","","\tif (context_idle) {","\t\tunsigned long flags;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c"},{"lane":"jd","to":"jd","title":"Wake dependants, post event","tag":"both","text":"<p>Atoms that depended on this one become runnable. The completed atom is reported.</p>","data":"<p><code>katom-&gt;status = COMPLETED</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2292,"name":"kbase_jd_done_nolock","line":621,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c","start":618,"focus":621,"lines":["\t\t */","\t\tkbase_disjoint_event_potential(kctx->kbdev);","\t\tif (post_immediately && list_empty(&kctx->completed_jobs))","\t\t\tkbase_event_post(kctx, katom);","\t\telse","\t\t\tlist_add_tail(&katom->jd_item, &kctx->completed_jobs);","","\t\t/* Decrement and check the TOTAL number of jobs. This includes","\t\t * those not tracked by the scheduler: 'not ready to run' and"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c"},{"lane":"jd","to":"core","title":"Queue event & wake readers","tag":"both","text":"<p>Appends to <code>kctx-&gt;event_list</code> and wakes <code>poll()</code>/<code>read()</code> waiters.</p>","data":"<p><code>kctx-&gt;event_count</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2222,"name":"kbase_event_post","line":206,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_event.c","start":203,"focus":206,"lines":["\t\tmutex_unlock(&kctx->event_mutex);","\t\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \"Reporting %d events\\n\", event_count);","","\t\tkbase_event_wakeup(kctx);","","\t\t/* Post-completion latency */","\t\ttrace_sysgraph(SGR_POST, kctx->id, kbase_jd_atom_id(kctx, atom));","\t}","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_event.c"},{"lane":"user","to":"core","title":"read() completed events","tag":"both","text":"<p>Userspace gets one <code>base_jd_event_v2</code> per atom.</p>","data":"<p><code>uevent.event_code</code>, <code>uevent.atom_number</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1997,"name":"kbase_read","line":2184,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":2181,"focus":2184,"lines":["\tmemset(&uevent, 0, sizeof(uevent));","","\tdo {","\t\twhile (kbase_event_dequeue(kctx, &uevent)) {","\t\t\tif (out_count > 0)","\t\t\t\tgoto out;","","\t\t\tif (filp->f_flags & O_NONBLOCK)","\t\t\t\treturn -EAGAIN;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"}]},{"id":"submit_csf","title":"Submitting work and completion: CSF GPUs","summary":"<p>Register queue → create group → bind (mmap I/O pages) → write ring buffer → kick → scheduler places group on a CSG slot → firmware runs it → SYNC_UPDATE IRQ → wake poll().</p>","lanes":[["user","Userspace (UMD / app)"],["core","kbase Linux glue (core_linux)"],["csf","CSF queues + scheduler"],["fw","MCU firmware"],["hw","GPU hardware"],["irq","IRQ handlers (top half)"]],"tag":"CSF","intro":"","dataflow":"<ul><li><strong>Userspace memory region (ring buffer):</strong> described by <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/422\"><code>struct kbase_ioctl_cs_queue_register</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_ioctl.h@151\" title=\"include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_ioctl.h:151\">include/uapi/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_ioctl.h:151</a>)</span>, it becomes a <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/61\"><code>struct kbase_queue</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h@414\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:414\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:414</a>)</span> (<code>base_addr</code>, <code>size</code>).</li><li><strong>Queue group:</strong> a <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/64\"><code>struct kbase_queue_group</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h@575\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:575\">csf/mali_kbase_csf_defs.h:575</a>)</span> with priority and core masks, created by <code>CS_QUEUE_GROUP_CREATE</code>.</li><li><strong>Bind:</strong> two <strong>user I/O pages</strong> per queue. The input page holds <code>CS_INSERT</code>; the output page holds <code>CS_EXTRACT</code> / <code>CS_ACTIVE</code>. They are mapped into both the process and the MCU.</li><li><strong>Doorbell page:</strong> writing to it wakes the firmware. It is mapped into the process once the group is on a slot.</li><li><strong>Scheduler → firmware:</strong> CSG input page (<code>CSG_EP_REQ</code>, <code>CSG_SUSPEND_BUF</code>, <code>CSG_CONFIG = as_nr</code>, <code>CSG_REQ = START</code>) and CS input page (<code>CS_BASE</code>, <code>CS_SIZE</code>, <code>CS_USER_INPUT/OUTPUT</code>, <code>CS_REQ = START</code>).</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong> the GPU writes sync objects in memory; the firmware sets <code>CSG_ACK.SYNC_UPDATE</code>. The IRQ path then wakes <code>kctx-&gt;event_queue</code>.</li></ul>","notes":"","steps":[{"lane":"user","to":"core","title":"ioctl CS_QUEUE_REGISTER","tag":"both","text":"<p>Registers a ring buffer that userspace already allocated with MEM_ALLOC.</p>","data":"<p><code>buffer_gpu_addr</code>, <code>buffer_size</code>, <code>priority</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":544,"name":"kbase_csf_queue_register","line":573,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c","start":573,"focus":573,"lines":["int kbase_csf_queue_register(struct kbase_context *kctx, struct kbase_ioctl_cs_queue_register *reg)","{","\t/* Validate the ring buffer configuration parameters */","\tif (reg->buffer_size < CS_RING_BUFFER_MIN_SIZE ||","\t    reg->buffer_size > CS_RING_BUFFER_MAX_SIZE ||","\t    reg->buffer_size & (reg->buffer_size - 1) || !reg->buffer_gpu_addr ||","\t    reg->buffer_gpu_addr & ~PAGE_MASK)","\t\treturn -EINVAL;","","\treturn csf_queue_register_internal(kctx, reg, NULL);","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c"},{"lane":"user","to":"core","title":"ioctl CS_QUEUE_GROUP_CREATE","tag":"both","text":"<p>Creates a group with core masks and a priority; it is not on any slot yet.</p>","data":"<p>Group handle returned to userspace.</p>","kind":"call","fn":568,"name":"kbase_csf_queue_group_create","line":1349,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c","start":1346,"focus":1349,"lines":["\t\t * (note: for CSF v1.0 all CSs in a CSG will have access to","\t\t * the same iterators)","\t\t */","\t\tconst int group_handle = create_queue_group(kctx, create);","","\t\tif (group_handle >= 0)","\t\t\tcreate->out.group_handle = group_handle;","\t\telse","\t\t\terr = group_handle;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c"},{"lane":"user","to":"csf","title":"ioctl CS_QUEUE_BIND","tag":"both","text":"<p>Binds a queue to a group and CS index. Allocates the user I/O pages and returns an mmap handle.</p>","data":"<p><code>bind.out.mmap_handle</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":548,"name":"kbase_csf_queue_bind","line":698,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c","start":698,"focus":698,"lines":["int kbase_csf_queue_bind(struct kbase_context *kctx, union kbase_ioctl_cs_queue_bind *bind)","{","\tstruct kbase_queue *queue;","\tstruct kbase_queue_group *group;","\tu8 max_streams;","\tint ret = -EINVAL;","","\tmutex_lock(&kctx->csf.lock);","","\tgroup = find_queue_group(kctx, bind->in.group_handle);","\tqueue = find_queue(kctx, bind->in.buffer_gpu_addr);",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c"},{"lane":"csf","to":"csf","title":"Allocate user I/O pages","tag":"both","text":"<p>Two pages per queue, mapped for the MCU too (in the MCU shared zone).</p>","data":"<p><code>queue-&gt;phys[2]</code>, <code>queue-&gt;user_io_gpu_va</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":536,"name":"kbase_csf_alloc_command_stream_user_pages","line":280,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c","start":280,"focus":280,"lines":["int kbase_csf_alloc_command_stream_user_pages(struct kbase_context *kctx, struct kbase_queue *queue)","{","\tstruct kbase_device *kbdev = kctx->kbdev;","\tint ret;","","\tlockdep_assert_held(&kctx->csf.lock);","","\tret = kbase_mem_pool_alloc_pages(&kctx->mem_pools.small[KBASE_MEM_GROUP_CSF_IO],","\t\t\t\t\t KBASEP_NUM_CS_USER_IO_PAGES, queue->phys, false,","\t\t\t\t\t kctx->task);","\tif (ret != KBASEP_NUM_CS_USER_IO_PAGES) {","\t\t/* Marking both the phys to zero for indicating there is no phys allocated */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c"},{"lane":"user","to":"core","title":"mmap the I/O pages","tag":"both","text":"<p>The process can now write <code>CS_INSERT</code> and read <code>CS_EXTRACT</code> directly.</p>","data":"<p>CPU mapping of the two pages.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2667,"name":"kbase_context_mmap","line":2840,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c","start":2837,"focus":2840,"lines":["\tcase PFN_DOWN(BASEP_MEM_CSF_USER_IO_PAGES_HANDLE)... PFN_DOWN(BASE_MEM_COOKIE_BASE) - 1: {","\t\tkbase_gpu_vm_unlock_with_pmode_sync(kctx);","\t\tmutex_lock(&kctx->csf.lock);","\t\terr = kbase_csf_cpu_mmap_user_io_pages(kctx, vma);","\t\tmutex_unlock(&kctx->csf.lock);","\t\tgoto out;","\t}","#endif","\tcase PFN_DOWN(BASE_MEM_COOKIE_BASE)... PFN_DOWN(BASE_MEM_FIRST_FREE_ADDRESS) - 1: {"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem_linux.c"},{"lane":"user","to":"core","title":"ioctl CS_QUEUE_KICK","tag":"both","text":"<p>After writing commands, userspace kicks the queue. The kernel only queues it and wakes the scheduler thread.</p>","data":"<p><code>queue-&gt;pending_kick_link</code> on <code>pending_gpuq_kick_queues[prio]</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":555,"name":"kbase_csf_queue_kick","line":926,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c","start":923,"focus":926,"lines":["\t\t\t\t * kick has been handled.","\t\t\t\t */","\t\t\t\tatomic_inc(&queue->pending_kick);","\t\t\t\tlist_add_tail(","\t\t\t\t\t&queue->pending_kick_link,","\t\t\t\t\t&kbdev->csf.pending_gpuq_kick_queues[queue->group_priority]);","\t\t\t\tif (atomic_cmpxchg(&kbdev->csf.pending_gpuq_kicks, false, true) ==","\t\t\t\t    false)","\t\t\t\t\tcomplete(&kbdev->csf.scheduler.kthread_signal);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c"},{"lane":"csf","to":"csf","title":"Wake scheduler kthread","tag":"both","text":"<p><code>mali-gpuq-kthread</code> handles kicks, sync updates, protected-mode requests, KCPU work, ticks and tocks.</p>","data":"<p>Completion signal.</p>","kind":"call","fn":555,"name":"kbase_csf_queue_kick","line":931,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c","start":928,"focus":931,"lines":["\t\t\t\t\t&kbdev->csf.pending_gpuq_kick_queues[queue->group_priority]);","\t\t\t\tif (atomic_cmpxchg(&kbdev->csf.pending_gpuq_kicks, false, true) ==","\t\t\t\t    false)","\t\t\t\t\tcomplete(&kbdev->csf.scheduler.kthread_signal);","\t\t\t}","\t\t\tspin_unlock(&kbdev->csf.pending_gpuq_kick_queues_lock);","\t\t}","\t} else {","\t\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev,"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c"},{"lane":"csf","to":"csf","title":"Scheduler loop","tag":"both","text":"<p>Each iteration processes pending requests in a fixed order, then tick/tock.</p>","data":"<p><code>scheduler-&gt;kthread_signal</code> (a completion), atomic flags <code>pending_tick_work</code> / <code>pending_tock_work</code>, and the per-priority kick lists.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1214,"name":"kbase_csf_scheduler_kthread","line":6711,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c","start":6708,"focus":6711,"lines":["\t\thandle_pending_sync_update_works(scheduler);","\t\thandle_pending_protm_requests(scheduler);","\t\thandle_pending_kcpuq_commands(scheduler);","\t\thandle_pending_queue_kicks(kbdev);","","\t\t/* Check if we need to perform a scheduling tick/tock. A tick","\t\t * event shall override a tock event but not vice-versa.","\t\t */","\t\tif (atomic_cmpxchg(&scheduler->pending_tick_work, true, false) == true) {"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c"},{"lane":"csf","to":"csf","title":"Process the kick","tag":"both","text":"<p>Blocks GPU reset while it runs (<code>kbase_reset_gpu_prevent_and_wait</code>).</p>","data":"<p>One <code>struct kbase_queue *</code> popped from <code>kbdev-&gt;csf.pending_gpuq_kick_queues[]</code>; <code>queue-&gt;pending_kick</code> is decremented when handled.</p>","kind":"call","fn":615,"name":"kbase_csf_process_queue_kick","line":3372,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c","start":3369,"focus":3372,"lines":["\tif (queue->bind_state != KBASE_CSF_QUEUE_BOUND)","\t\tgoto out_allow_gpu_reset;","","\terr = kbase_csf_scheduler_queue_start(queue);","\tif (unlikely(err)) {","\t\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \"Failed to start queue\");","\t\tif (err == -EBUSY) {","\t\t\tretry_kick = true;",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c"},{"lane":"csf","to":"csf","title":"Start queue","tag":"both","text":"<p>Makes the group runnable. If its group is already on a slot, ring the queue's doorbell directly; otherwise schedule a tick.</p>","data":"<p>Group → runnable list.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1114,"name":"kbase_csf_scheduler_queue_start","line":1881,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c","start":1878,"focus":1881,"lines":["\t\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \"blocked queue(csi_index=%d) of group %d was kicked\",","\t\t\tqueue->csi_index, group->handle);","\t} else {","\t\terr = scheduler_group_schedule(group);","","\t\tif (!err) {","\t\t\tqueue->enabled = true;","\t\t\tif (kbasep_csf_scheduler_group_is_on_slot_locked(group)) {","\t\t\t\tif (cs_enabled) {"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c"},{"lane":"csf","to":"csf","title":"Tick: decide slot assignment","tag":"both","text":"<p>Updates idle slots, rotates for fairness, chooses up to N groups by priority, then applies.</p>","data":"<p><code>scheduler-&gt;csg_slots[]</code> plan.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1188,"name":"schedule_actions","line":5389,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c","start":5386,"focus":5389,"lines":["\t\tscheduler_rotate(kbdev);","","redo_local_tock:","\tscheduler_prepare(kbdev);","\t/* Need to specifically enqueue the GPU idle work if there are no groups","\t * to schedule despite the runnable groups. This scenario will happen","\t * if System suspend is done when all groups are idle and and no work","\t * is submitted for the groups after the System resume.","\t */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c"},{"lane":"csf","to":"fw","title":"Program the CSG slot","tag":"both","text":"<p>Gets an AS for the context (<code>kbase_ctx_sched_retain_ctx</code>), programs each bound CS, writes core masks, endpoint config, AS number and suspend buffers.</p>","data":"<p>CSG input page.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1141,"name":"program_csg_slot","line":2955,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c","start":2952,"focus":2955,"lines":["\tkbase_csf_firmware_csg_input(ginfo, CSG_EP_REQ_LO, ep_cfg & U32_MAX);","","\t/* Program the address space number assigned to the context */","\tkbase_csf_firmware_csg_input(ginfo, CSG_CONFIG, (u32)kctx->as_nr);","","\tkbase_csf_firmware_csg_input(ginfo, CSG_SUSPEND_BUF_LO, normal_suspend_buf & U32_MAX);","\tkbase_csf_firmware_csg_input(ginfo, CSG_SUSPEND_BUF_HI, normal_suspend_buf >> 32);","","\t/* Note, we program the P-mode buffer pointer here, but actual runtime"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c"},{"lane":"csf","to":"fw","title":"Program each CS","tag":"both","text":"<p>Tells the firmware where the ring buffer and user I/O pages are.</p>","data":"<p><code>CS_BASE</code>, <code>CS_SIZE</code>, <code>CS_USER_INPUT/OUTPUT</code>, <code>CS_CONFIG</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1112,"name":"program_cs","line":1774,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c","start":1771,"focus":1774,"lines":["","\tstream = &ginfo->streams[csi_index];","","\tkbase_csf_firmware_cs_input(stream, CS_BASE_LO, queue->base_addr & 0xFFFFFFFF);","\tkbase_csf_firmware_cs_input(stream, CS_BASE_HI, queue->base_addr >> 32);","\tkbase_csf_firmware_cs_input(stream, CS_SIZE, queue->size);","","\tuser_input = queue->user_io_gpu_va;","\tWARN_ONCE(!user_input && queue->enabled, \"Enabled queue should have a valid gpu_va\");"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c"},{"lane":"csf","to":"fw","title":"START + doorbell","tag":"both","text":"<p>Toggles <code>CSG_REQ.STATE = START</code> (or RESUME) and rings the CSG doorbell. The firmware acknowledges via <code>CSG_ACK</code>.</p>","data":"<p>REQ/ACK toggle.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1141,"name":"program_csg_slot","line":2992,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c","start":2989,"focus":2992,"lines":["\t}","","\tkbase_csf_firmware_csg_input_mask(ginfo, CSG_REQ, state, CSG_REQ_STATE_MASK);","\tkbase_csf_ring_csg_doorbell(kbdev, slot);","\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->csf.scheduler.interrupt_lock, flags);","","\t/* Update status before rings the door-bell, marking ready => run */","\tatomic_set(&csg_slot->state, CSG_SLOT_READY2RUN);","\tcsg_slot->trigger_jiffies = jiffies;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_scheduler.c"},{"lane":"fw","to":"hw","title":"Firmware executes the command stream","tag":"both","text":"<p>The firmware binary is not part of this archive, so its internals are out of scope. It fetches commands from the ring buffer and drives the GPU's iterators (compute, fragment, tiler).</p>","data":"<p>Ring-buffer contents written by userspace.</p>","kind":"call","line":331,"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c","name":"mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c","ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_firmware.c","start":329,"focus":331,"lines":["}","","static void boot_csf_firmware(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{","\tenable_mcu(kbdev);","","\twait_for_firmware_boot(kbdev);","}",""]}},{"lane":"hw","to":"irq","title":"Firmware interrupt (JOB line)","tag":"both","text":"<p>On CSF the JOB IRQ carries firmware interrupts: one bit per CSG plus <code>JOB_IRQ_GLOBAL_IF</code>.</p>","data":"<p><code>val</code> = CSG bitmask.</p>","kind":"call","fn":124,"name":"kbase_job_irq_handler","line":66,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c","start":63,"focus":66,"lines":["","#if MALI_USE_CSF","\t/* call the csf interrupt handler */","\tkbase_csf_interrupt(kbdev, val);","#else","\tkbase_job_done(kbdev, val);","#endif","","\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c"},{"lane":"irq","to":"csf","title":"Process CSG interrupts","tag":"both","text":"<p>For each signalled CSG compare <code>CSG_REQ</code> and <code>CSG_ACK</code> to see which events fired.</p>","data":"<p><code>csg_req ^ csg_ack</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":606,"name":"kbase_csf_interrupt","line":3103,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c","start":3100,"focus":3103,"lines":["\t\t\twhile (csg_interrupts != 0) {","\t\t\t\tu32 const csg_nr = (u32)ffs((int)csg_interrupts) - 1;","","\t\t\t\tprocess_csg_interrupts(kbdev, csg_nr, &track,","\t\t\t\t\t\t       progress_timeout_csgs);","\t\t\t\tcsg_interrupts &= ~(1U << csg_nr);","\t\t\t}","","\t\t\t/* Handle protm from the tracked information */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c"},{"lane":"irq","to":"csf","title":"SYNC_UPDATE","tag":"both","text":"<p>A sync object was updated: acknowledge it and wake CPU-side waiters (and KCPU queues).</p>","data":"<p><code>CSG_REQ.SYNC_UPDATE</code> acked.</p>","kind":"call","fn":607,"name":"kbase_csf_handle_csg_sync_update","line":3218,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c","start":3215,"focus":3218,"lines":["\t\t/* SYNC_UPDATE events shall invalidate GPU idle event */","\t\tatomic_set(&kbdev->csf.scheduler.gpu_no_longer_idle, true);","","\t\tkbase_csf_event_signal_cpu_only(group->kctx);","\t}","}","","void kbase_csf_doorbell_mapping_term(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c"},{"lane":"csf","to":"user","title":"Wake userspace","tag":"both","text":"<p><code>poll()</code> on the fd returns. Userspace checks its sync objects in memory to see what completed.</p>","data":"<p><code>kctx-&gt;event_count</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":662,"name":"kbase_csf_event_signal","line":120,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_event.c","start":117,"focus":120,"lines":["\t/* First increment the signal count and wake up event thread.","\t */","\tatomic_set(&kctx->event_count, 1);","\tkbase_event_wakeup(kctx);","","\t/* Signal the CSF firmware. This is to ensure that pending command","\t * stream synch object wait operations are re-evaluated.","\t * Write to GLB_DOORBELL would suffice as spec says that all pending","\t * synch object wait operations are re-evaluated on a write to any"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_event.c"}]},{"id":"irq","title":"GPU interrupt handling (top half → bottom half)","summary":"<p>Three GPU interrupt sources, minimal work under a spinlock, heavy work deferred.</p>","lanes":[["hw","GPU hardware"],["irq","IRQ handlers (top half)"],["be","JM backend / HW access"],["mmu","GPU MMU"],["pm","Power mgmt"],["wq","Workqueue / kthread (bottom half)"]],"tag":"both","intro":"","dataflow":"<ul><li><strong>Interrupt status registers:</strong> <code>JOB_IRQ_STATUS</code>, <code>MMU_IRQ_STATUS</code> and <code>GPU_IRQ_STATUS</code>, read into a <code>u32 val</code>.</li><li><strong>Per-source dispatch:</strong><ul><li>Each JOB bit means a job slot (JM) or a CSG (CSF).</li><li>Each MMU bit means a page fault or bus fault on an AS number.</li><li>GPU bits mean power transitions, cache clean done, reset completed or a fault.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Fault details:</strong> <code>AS_FAULTSTATUS</code> / <code>FAULTADDRESS</code> go into <code>kbdev-&gt;as[n].pf_data</code> (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/250\"><code>struct kbase_fault</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@271\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:271\">mali_kbase_defs.h:271</a>)</span>) and are handed to a workqueue.</li></ul>","notes":"","steps":[{"lane":"hw","to":"irq","title":"Handlers installed at probe","tag":"both","text":"<p><code>request_irq</code> for each line (or one combined line), with the device pointer tagged by IRQ type.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;irqs[i].irq</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":136,"name":"kbase_install_interrupts","line":448,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c","start":448,"focus":448,"lines":["int kbase_install_interrupts(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{","\tu32 i;","","\tfor (i = 0; i < kbdev->nr_irqs; i++) {","\t\tconst int result = request_irq(kbdev->irqs[i].irq,","\t\t\t\t\t       kbase_get_interrupt_handler(kbdev, i),","\t\t\t\t\t       kbdev->irqs[i].flags | IRQF_SHARED,","\t\t\t\t\t       dev_name(kbdev->dev), kbase_tag(kbdev, i));","\t\tif (result) {","\t\t\tdev_err(kbdev->dev, \"Can't request interrupt %u (index %u)\\n\",","\t\t\t\tkbdev->irqs[i].irq, i);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c"},{"lane":"irq","to":"irq","title":"Choose handler table","tag":"both","text":"<p>With one IRQ line, <code>kbase_combined_irq_handler</code> calls all three handlers in turn.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;nr_irqs</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":129,"name":"kbase_get_interrupt_handler","line":180,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c","start":180,"focus":180,"lines":["irq_handler_t kbase_get_interrupt_handler(struct kbase_device *kbdev, u32 irq_tag)","{","\tif (kbdev->nr_irqs == 1)","\t\treturn kbase_combined_irq_handler;","\telse if (irq_tag < ARRAY_SIZE(kbase_handler_table))","\t\treturn kbase_handler_table[irq_tag];","\telse","\t\treturn NULL;","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c"},{"lane":"irq","to":"irq","title":"JOB IRQ: guard on power","tag":"both","text":"<p>Under <code>hwaccess_lock</code>: if the GPU is off, the IRQ isn't ours (lines can be shared).</p>","data":"<p><code>gpu_powered</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":124,"name":"kbase_job_irq_handler","line":49,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c","start":46,"focus":49,"lines":["","\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","","\tif (!kbdev->pm.backend.gpu_powered) {","\t\t/* GPU is turned off - IRQ is not for us */","\t\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\t\treturn IRQ_NONE;","\t}",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c"},{"lane":"irq","to":"be","title":"JOB IRQ dispatch","tag":"both","text":"<p>JM → <code>kbase_job_done</code>; CSF → <code>kbase_csf_interrupt</code>.</p>","data":"<p><code>JOB_IRQ_STATUS</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":124,"name":"kbase_job_irq_handler","line":55,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c","start":52,"focus":55,"lines":["\t\treturn IRQ_NONE;","\t}","","\tval = kbase_reg_read32(kbdev, JOB_CONTROL_ENUM(JOB_IRQ_STATUS));","","\tif (!val) {","\t\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\t\treturn IRQ_NONE;","\t}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c"},{"lane":"irq","to":"mmu","title":"MMU IRQ","tag":"both","text":"<p>Reads <code>MMU_IRQ_STATUS</code> and hands it to the backend MMU interrupt function.</p>","data":"<p><code>val</code> (page-fault bits low, bus-fault bits shifted).</p>","kind":"call","fn":125,"name":"kbase_mmu_irq_handler","line":103,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c","start":100,"focus":103,"lines":["","\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \"%s: irq %d irqstatus 0x%x\\n\", __func__, irq, val);","","\tkbase_mmu_interrupt(kbdev, val);","","\tatomic_dec(&kbdev->faults_pending);","","\treturn IRQ_HANDLED;","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c"},{"lane":"mmu","to":"mmu","title":"Mask MMU IRQs, read fault","tag":"both","text":"<p>Masks MMU interrupts and, per faulting AS, records the fault address, status and protected-mode flag.</p>","data":"<p><code>fault-&gt;addr</code>, <code>fault-&gt;status</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2967,"name":"kbase_mmu_interrupt","line":355,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c","start":352,"focus":355,"lines":["\t\tkctx = kbase_ctx_sched_as_to_ctx_refcount(kbdev, as_no);","","\t\t/* find faulting address */","\t\tfault->addr = kbase_reg_read64(kbdev, MMU_AS_OFFSET(as_no, FAULTADDRESS));","\t\t/* Mark the fault protected or not */","\t\tfault->protected_mode = kbdev->protected_mode;","","\t\tif (kbdev->protected_mode && fault->addr) {","\t\t\t/* check if address reporting is allowed */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c"},{"lane":"mmu","to":"wq","title":"Queue page-fault work","tag":"both","text":"<p>Page faults may need to allocate memory (which can sleep), so they are handled in <code>kbase_mmu_page_fault_worker</code>.</p>","data":"<p><code>as-&gt;work_pagefault</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2965,"name":"kbase_mmu_interrupt_process","line":273,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c","start":270,"focus":273,"lines":["\t\tWARN_ON(!queue_work(as->pf_wq, &as->work_busfault));","\t\tatomic_inc(&kbdev->faults_pending);","\t} else {","\t\tWARN_ON(!queue_work(as->pf_wq, &as->work_pagefault));","\t\tatomic_inc(&kbdev->faults_pending);","\t}","","\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \"Leaving %s kctx %pK, as %pK\\n\", __func__, (void *)kctx, (void *)as);","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c"},{"lane":"irq","to":"pm","title":"GPU IRQ","tag":"both","text":"<p>Reads <code>GPU_IRQ_STATUS</code>.</p>","data":"<p><code>gpu_irq_status</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":126,"name":"kbase_gpuonly_irq_handler","line":132,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c","start":129,"focus":132,"lines":["","\tif (gpu_irq_status) {","\t\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \"%s: irq %d irqstatus 0x%x\\n\", __func__, irq, gpu_irq_status);","\t\tkbase_gpu_interrupt(kbdev, gpu_irq_status);","","\t\tirq_state = IRQ_HANDLED;","\t}","","\treturn irq_state;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"pm","title":"GPU IRQ: power and cache events","tag":"both","text":"<p>Power-transition-complete drives the PM state machines (<code>kbase_pm_power_changed</code>); cache-clean-complete wakes cache flush waiters; GPU faults are reported.</p>","data":"<p><code>POWER_CHANGED_ALL</code>, <code>CLEAN_CACHES_COMPLETED</code>, <code>GPU_FAULT</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1437,"name":"kbase_gpu_interrupt","line":96,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_hw_jm.c","start":93,"focus":96,"lines":["\tif (val & CLEAN_CACHES_COMPLETED)","\t\tkbase_clean_caches_done(kbdev);","","\tif (val & POWER_CHANGED_ALL) {","\t\tkbase_pm_power_changed(kbdev);","\t} else if (val & CLEAN_CACHES_COMPLETED) {","\t\t/* If cache line evict messages can be lost when shader cores","\t\t * power down then we need to flush the L2 cache before powering","\t\t * down cores. When the flush completes, the shaders' state"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/backend/mali_kbase_device_hw_jm.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"pm","title":"Advance PM state machines","tag":"both","text":"<p>Re-runs <code>kbase_pm_update_state</code> now that the hardware reports the transition finished.</p>","data":"<p>L2/shader/MCU states.</p>","kind":"call","fn":298,"name":"kbase_pm_power_changed","line":850,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c","start":850,"focus":850,"lines":["void kbase_pm_power_changed(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{","\tunsigned long flags;","","\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\tkbase_pm_update_state(kbdev);","","#if !MALI_USE_CSF","\tkbase_backend_slot_update(kbdev);","#endif /* !MALI_USE_CSF */","","\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c"}]},{"id":"power","title":"Power up / power down (runtime)","summary":"<p>A reference count drives the policy; the policy drives the L2/shader/MCU state machines; platform callbacks switch clocks.</p>","lanes":[["core","kbase Linux glue (core_linux)"],["pm","Power mgmt"],["plat","Platform (clocks/regulators)"],["hw","GPU hardware"]],"tag":"both","intro":"","dataflow":"<ul><li><strong><code>pm.active_count</code>:</strong> the number of users that need the GPU powered.</li><li><strong>Policy decision:</strong> <code>get_core_active()</code> returns a bool. It sets <code>backend-&gt;gpu_powered</code> and the desired L2, shader and MCU states.</li><li><strong>Power registers:</strong> core bitmasks are written to <code>L2_PWRON</code>, <code>SHADER_PWRON</code> (and <code>*_PWROFF</code>). The hardware raises <code>POWER_CHANGED</code> when done.</li><li><strong>Platform callbacks:</strong> <code>power_on_callback</code> / <code>power_off_callback</code> (clocks, regulators, runtime PM).</li></ul>","notes":"","steps":[{"lane":"core","to":"pm","title":"Someone needs the GPU","tag":"both","text":"<p>For example the job scheduler, the CSF scheduler or firmware loading. This is a thin wrapper.</p>","data":"<p>Only <code>kbdev</code>. The caller now owns one PM reference, which it must drop with <code>kbase_pm_context_idle()</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2806,"name":"kbase_pm_context_active","line":50,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c","start":50,"focus":50,"lines":["void kbase_pm_context_active(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{","\t(void)kbase_pm_context_active_handle_suspend(kbdev, KBASE_PM_SUSPEND_HANDLER_NOT_POSSIBLE);","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"pm","title":"Refcount 0 → 1","tag":"both","text":"<p>Only the first reference does real work. While a system suspend is in progress, callers may be refused.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;pm.active_count</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2807,"name":"kbase_pm_context_active_handle_suspend_locked","line":86,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c","start":83,"focus":86,"lines":["\t\t\tbreak;","\t\t}","\t}","\tc = ++kbdev->pm.active_count;","\tKBASE_KTRACE_ADD(kbdev, PM_CONTEXT_ACTIVE, NULL, (u64)c);","","\tif (c == 1) {","\t\t/* First context active: Power on the GPU and","\t\t * any cores requested by the policy"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"pm","title":"Ask the policy","tag":"both","text":"<p><code>coarse_demand</code> says active whenever <code>active_count &gt; 0</code>; <code>always_on</code> always says active.</p>","data":"<p><code>active</code> bool.</p>","kind":"call","fn":439,"name":"kbase_pm_update_active","line":115,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_policy.c","start":112,"focus":115,"lines":["","\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","","\tactive = backend->pm_current_policy->get_core_active(kbdev);","\tWARN((kbase_pm_is_active(kbdev) && !active),","\t     \"GPU is active but policy '%s' is indicating that it can be powered off\",","\t     kbdev->pm.backend.pm_current_policy->name);","","\tif (active) {"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_policy.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"plat","title":"Power on","tag":"both","text":"<p>Clock on, then update the state machines.</p>","data":"<p><code>is_resume</code> flag. Clock-on sets <code>backend-&gt;gpu_powered</code>; <code>kbase_pm_update_cores_state()</code> recomputes the desired core masks.</p>","kind":"call","fn":282,"name":"kbase_pm_do_poweron","line":241,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c","start":238,"focus":241,"lines":["\t/* Turn clocks and interrupts on - no-op if we haven't done a previous","\t * kbase_pm_clock_off()","\t */","\tkbase_pm_clock_on(kbdev, is_resume);","","\tif (!is_resume) {","\t\tunsigned long flags;","","\t\t/* Force update of L2 state - if we have abandoned a power off"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"plat","title":"Platform power callback","tag":"both","text":"<p>The SoC turns on clocks and regulators. If the GPU lost state (returned non-zero), the driver re-initialises the hardware.</p>","data":"<p><code>backend-&gt;gpu_powered = true</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":390,"name":"kbase_pm_clock_on","line":2868,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c","start":2865,"focus":2868,"lines":["\t\tbackend->callback_power_resume(kbdev);","\t\treturn;","\t} else if (backend->callback_power_on) {","\t\tret = backend->callback_power_on(kbdev);","\t}","","\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\tbackend->gpu_powered = true;","\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"hw","title":"Run the state machines","tag":"both","text":"<p>L2 first, then shader cores; on CSF also the MCU. Each machine issues PWRON/PWROFF and returns when it must wait for hardware.</p>","data":"<p><code>backend-&gt;l2_state</code>, <code>shaders_state</code>, <code>mcu_state</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":369,"name":"kbase_pm_update_state","line":2281,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c","start":2278,"focus":2281,"lines":["\tif (!kbdev->pm.backend.gpu_ready)","\t\treturn; /* Do nothing if the GPU is not ready */","","\tif (kbase_pm_l2_update_state(kbdev))","\t\treturn;","","#if !MALI_USE_CSF","\tif (kbase_pm_shaders_update_state(kbdev))","\t\treturn;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"hw","title":"Write PWRON/PWROFF registers","tag":"both","text":"<p>Writes the core bitmask to the right <code><em>_PWRON_</em></code>/<code><em>_PWROFF_</em></code> register pair.</p>","data":"<p><code>cores</code> bitmask.</p>","kind":"call","fn":329,"name":"kbase_pm_invoke","line":414,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c","start":414,"focus":414,"lines":["static void kbase_pm_invoke(struct kbase_device *kbdev, enum kbase_pm_core_type core_type,","\t\t\t    u64 cores, enum kbasep_pm_action action)","{","\tu32 reg;","","\tlockdep_assert_held(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock);","","\treg = core_type_to_reg(kbdev, core_type, action);","","#if !MALI_USE_CSF","\tif (cores) {","\t\tu64 state = kbase_pm_get_state(kbdev, core_type, ACTION_READY);",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"pm","title":"Work finished: drop reference","tag":"both","text":"<p>When the count reaches 0 the policy may power down. Waiters for <code>zero_active_count_wait</code> are woken (used by suspend).</p>","data":"<p><code>--pm.active_count</code>. At 0: <code>kbase_hwaccess_pm_gpu_idle()</code> and <code>wake_up(&amp;pm.zero_active_count_wait)</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2810,"name":"kbase_pm_context_idle","line":146,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c","start":146,"focus":146,"lines":["void kbase_pm_context_idle(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{","\tkbase_pm_lock(kbdev);","\tkbase_pm_context_idle_locked(kbdev);","\tkbase_pm_unlock(kbdev);","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"plat","title":"Power off","tag":"both","text":"<p>Requests the L2 and shaders be turned off; the final clock-off happens in the power-off worker once the hardware is off.</p>","data":"<p><code>backend-&gt;poweroff_wait_in_progress</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":292,"name":"kbase_pm_do_poweroff","line":653,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c","start":653,"focus":653,"lines":["void kbase_pm_do_poweroff(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{","\tunsigned long flags;","","\tlockdep_assert_held(&kbdev->pm.lock);","","\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","","\tif (!kbdev->pm.backend.gpu_powered)","\t\tgoto unlock_hwaccess;","","\tif (kbdev->pm.backend.poweroff_wait_in_progress)"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c"},{"lane":"plat","to":"pm","title":"Runtime PM callbacks","tag":"both","text":"<p>Only when <code>KBASE_PM_RUNTIME</code> is defined: Linux runtime PM calls into the driver, which calls the platform's runtime off callback.</p>","data":"<p>The Linux runtime-PM usage count of <code>kbdev-&gt;dev</code>, then the platform's <code>power_runtime_off_callback</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2110,"name":"kbase_device_runtime_suspend","line":6099,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":6099,"focus":6099,"lines":["static int kbase_device_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)","{","\tstruct kbase_device *kbdev = to_kbase_device(dev);","\tint ret = 0;","","\tif (!kbdev)","\t\treturn -ENODEV;","","\tdev_dbg(dev, \"Callback %s\\n\", __func__);","\tKBASE_KTRACE_ADD(kbdev, PM_RUNTIME_SUSPEND_CALLBACK, NULL, 0);","","#if MALI_USE_CSF"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"}]},{"id":"suspend","title":"System suspend and resume","summary":"<p>The OS asks the driver to suspend: stop scheduling, drain the active count to zero, power off; resume runs the reverse.</p>","lanes":[["vfs","Linux kernel core"],["core","kbase Linux glue (core_linux)"],["jd","JM: JD + JS"],["csf","CSF queues + scheduler"],["pm","Power mgmt"],["plat","Platform (clocks/regulators)"]],"tag":"both","intro":"","dataflow":"<ul><li><strong>The <code>kbdev-&gt;pm.suspending</code> flag:</strong> blocks new active references. Callers with <code>KBASE_PM_SUSPEND_HANDLER_*</code> get an error.</li><li><strong>JM:</strong> running atoms are soft-stopped and requeued.</li><li><strong>CSF:</strong> running groups are suspended by the firmware into their <strong>suspend buffers</strong> (GPU memory), and the MCU is halted.</li><li><strong>Hardware counters:</strong> the accumulated values are kept; counting is disabled.</li></ul>","notes":"","steps":[{"lane":"vfs","to":"core","title":"OS suspend callback","tag":"both","text":"<p><code>kbase_pm_ops.suspend</code>. Devfreq is suspended afterwards.</p>","data":"<p><code>struct device *</code> → <code>kbdev</code> (<code>to_kbase_device</code>).</p>","kind":"call","fn":2108,"name":"kbase_device_suspend","line":6031,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":6031,"focus":6031,"lines":["static int kbase_device_suspend(struct device *dev)","{","\tstruct kbase_device *kbdev = to_kbase_device(dev);","","\tif (!kbdev)","\t\treturn -ENODEV;","","\tif (kbase_pm_suspend(kbdev)) {","\t\tdev_warn(kbdev->dev, \"Abort suspend as GPU suspension failed\");","\t\treturn -EBUSY;","\t}",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"pm","title":"kbase_pm_suspend","tag":"both","text":"<p>With the arbiter, this becomes a VM event; otherwise it calls the driver suspend directly.</p>","data":"<p>With the arbiter: <code>KBASE_VM_OS_SUSPEND_EVENT</code>; without: direct call.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2815,"name":"kbase_pm_suspend","line":370,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c","start":370,"focus":370,"lines":["int kbase_pm_suspend(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{","\tint result = 0;","","#ifdef CONFIG_MALI_ARBITER_SUPPORT","\tif (kbdev->arb.arb_if)","\t\tkbase_arbiter_pm_vm_event(kbdev, KBASE_VM_OS_SUSPEND_EVENT);","\telse","\t\tresult = kbase_pm_driver_suspend(kbdev);","#else","\tresult = kbase_pm_driver_suspend(kbdev);","#endif /* CONFIG_MALI_ARBITER_SUPPORT */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"pm","title":"Disable hwcnt, mark suspending","tag":"both","text":"<p>Perf counters are disabled first.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;pm.suspending = true</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2813,"name":"kbase_pm_driver_suspend","line":214,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c","start":211,"focus":214,"lines":["\t/* Disable GPU hardware counters.","\t * This call will block until counters are disabled.","\t */","\tkbase_hwcnt_context_disable(kbdev->hwcnt_gpu_ctx);","","\tmutex_lock(&kbdev->pm.lock);","\tif (WARN_ON(kbase_pm_is_suspending(kbdev))) {","\t\tmutex_unlock(&kbdev->pm.lock);","\t\t/* No error handling for this condition */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"jd","title":"JM: suspend job scheduler","tag":"JM","text":"<p>Removes running contexts, which releases their PM references.</p>","data":"<p>Submission is disabled; every scheduled context is retained and then pulled out of the run pool, releasing its PM reference.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2813,"name":"kbase_pm_driver_suspend","line":256,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c","start":253,"focus":256,"lines":["\t/* Suspend job scheduler and associated components, so that it releases all","\t * the PM active count references","\t */","\tkbasep_js_suspend(kbdev);","#else","\tif (kbase_csf_scheduler_pm_suspend(kbdev))","\t\tgoto exit;","#endif",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"csf","title":"CSF: suspend the scheduler","tag":"CSF","text":"<p>Suspends all on-slot groups and stops the tick timer.</p>","data":"<p>Group state → SUSPENDED.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2813,"name":"kbase_pm_driver_suspend","line":258,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c","start":255,"focus":258,"lines":["\t */","\tkbasep_js_suspend(kbdev);","#else","\tif (kbase_csf_scheduler_pm_suspend(kbdev))","\t\tgoto exit;","#endif","","\tscheduling_suspended = true;",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"pm","title":"Wait for active_count == 0","tag":"both","text":"<p>Nothing may be holding the GPU powered past this point.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;pm.active_count</code> must reach 0.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2813,"name":"kbase_pm_driver_suspend","line":270,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c","start":267,"focus":270,"lines":["\t */","\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \">wait_event - waiting for active_count == 0 (pid = %d)\\n\",","\t\tcurrent->pid);","\twait_event(kbdev->pm.zero_active_count_wait, kbdev->pm.active_count == 0);","\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \">wait_event - waiting done\\n\");","","#if MALI_USE_CSF","\t/* At this point, any kbase context termination should either have run to","\t * completion and any further context termination can only begin after"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"plat","title":"Backend suspend: power off","tag":"both","text":"<p>Forces the GPU (and MCU) off and calls the platform suspend callback.</p>","data":"<p>PM backend state: L2/shader (and MCU) driven to OFF; <code>gpu_powered = false</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":303,"name":"kbase_hwaccess_pm_suspend","line":910,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c","start":910,"focus":910,"lines":["int kbase_hwaccess_pm_suspend(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{","\tint ret = 0;","","#if MALI_USE_CSF && defined(KBASE_PM_RUNTIME)","\tret = kbase_pm_do_poweroff_sync(kbdev);","\tif (ret)","\t\treturn ret;","#else","\t/* Force power off the GPU and all cores (regardless of policy), only","\t * after the PM active count reaches zero (otherwise, we risk turning it","\t * off prematurely)"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_backend.c"},{"lane":"vfs","to":"core","title":"OS resume callback","tag":"both","text":"<p>Mirror of suspend.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev</code>; devfreq resume work is queued (<code>DEVFREQ_WORK_RESUME</code>).</p>","kind":"call","fn":2109,"name":"kbase_device_resume","line":6066,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":6066,"focus":6066,"lines":["static int kbase_device_resume(struct device *dev)","{","\tstruct kbase_device *kbdev = to_kbase_device(dev);","","\tif (!kbdev)","\t\treturn -ENODEV;","","\tkbase_pm_resume(kbdev);","","#ifdef CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD_DVFS","\tkbase_pm_metrics_start(kbdev);","#endif"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"plat","title":"Backend resume","tag":"both","text":"<p>Powers back on and re-enables scheduling and counters (<code>resume_job_scheduling</code>, <code>reenable_hwcnt_on_resume</code>).</p>","data":"<p><code>pm.suspending = false</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2814,"name":"kbase_pm_driver_resume","line":339,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c","start":336,"focus":339,"lines":["\tCSTD_UNUSED(arb_gpu_start);","","\t/* MUST happen before any pm_context_active calls occur */","\tkbase_hwaccess_pm_resume(kbdev);","","\t/* Initial active call, to power on the GPU/cores if needed */","#ifdef CONFIG_MALI_ARBITER_SUPPORT","\tif (kbase_pm_context_active_handle_suspend(","\t\t    kbdev, (arb_gpu_start ? KBASE_PM_SUSPEND_HANDLER_VM_GPU_GRANTED :"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_pm.c"}]},{"id":"fault","title":"GPU page fault handling (grow or kill)","summary":"<p>The GPU touches an unmapped address → MMU IRQ → worker → either allocate pages for a growable region or report and kill.</p>","lanes":[["hw","GPU hardware"],["irq","IRQ handlers (top half)"],["wq","Workqueue / kthread (bottom half)"],["mem","Memory mgmt"],["mmu","GPU MMU"]],"tag":"both","intro":"","dataflow":"<ul><li><strong>Fault registers:</strong> <code>FAULTADDRESS</code> and <code>FAULTSTATUS</code> (exception type and access type) go into <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/250\"><code>struct kbase_fault</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@271\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:271\">mali_kbase_defs.h:271</a>)</span>.</li><li><strong>Region lookup:</strong> the address is matched to a <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/319\"><code>struct kbase_va_region</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.h@665\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_mem.h:665\">mali_kbase_mem.h:665</a>)</span>, and the driver checks <code>KBASE_REG_GROWABLE</code> and <code>extension</code>.</li><li><strong>Growing:</strong> new pages go into <code>gpu_alloc-&gt;pages[]</code> and new PTEs are written. Then the fault is cleared and the AS is unlocked.</li><li><strong>Killing:</strong> the error is reported to the context. JM marks the atom <code>BASE_JD_EVENT_*</code> fault; CSF reports a group fatal error.</li></ul>","notes":"","steps":[{"lane":"hw","to":"irq","title":"MMU interrupt","tag":"both","text":"<p>See <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/irq\">GPU interrupt handling (top half → bottom half)</a>.</p>","data":"<p><code>MMU_IRQ_STATUS</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":125,"name":"kbase_mmu_irq_handler","line":76,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c","start":76,"focus":76,"lines":["static irqreturn_t kbase_mmu_irq_handler(int irq, void *data)","{","\tunsigned long flags;","\tstruct kbase_device *kbdev = kbase_untag(data);","\tu32 val;","","\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","","\tif (!kbdev->pm.backend.gpu_powered) {","\t\t/* GPU is turned off - IRQ is not for us */","\t\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\t\treturn IRQ_NONE;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_irq_linux.c"},{"lane":"irq","to":"wq","title":"Record + queue work","tag":"both","text":"<p>Saves the fault address and status into <code>as-&gt;pf_data</code> and queues the worker.</p>","data":"<p><a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/250\"><code>struct kbase_fault</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@271\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:271\">mali_kbase_defs.h:271</a>)</span>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2967,"name":"kbase_mmu_interrupt","line":355,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c","start":352,"focus":355,"lines":["\t\tkctx = kbase_ctx_sched_as_to_ctx_refcount(kbdev, as_no);","","\t\t/* find faulting address */","\t\tfault->addr = kbase_reg_read64(kbdev, MMU_AS_OFFSET(as_no, FAULTADDRESS));","\t\t/* Mark the fault protected or not */","\t\tfault->protected_mode = kbdev->protected_mode;","","\t\tif (kbdev->protected_mode && fault->addr) {","\t\t\t/* check if address reporting is allowed */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_jm.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"mmu","title":"Page fault worker","tag":"both","text":"<p>Takes a reference on the context owning the AS, then decodes the exception type.</p>","data":"<p><code>as-&gt;pf_data</code> (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/250\"><code>struct kbase_fault</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h@271\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_defs.h:271\">mali_kbase_defs.h:271</a>)</span>) and the owning <code>kctx</code>, looked up from the AS number.</p>","kind":"call","fn":3004,"name":"kbase_mmu_page_fault_worker","line":1230,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c","start":1230,"focus":1230,"lines":["void kbase_mmu_page_fault_worker(struct work_struct *data)","{","\tu64 fault_pfn;","\tu32 fault_status;","\tsize_t new_pages;","\tsize_t fault_rel_pfn;","\tstruct kbase_as *faulting_as;","\tunsigned int as_no;","\tstruct kbase_context *kctx;","\tstruct kbase_device *kbdev;","\tstruct kbase_va_region *region;","\tstruct kbase_fault *fault;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"mmu","title":"Non-translation faults → kill","tag":"both","text":"<p>Permission, address-size and memory-attribute faults are not recoverable for this context.</p>","data":"<p>Exception type decoded from <code>fault-&gt;status</code> → fatal for this context.</p>","kind":"call","fn":3004,"name":"kbase_mmu_page_fault_worker","line":1337,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c","start":1334,"focus":1337,"lines":["\t\t}","#endif","","\t\tkbase_mmu_report_fault_and_kill(kctx, faulting_as, \"Permission failure\", fault);","\t\tgoto fault_done;","","#if !MALI_USE_CSF","\tcase AS_FAULTSTATUS_EXCEPTION_TYPE_TRANSTAB_BUS_FAULT_0:","\t\tfallthrough;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"mem","title":"Find the region","tag":"both","text":"<p>Under <code>kbase_gpu_vm_lock</code>.</p>","data":"<p><code>region</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":3004,"name":"kbase_mmu_page_fault_worker","line":1438,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c","start":1435,"focus":1438,"lines":["\t */","\tkbase_gpu_vm_lock(kctx);","","\tregion = kbase_region_tracker_find_region_enclosing_address(kctx, fault->addr);","\tif (kbase_is_region_invalid_or_free(region)) {","\t\tkbase_gpu_vm_unlock(kctx);","\t\tkbase_mmu_report_fault_and_kill(kctx, faulting_as,","\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Memory is not mapped on the GPU\", fault);","\t\tgoto fault_done;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"mem","title":"Not growable → kill","tag":"both","text":"<p>Faults outside growable memory are application bugs (or use-after-free).</p>","data":"<p><code>region-&gt;flags</code> lacks <code>KBASE_REG_GROWABLE</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":3004,"name":"kbase_mmu_page_fault_worker","line":1470,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c","start":1467,"focus":1470,"lines":["","\tif ((region->flags & GROWABLE_FLAGS_REQUIRED) != GROWABLE_FLAGS_REQUIRED) {","\t\tkbase_gpu_vm_unlock(kctx);","\t\tkbase_mmu_report_fault_and_kill(kctx, faulting_as, \"Memory is not growable\", fault);","\t\tgoto fault_done;","\t}","","\tif ((region->flags & KBASE_REG_DONT_NEED)) {","\t\tkbase_gpu_vm_unlock(kctx);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mem","title":"Grow: allocate pages","tag":"both","text":"<p>Allocates <code>extension</code>-sized chunks from the context/device pools. It may need to grow the pools without holding locks, then retry.</p>","data":"<p>New pages.</p>","kind":"call","fn":3003,"name":"page_fault_try_alloc","line":1077,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c","start":1077,"focus":1077,"lines":["static bool page_fault_try_alloc(struct kbase_context *kctx, struct kbase_va_region *region,","\t\t\t\t size_t new_pages, size_t *pages_to_grow, bool *grow_2mb_pool,","\t\t\t\t bool fallback_to_small, struct kbase_sub_alloc **prealloc_sas)","{","\tsize_t total_gpu_pages_alloced = 0;","\tsize_t total_cpu_pages_alloced = 0;","\tstruct kbase_mem_pool *pool, *root_pool;","\tbool alloc_failed = false;","\tsize_t pages_still_required;","\tsize_t total_mempools_free_small = 0;","","\tlockdep_assert_held(&kctx->reg_lock);","\tlockdep_assert_held(&kctx->mem_partials_lock);",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c"},{"lane":"mem","to":"mmu","title":"Map new pages","tag":"both","text":"<p>Inserts the new pages into the page table at the faulting offset.</p>","data":"<p>PTEs.</p>","kind":"call","fn":3004,"name":"kbase_mmu_page_fault_worker","line":1609,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c","start":1606,"focus":1609,"lines":["\t\t * so the no_flush version of insert_pages is used which allows","\t\t * us to unlock the MMU as we see fit.","\t\t */","\t\terr = mmu_insert_pages_no_flush(kbdev, &kctx->mmu, region->start_pfn + pfn_offset,","\t\t\t\t\t\t&kbase_get_gpu_phy_pages(region)[pfn_offset],","\t\t\t\t\t\tnew_pages, region->flags,","\t\t\t\t\t\tregion->gpu_alloc->group_id, &dirty_pgds, region,","\t\t\t\t\t\tfalse);","\t\tif (err) {"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c"},{"lane":"mmu","to":"hw","title":"Clear fault & re-enable","tag":"both","text":"<p>The GPU retries the access and continues.</p>","data":"<p><code>MMU_IRQ_MASK</code> bit for this AS set again; the AS is unlocked so the GPU retries the access.</p>","kind":"call","fn":3004,"name":"kbase_mmu_page_fault_worker","line":1669,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c","start":1666,"focus":1669,"lines":["\t\t/* AS transaction end */","","\t\t/* reenable this in the mask */","\t\tkbase_mmu_hw_enable_fault(kbdev, faulting_as, KBASE_MMU_FAULT_TYPE_PAGE);","","#ifdef CONFIG_MALI_CINSTR_GWT","\t\tif (kctx->gwt_enabled) {","\t\t\t/* GWT also tracks growable regions. */","\t\t\tstruct kbasep_gwt_list_element *pos;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/mali_kbase_mmu.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"mmu","title":"Report and kill (CSF variant)","tag":"both","text":"<p>Prints the decoded fault, disables the AS for the context and reports to the scheduler, which evicts the context's groups.</p>","data":"<p>Fault address/status printed; the AS is disabled for the context and its GPU work terminated.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2949,"name":"kbase_mmu_report_fault_and_kill","line":195,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_csf.c","start":195,"focus":195,"lines":["void kbase_mmu_report_fault_and_kill(struct kbase_context *kctx, struct kbase_as *as,","\t\t\t\t     const char *reason_str, struct kbase_fault *fault)","{","\tunsigned long flags;","\tstruct kbase_device *kbdev = kctx->kbdev;","","\t/* Make sure the context was active */","\tif (WARN_ON(atomic_read(&kctx->refcount) <= 0))","\t\treturn;","","\tif (!kbase_ctx_flag(kctx, KCTX_PAGE_FAULT_REPORT_SKIP)) {","\t\tconst u32 status = fault->status;","\t\t/* decode the fault status */"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mmu/backend/mali_kbase_mmu_csf.c"}]},{"id":"reset","title":"GPU reset and recovery","summary":"<p>Something hangs → prepare + request reset → worker stops everything, soft-resets the GPU, re-inits, restores address spaces, restarts work.</p>","lanes":[["core","kbase Linux glue (core_linux)"],["wq","Workqueue / kthread (bottom half)"],["jd","JM: JD + JS"],["csf","CSF queues + scheduler"],["pm","Power mgmt"],["hw","GPU hardware"],["mmu","GPU MMU"]],"tag":"both","intro":"","dataflow":"<ul><li><strong>Reset state machine:</strong><ul><li>JM: <code>hwaccess.backend.reset_gpu</code> goes NOT_PENDING → PREPARED → COMMITTED → HAPPENING.</li><li>CSF: <code>csf.reset.state</code>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>In-flight work:</strong><ul><li>JM atoms are evicted from the slot ringbuffers and returned to JS, or failed.</li><li>CSF groups are evicted from their slots. Those that were running get a fatal error.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Hardware state:</strong> lost by the reset, then rebuilt. The driver repeats the <code>kbase_pm_init_hw</code> configuration, rewrites every AS's TRANSTAB from <code>kctx-&gt;mmu</code> (<code>kbase_ctx_sched_restore_all_as</code>) and, on CSF, reboots the firmware.</li></ul>","notes":"","steps":[{"lane":"core","to":"wq","title":"JM: request reset","tag":"JM","text":"<p>After <code>kbase_prepare_to_reset_gpu</code> succeeds, arm a timer to let soft-stopped jobs drain first.</p>","data":"<p><code>reset_gpu = COMMITTED</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":176,"name":"kbase_reset_gpu","line":1192,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c","start":1189,"focus":1192,"lines":["\t\t\"Preparing to soft-reset GPU: Waiting (up to %d ms) for all jobs to complete soft-stop\\n\",","\t\tkbdev->reset_timeout_ms);","","\thrtimer_start(&kbdev->hwaccess.backend.reset_timer,","\t\t      HR_TIMER_DELAY_MSEC(kbdev->reset_timeout_ms), HRTIMER_MODE_REL);","","\t/* Try resetting early */","\tkbasep_try_reset_gpu_early(kbdev);","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"wq","title":"JM: timer → worker","tag":"JM","text":"<p>Runs <code>kbasep_reset_timeout_worker</code> on the reset workqueue.</p>","data":"<p><code>hwaccess.backend.reset_work</code> queued on <code>reset_workq</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":171,"name":"kbasep_reset_timer_callback","line":1060,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c","start":1057,"focus":1060,"lines":["\t/* Reset still pending? */","\tif (atomic_cmpxchg(&kbdev->hwaccess.backend.reset_gpu, KBASE_RESET_GPU_COMMITTED,","\t\t\t   KBASE_RESET_GPU_HAPPENING) == KBASE_RESET_GPU_COMMITTED)","\t\tqueue_work(kbdev->hwaccess.backend.reset_workq,","\t\t\t   &kbdev->hwaccess.backend.reset_work);","","\treturn HRTIMER_NORESTART;","}",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"jd","title":"JM: stop and evict","tag":"JM","text":"<p>Disables IRQs and evicts every atom in the slot ringbuffers.</p>","data":"<p>Atoms in the slot ringbuffers → returned to JS or completed with an error code.</p>","kind":"call","fn":170,"name":"kbasep_reset_timeout_worker","line":983,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c","start":980,"focus":983,"lines":["\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\tkbdev->protected_mode = false;","\tif (!kbdev->pm.backend.protected_entry_transition_override)","\t\tkbase_backend_reset(kbdev, &end_timestamp);","\tkbase_pm_metrics_update(kbdev, NULL);","\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","","\t/* Tell hardware counters a reset is about to occur.","\t * If the instr backend is in an unrecoverable error state (e.g. due to"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"hw","title":"JM: soft reset + init","tag":"JM","text":"<p><code>kbase_pm_init_hw</code> → <code>kbase_pm_do_reset</code> writes <code>GPU_COMMAND = SOFT_RESET</code> and waits for <code>RESET_COMPLETED</code>.</p>","data":"<p><code>GPU_COMMAND = SOFT_RESET</code>, then wait for <code>RESET_COMPLETED</code>; workarounds/config re-applied.</p>","kind":"call","fn":170,"name":"kbasep_reset_timeout_worker","line":995,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c","start":992,"focus":995,"lines":["\tkbase_instr_hwcnt_on_before_reset(kbdev);","","\t/* Reset the GPU */","\tkbase_pm_init_hw(kbdev, 0);","","\tmutex_unlock(&kbdev->pm.lock);","","\tmutex_lock(&js_devdata->runpool_mutex);",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"mmu","title":"JM: restore address spaces","tag":"JM","text":"<p>Re-programs every AS that had a context.</p>","data":"<p><code>TRANSTAB</code>/<code>MEMATTR</code>/<code>TRANSCFG</code> re-written from each <code>kctx-&gt;mmu</code> in <code>kbdev-&gt;as_to_kctx[]</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":170,"name":"kbasep_reset_timeout_worker","line":1003,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c","start":1000,"focus":1003,"lines":["","\tmutex_lock(&kbdev->mmu_hw_mutex);","\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\tkbase_ctx_sched_restore_all_as(kbdev);","\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\tmutex_unlock(&kbdev->mmu_hw_mutex);","","\tkbase_pm_enable_interrupts(kbdev);",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"jd","title":"JM: restart scheduling","tag":"JM","text":"<p>Atoms run again.</p>","data":"<p>Runnable contexts on the JS lists are pulled and submitted again.</p>","kind":"call","fn":170,"name":"kbasep_reset_timeout_worker","line":1035,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c","start":1032,"focus":1035,"lines":["","\t/* Try submitting some jobs to restart processing */","\tKBASE_KTRACE_ADD_JM(kbdev, JM_SUBMIT_AFTER_RESET, NULL, NULL, 0u, 0);","\tkbase_js_sched_all(kbdev);","","\t/* Process any pending slot updates */","\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\tkbase_backend_slot_update(kbdev);","\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_hw.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"wq","title":"CSF: request reset","tag":"CSF","text":"<p>Queues <code>kbase_csf_reset_gpu_worker</code>.</p>","data":"<p><code>csf.reset.state</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1050,"name":"kbase_reset_gpu","line":546,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c","start":543,"focus":546,"lines":["","\tkbase_disjoint_state_up(kbdev);","","\tqueue_work(kbdev->csf.reset.workq, &kbdev->csf.reset.work);","}","KBASE_EXPORT_TEST_API(kbase_reset_gpu);","","void kbase_reset_gpu_locked(struct kbase_device *kbdev)","{"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"csf","title":"CSF: evict groups","tag":"CSF","text":"<p>Groups leave their slots. Those that were running get an error reported.</p>","data":"<p>Groups resident on CSG slots are evicted; <code>scheduler-&gt;csg_slots[]</code> is cleared.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1046,"name":"kbase_csf_reset_gpu_now","line":402,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c","start":399,"focus":402,"lines":["\t * of active CSG slots would also be done as a part of reset.","\t */","\tif (likely(firmware_inited))","\t\tkbase_csf_scheduler_reset(kbdev);","","\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\tkbdev->csf.firmware_reload_needed = false;","\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"hw","title":"CSF: reset once","tag":"CSF","text":"<p>Disables IRQs, flushes the MMU workqueues, dumps the firmware log, resets the GPU.</p>","data":"<p>Firmware log dumped (if enabled); GPU registers reset to defaults.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1045,"name":"kbase_csf_reset_gpu_once","line":344,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c","start":341,"focus":344,"lines":["","\tmutex_lock(&kbdev->pm.lock);","\t/* Reset the GPU */","\terr = kbase_pm_init_hw(kbdev, 0);","","\tmutex_unlock(&kbdev->pm.lock);","","\tif (WARN_ON(err))","\t\treturn SOFT_RESET_FAILED;"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c"},{"lane":"wq","to":"mmu","title":"CSF: restore AS","tag":"CSF","text":"<p>Same as JM: every AS that had a context is re-programmed, so contexts keep their GPU address spaces across the reset.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;as_to_kctx[]</code> → each assigned AS re-programmed.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1045,"name":"kbase_csf_reset_gpu_once","line":353,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c","start":350,"focus":353,"lines":["","\tmutex_lock(&kbdev->mmu_hw_mutex);","\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\tkbase_ctx_sched_restore_all_as(kbdev);","\t{","\t\tkbase_ipa_control_handle_gpu_reset_post(kbdev);","\t}","\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\tmutex_unlock(&kbdev->mmu_hw_mutex);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c"},{"lane":"pm","to":"hw","title":"CSF: reboot firmware","tag":"CSF","text":"<p>The MCU state machine reloads and reboots the firmware; the global interface is re-initialised (<code>kbase_csf_firmware_global_reinit</code>).</p>","data":"<p>MCU state machine reboots the firmware from the retained image in <code>kbdev-&gt;csf.fw</code>; the global interface is re-initialised.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1045,"name":"kbase_csf_reset_gpu_once","line":365,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c","start":362,"focus":365,"lines":["\tmutex_lock(&kbdev->pm.lock);","\tkbase_pm_reset_complete(kbdev);","\t/* Synchronously wait for the reload of firmware to complete */","\terr = kbase_pm_wait_for_desired_state(kbdev);","\tmutex_unlock(&kbdev->pm.lock);","","\tif (err) {","\t\tspin_lock_irqsave(&kbdev->hwaccess_lock, flags);","\t\tif (!kbase_pm_l2_is_in_desired_state(kbdev))"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_reset_gpu.c"}]},{"id":"close","title":"Closing the device: context teardown","summary":"<p><code>close()</code> → <code>kbase_release</code> → destroy context: stop work, free memory, release the address space.</p>","lanes":[["user","Userspace (UMD / app)"],["core","kbase Linux glue (core_linux)"],["dev","Device / context init"],["csf","CSF queues + scheduler"],["jd","JM: JD + JS"],["mem","Memory mgmt"],["mmu","GPU MMU"]],"tag":"both","intro":"","dataflow":"<ul><li><strong>Outstanding GPU work:</strong> flushed or killed. JM uses <code>kbase_context_flush_jobs</code> / <code>kbase_jd_zap_context</code>; CSF terminates the context's groups.</li><li><strong>Regions:</strong> every region in every zone is freed and its pages return to the pools.</li><li><strong>Page tables:</strong> freed. The AS is released.</li></ul>","notes":"","steps":[{"lane":"user","to":"core","title":"close(fd)","tag":"both","text":"<p>Last reference to the file dropped.</p>","data":"<p><code>filp-&gt;private_data</code> → <code>struct kbase_file</code>.</p>","kind":"call","fn":1939,"name":"kbase_release","line":779,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":779,"focus":779,"lines":["static int kbase_release(struct inode *inode, struct file *filp)","{","\tstruct kbase_file *const kfile = filp->private_data;","","\tCSTD_UNUSED(inode);","","\tkbase_file_delete(kfile);","\treturn 0;","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"core","to":"dev","title":"Delete kbase_file","tag":"both","text":"<p>Destroys the context if setup completed.</p>","data":"<p><code>kfile-&gt;kctx</code> (only if setup completed).</p>","kind":"call","fn":1920,"name":"kbase_file_delete","line":355,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c","start":352,"focus":355,"lines":["#endif","\t\tkbase_context_debugfs_term(kctx);","","\t\tkbase_destroy_context(kctx);","","\t\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \"deleted base context\\n\");","\t}","","\tkbase_release_device(kbdev);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"dev","title":"Wait out system suspend","tag":"both","text":"<p>Teardown needs the GPU, so it blocks while a system suspend is in progress.</p>","data":"<p><code>kbdev-&gt;pm.suspending</code> flag / <code>pm.resume_wait</code> wait queue.</p>","kind":"call","fn":471,"name":"kbase_destroy_context","line":192,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c","start":189,"focus":192,"lines":["#ifdef CONFIG_MALI_ARBITER_SUPPORT","\tatomic_inc(&kbdev->pm.gpu_users_waiting);","#endif /* CONFIG_MALI_ARBITER_SUPPORT */","\twhile (kbase_pm_context_active_handle_suspend(kbdev,","\t\t\t\t\t\t      KBASE_PM_SUSPEND_HANDLER_DONT_INCREASE)) {","\t\tdev_dbg(kbdev->dev, \"Suspend in progress when destroying context\");","\t\twait_event(kbdev->pm.resume_wait, !kbase_pm_is_suspending(kbdev));","\t}","#ifdef CONFIG_MALI_ARBITER_SUPPORT"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"dev","title":"Run term steps in reverse","tag":"both","text":"<p>Calls each <code>context_init[].term</code> from last to first.</p>","data":"<p><code>context_init[]</code> table, walked from the last row to the first.</p>","kind":"call","fn":471,"name":"kbase_destroy_context","line":213,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c","start":210,"focus":213,"lines":["","\tkbase_mem_pool_group_mark_dying(&kctx->mem_pools);","","\tkbase_context_term_partial(kctx, ARRAY_SIZE(context_init));","","\tkbase_pm_context_idle(kbdev);","}","KBASE_EXPORT_SYMBOL(kbase_destroy_context);",""]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/backend/mali_kbase_context_csf.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"csf","title":"CSF: terminate groups and queues","tag":"CSF","text":"<p>Terminates every queue group, KCPU queue and tiler heap of the context.</p>","data":"<p><code>kctx-&gt;csf.queue_groups[]</code>, the KCPU queue array and the tiler heap list.</p>","kind":"call","fn":583,"name":"kbase_csf_ctx_term","line":1777,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c","start":1777,"focus":1777,"lines":["void kbase_csf_ctx_term(struct kbase_context *kctx)","{","\tstruct kbase_device *kbdev = kctx->kbdev;","\tstruct kbase_as *as = NULL;","\tunsigned long flags;","\tu32 i;","\tint err;","\tbool reset_prevented = false;","","\t/* As the kbase context is terminating, its debugfs sub-directory would","\t * have been removed already and so would be the debugfs file created","\t * for queue groups & kcpu queues, hence no need to explicitly remove"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"mem","title":"Free all regions","tag":"both","text":"<p>Every remaining region is freed; physical pages go back to the pools.</p>","data":"<p>Every <code>kbase_va_region</code> in <code>kctx-&gt;reg_zone[]</code>; physical pages return to the context/device pools.</p>","kind":"call","fn":2852,"name":"kbase_region_tracker_term","line":994,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.c","start":994,"focus":994,"lines":["void kbase_region_tracker_term(struct kbase_context *kctx)","{","\tunsigned int i;","","\tWARN(kctx->as_nr != KBASEP_AS_NR_INVALID,","\t     \"kctx-%d_%d must first be scheduled out to flush GPU caches+tlbs before erasing remaining regions\",","\t     kctx->tgid, kctx->id);","","\tkbase_gpu_vm_lock(kctx);","","\tfor (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(zones_init); i++)","\t\tzones_init[i].term(kctx);"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_reg_track.c"},{"lane":"dev","to":"mmu","title":"Free page tables","tag":"both","text":"<p>Tears down the context's MMU tables.</p>","data":"<p><code>kctx-&gt;mmu.pgd</code> and all lower-level page-table pages.</p>","kind":"call","fn":495,"name":"kbase_context_mmu_term","line":314,"ex":{"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c","start":314,"focus":314,"lines":["void kbase_context_mmu_term(struct kbase_context *kctx)","{","\tkbase_mmu_term(kctx->kbdev, &kctx->mmu);","}"]},"file":"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c"}]}],"glossary":[{"id":"module","term":"kernel module","aka":["module"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Code loaded into the running kernel (<code>insmod</code>/<code>modprobe</code>). Entry/exit functions are declared with <code>module_init</code>/<code>module_exit</code>. This driver builds as <code>mali_kbase.ko</code>.</p>","plain":"Code loaded into the running kernel (`insmod`/`modprobe`). Entry/exit functions are declared with `module_init`/`module_exit`. This driver builds as `mali_kbase.ko`."},{"id":"platform-driver","term":"platform driver","aka":["probe"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>A Linux driver for a device that is not on a discoverable bus (like PCI). The kernel matches it to a device-tree node and calls its <code>probe</code>. See <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/2107\"><code>kbase_platform_device_probe()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@5954\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5954\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:5954</a>)</span>.</p>","plain":"A Linux driver for a device that is not on a discoverable bus (like PCI). The kernel matches it to a device-tree node and calls its `probe`. See kbase_platform_device_probe."},{"id":"device-tree","term":"device tree","aka":["DT","DTB"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>A data structure (DT/DTB) passed by the bootloader describing the hardware: register addresses, IRQs, clocks, regulators. Mali bindings: <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/arm,mali-midgard.yaml\"><code>Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/arm,mali-midgard.yaml</code></a>.</p>","plain":"A data structure (DT/DTB) passed by the bootloader describing the hardware: register addresses, IRQs, clocks, regulators. Mali bindings: Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/arm,mali-midgard.yaml."},{"id":"soc","term":"SoC","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>System-on-Chip: CPU, GPU, memory controller etc. on one chip. Each SoC integrates the Mali GPU differently, which is why the driver has a <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/platform\">Platform integration (DT, clocks, regulators, memory groups)</a> layer.</p>","plain":"System-on-Chip: CPU, GPU, memory controller etc. on one chip. Each SoC integrates the Mali GPU differently, which is why the driver has a platform layer."},{"id":"mmio","term":"MMIO","aka":["memory-mapped I/O"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Memory-mapped I/O: device registers appear at physical addresses; the driver <code>ioremap</code>s them and accesses them with read/write helpers (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1502\"><code>kbase_reg_read32()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hw_access/backend/mali_kbase_hw_access_real_hw.c@39\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/hw_access/backend/mali_kbase_hw_access_real_hw.c:39\">hw_access/backend/mali_kbase_hw_access_real_hw.c:39</a>)</span>).</p>","plain":"Memory-mapped I/O: device registers appear at physical addresses; the driver `ioremap`s them and accesses them with read/write helpers (kbase_reg_read32@real_hw)."},{"id":"irq","term":"IRQ","aka":["interrupt"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Interrupt request: a hardware signal that makes the CPU run an interrupt handler. The Mali GPU has JOB, MMU and GPU interrupt sources.</p>","plain":"Interrupt request: a hardware signal that makes the CPU run an interrupt handler. The Mali GPU has JOB, MMU and GPU interrupt sources."},{"id":"top-half","term":"top half / bottom half","aka":["bottom half"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>The interrupt handler itself (top half) must be fast and cannot sleep; longer work is deferred to a workqueue or kthread (bottom half), where sleeping and mutexes are allowed.</p>","plain":"The interrupt handler itself (top half) must be fast and cannot sleep; longer work is deferred to a workqueue or kthread (bottom half), where sleeping and mutexes are allowed."},{"id":"workqueue","term":"workqueue","aka":["work_struct","queue_work"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Kernel facility to run a function (<code>work_struct</code>) later in process context. kbase uses many: reset, page-fault, power-off, devfreq…</p>","plain":"Kernel facility to run a function (`work_struct`) later in process context. kbase uses many: reset, page-fault, power-off, devfreq…"},{"id":"kthread","term":"kthread","aka":["kernel thread"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>A kernel thread. kbase uses <code>mali-gpuq-kthread</code> (CSF scheduler) and per-context <code>mali_jd/&lt;id&gt;</code> kthread workers (JM job completion).</p>","plain":"A kernel thread. kbase uses `mali-gpuq-kthread` (CSF scheduler) and per-context `mali_jd/<id>` kthread workers (JM job completion)."},{"id":"spinlock","term":"spinlock","aka":["spin_lock_irqsave"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>A lock that busy-waits; usable in interrupt context (<code>spin_lock_irqsave</code> also disables local IRQs). Example: <a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_device::hwaccess_lock\"><code>kbase_device::hwaccess_lock</code></a>.</p>","plain":"A lock that busy-waits; usable in interrupt context (`spin_lock_irqsave` also disables local IRQs). Example: kbase_device::hwaccess_lock."},{"id":"mutex","term":"mutex","aka":["mutex_lock"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>A sleeping lock; cannot be taken in interrupt context. Example: <a class=\"lockref\" href=\"#/locks/kbase_pm_device_data::lock\"><code>kbase_pm_device_data::lock</code></a>.</p>","plain":"A sleeping lock; cannot be taken in interrupt context. Example: kbase_pm_device_data::lock."},{"id":"lockdep","term":"lockdep","aka":["lockdep_assert_held"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>The kernel's lock-correctness checker. <code>lockdep_assert_held(&amp;lock)</code> documents (and, in debug kernels, checks) that the caller holds a lock. This site's lock tables are generated from those asserts.</p>","plain":"The kernel's lock-correctness checker. `lockdep_assert_held(&lock)` documents (and, in debug kernels, checks) that the caller holds a lock. This site's lock tables are generated from those asserts."},{"id":"atomic","term":"atomic_t","aka":["atomic_cmpxchg"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>An integer with atomic operations (<code>atomic_inc_return</code>, <code>atomic_cmpxchg</code>), used for refcounts and small state machines without locks.</p>","plain":"An integer with atomic operations (`atomic_inc_return`, `atomic_cmpxchg`), used for refcounts and small state machines without locks."},{"id":"kref","term":"kref","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Reference counter helper; the object is freed when the count drops to zero. <code>kbase_mem_phy_alloc</code> uses one.</p>","plain":"Reference counter helper; the object is freed when the count drops to zero. `kbase_mem_phy_alloc` uses one."},{"id":"fops","term":"file_operations","aka":["fops"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Table of callbacks (open, read, mmap, unlocked_ioctl…) for a device file. kbase's is <code>kbase_fops</code>.</p>","plain":"Table of callbacks (open, read, mmap, unlocked_ioctl…) for a device file. kbase's is `kbase_fops`."},{"id":"ioctl","term":"ioctl","aka":["_IOWR","_IOW","_IOR"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p><code>ioctl(fd, cmd, arg)</code>: the generic \"device-specific command\" syscall. The <code>cmd</code> number encodes direction, type (0x80 for kbase), number and argument size (<code>_IOWR</code> etc.). See the <a href=\"#/ioctls\">ioctl reference</a>.</p>","plain":"`ioctl(fd, cmd, arg)`: the generic \"device-specific command\" syscall. The `cmd` number encodes direction, type (0x80 for kbase), number and argument size (`_IOWR` etc.). See the ioctl reference."},{"id":"mmap","term":"mmap","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Maps memory into a process's address space. kbase uses the mmap <em>offset</em> as a command: cookies for SAME_VA allocations, special handles for CSF I/O pages, the tracking page and MMU dumps.</p>","plain":"Maps memory into a process's address space. kbase uses the mmap *offset* as a command: cookies for SAME_VA allocations, special handles for CSF I/O pages, the tracking page and MMU dumps."},{"id":"vma","term":"VMA","aka":["vm_area_struct"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p><code>struct vm_area_struct</code>: one contiguous CPU virtual mapping in a process.</p>","plain":"`struct vm_area_struct`: one contiguous CPU virtual mapping in a process."},{"id":"copy-from-user","term":"copy_from_user / copy_to_user","aka":["copy_from_user","copy_to_user"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Safe copying between user and kernel memory. Every ioctl argument goes through these in the <code>KBASE_HANDLE_IOCTL_*</code> macros.</p>","plain":"Safe copying between user and kernel memory. Every ioctl argument goes through these in the `KBASE_HANDLE_IOCTL_*` macros."},{"id":"misc-device","term":"misc device","aka":["miscdevice"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>A simple character device registered with <code>misc_register</code>; how <code>/dev/maliN</code> is created (<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1472\"><code>kbase_device_misc_register()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c@443\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/device/mali_kbase_device.c:443\">device/mali_kbase_device.c:443</a>)</span>).</p>","plain":"A simple character device registered with `misc_register`; how `/dev/maliN` is created (kbase_device_misc_register)."},{"id":"sysfs","term":"sysfs","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p><code>/sys/...</code> files exposing device attributes (e.g. <code>power_policy</code>). See the <a href=\"#/interfaces\">interfaces page</a>.</p>","plain":"`/sys/...` files exposing device attributes (e.g. `power_policy`). See the interfaces page."},{"id":"debugfs","term":"debugfs","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p><code>/sys/kernel/debug/...</code> debug files; no ABI guarantees. kbase creates ~90 (under <code>/sys/kernel/debug/mali0/</code>).</p>","plain":"`/sys/kernel/debug/...` debug files; no ABI guarantees. kbase creates ~90 (under `/sys/kernel/debug/mali0/`)."},{"id":"ftrace","term":"ftrace / tracepoint","aka":["tracepoint","TRACE_EVENT"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Kernel tracing infrastructure; <code>TRACE_EVENT</code> definitions create tracepoints such as <code>mali_job_slots_event</code>.</p>","plain":"Kernel tracing infrastructure; `TRACE_EVENT` definitions create tracepoints such as `mali_job_slots_event`."},{"id":"runtime-pm","term":"runtime PM","aka":["pm_runtime"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Linux framework to power devices down while the system is running but the device is idle (<code>pm_runtime_get/put</code>). kbase supports it when <code>KBASE_PM_RUNTIME</code> is defined.</p>","plain":"Linux framework to power devices down while the system is running but the device is idle (`pm_runtime_get/put`). kbase supports it when `KBASE_PM_RUNTIME` is defined."},{"id":"regulator","term":"regulator","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Kernel abstraction for a power supply whose voltage can be switched/changed. Found via DT <code>*-supply</code> properties.</p>","plain":"Kernel abstraction for a power supply whose voltage can be switched/changed. Found via DT `*-supply` properties."},{"id":"clk","term":"clock (clk)","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Kernel clock framework object (<code>struct clk</code>), used to turn the GPU clock on/off and set its rate.</p>","plain":"Kernel clock framework object (`struct clk`), used to turn the GPU clock on/off and set its rate."},{"id":"dma-buf","term":"dma-buf","aka":["dmabuf","UMM"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Linux mechanism for sharing buffers between devices (camera, display, GPU) by file descriptor. kbase imports them as <code>KBASE_MEM_TYPE_IMPORTED_UMM</code>.</p>","plain":"Linux mechanism for sharing buffers between devices (camera, display, GPU) by file descriptor. kbase imports them as `KBASE_MEM_TYPE_IMPORTED_UMM`."},{"id":"fence","term":"dma-fence / sync_file","aka":["sync_file","dma_fence"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>A one-shot completion signal for cross-device synchronisation; exported to userspace as a <code>sync_file</code> fd. Used by JM soft jobs and CSF KCPU commands.</p>","plain":"A one-shot completion signal for cross-device synchronisation; exported to userspace as a `sync_file` fd. Used by JM soft jobs and CSF KCPU commands."},{"id":"rbtree","term":"red-black tree","aka":["rb_tree","rb_root"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Balanced binary search tree (<code>struct rb_root</code>); kbase keeps memory regions sorted by GPU address in one per zone.</p>","plain":"Balanced binary search tree (`struct rb_root`); kbase keeps memory regions sorted by GPU address in one per zone."},{"id":"shrinker","term":"shrinker","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Callback the kernel invokes under memory pressure to reclaim memory. kbase registers shrinkers for evictable memory, pools and tiler heaps.</p>","plain":"Callback the kernel invokes under memory pressure to reclaim memory. kbase registers shrinkers for evictable memory, pools and tiler heaps."},{"id":"hrtimer","term":"hrtimer","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>High-resolution kernel timer. Used for JM scheduling ticks, reset delay and the CSF tick timer.</p>","plain":"High-resolution kernel timer. Used for JM scheduling ticks, reset delay and the CSF tick timer."},{"id":"devfreq","term":"devfreq","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Linux framework for device DVFS: a governor periodically reads utilisation (<code>get_dev_status</code>) and picks a frequency (<code>target</code>). See <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/dvfs\">DVFS, devfreq &amp; thermal (IPA)</a>.</p>","plain":"Linux framework for device DVFS: a governor periodically reads utilisation (`get_dev_status`) and picks a frequency (`target`). See dvfs."},{"id":"opp","term":"OPP","aka":["operating point"],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Operating Performance Point: a (frequency, voltage) pair from DT <code>operating-points-v2</code>.</p>","plain":"Operating Performance Point: a (frequency, voltage) pair from DT `operating-points-v2`."},{"id":"request-firmware","term":"request_firmware","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Loads a firmware file from <code>/lib/firmware</code>; used for <code>mali_csffw.bin</code>.</p>","plain":"Loads a firmware file from `/lib/firmware`; used for `mali_csffw.bin`."},{"id":"gki","term":"GKI","aka":[],"cat":"kernel","def":"<p>Android Generic Kernel Image; vendor drivers are modules with restrictions — the reason CSF firmware loading was moved from probe to first open.</p>","plain":"Android Generic Kernel Image; vendor drivers are modules with restrictions — the reason CSF firmware loading was moved from probe to first open."},{"id":"gpu-va","term":"GPU virtual address","aka":["GPU VA"],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>Address as seen by GPU jobs. Translated by the GPU MMU using the context's page table.</p>","plain":"Address as seen by GPU jobs. Translated by the GPU MMU using the context's page table."},{"id":"page-table","term":"page table","aka":["PGD","page directory"],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>Tree of tables translating virtual to physical addresses. kbase's GPU tables have 4 levels with 512 entries each.</p>","plain":"Tree of tables translating virtual to physical addresses. kbase's GPU tables have 4 levels with 512 entries each."},{"id":"pte","term":"PTE / ATE","aka":["ATE"],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>Page table entry. kbase calls a leaf entry that maps a page an ATE (address translation entry).</p>","plain":"Page table entry. kbase calls a leaf entry that maps a page an ATE (address translation entry)."},{"id":"tlb","term":"TLB","aka":[],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>Translation lookaside buffer: cache of address translations. Must be invalidated after changing page tables (the MMU flush/UNLOCK commands).</p>","plain":"Translation lookaside buffer: cache of address translations. Must be invalidated after changing page tables (the MMU flush/UNLOCK commands)."},{"id":"as","term":"address space (AS)","aka":["AS","address space"],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>A hardware slot in the GPU MMU holding one page table root (TRANSTAB). Few exist (e.g. 8–16); contexts are multiplexed onto them by <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/ctxsched\">Address-space scheduling</a>.</p>","plain":"A hardware slot in the GPU MMU holding one page table root (TRANSTAB). Few exist (e.g. 8–16); contexts are multiplexed onto them by ctxsched."},{"id":"l2","term":"L2 cache","aka":["L2"],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>The GPU's shared cache. It must be powered before shader cores; its state machine is <a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/360\"><code>kbase_pm_l2_update_state()</code></a> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c@1433\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:1433\">backend/gpu/mali_kbase_pm_driver.c:1433</a>)</span>.</p>","plain":"The GPU's shared cache. It must be powered before shader cores; its state machine is kbase_pm_l2_update_state."},{"id":"shader-core","term":"shader core","aka":["shader cores"],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>GPU compute unit executing shaders. Powered on/off as a bitmask (<code>SHADER_PWRON</code>). <code>core_mask</code> (sysfs) restricts which are used.</p>","plain":"GPU compute unit executing shaders. Powered on/off as a bitmask (`SHADER_PWRON`). `core_mask` (sysfs) restricts which are used."},{"id":"tiler","term":"tiler","aka":[],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>Fixed-function unit that bins geometry into screen tiles. On CSF it writes into a growable <em>tiler heap</em>.</p>","plain":"Fixed-function unit that bins geometry into screen tiles. On CSF it writes into a growable *tiler heap*."},{"id":"job-chain","term":"job chain","aka":[],"cat":"jm","def":"<p>On JM GPUs a linked list of job descriptors in GPU memory; the kernel only writes its address (<code>jc</code>) to <code>JS_HEAD_NEXT</code>.</p>","plain":"On JM GPUs a linked list of job descriptors in GPU memory; the kernel only writes its address (`jc`) to `JS_HEAD_NEXT`."},{"id":"coherency","term":"coherency","aka":[],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>Whether CPU and GPU caches see each other's writes automatically (ACE/ACE-Lite) or need explicit cache maintenance (<code>kbase_sync_*</code>).</p>","plain":"Whether CPU and GPU caches see each other's writes automatically (ACE/ACE-Lite) or need explicit cache maintenance (`kbase_sync_*`)."},{"id":"hwcnt","term":"hardware counters","aka":["performance counters","HWC"],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>Performance counters inside the GPU (cycles, instructions, cache hits…), exposed through <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwcnt\">Hardware performance counters</a>.</p>","plain":"Performance counters inside the GPU (cycles, instructions, cache hits…), exposed through hwcnt."},{"id":"dvfs","term":"DVFS","aka":[],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>Dynamic Voltage and Frequency Scaling: lower clocks when lightly loaded to save power.</p>","plain":"Dynamic Voltage and Frequency Scaling: lower clocks when lightly loaded to save power."},{"id":"protected-mode","term":"protected mode","aka":["protm","protected memory"],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>A GPU mode for processing protected (DRM/secure) content; normal-world software cannot read protected memory.</p>","plain":"A GPU mode for processing protected (DRM/secure) content; normal-world software cannot read protected memory."},{"id":"soft-reset","term":"soft reset","aka":[],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p><code>GPU_COMMAND = SOFT_RESET</code>: resets GPU internals without power cycling; used for recovery (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/reset\">GPU reset &amp; fault recovery</a>).</p>","plain":"`GPU_COMMAND = SOFT_RESET`: resets GPU internals without power cycling; used for recovery (reset)."},{"id":"doorbell","term":"doorbell","aka":[],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>A register page; writing to it notifies the firmware that new work or requests exist. User queues get their own doorbell page mapped into the process.</p>","plain":"A register page; writing to it notifies the firmware that new work or requests exist. User queues get their own doorbell page mapped into the process."},{"id":"kbdev","term":"kbase_device (kbdev)","aka":["kbdev"],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>The per-GPU driver object <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/266\"><code>kbase_device</code></a>; almost every function takes it.</p>","plain":"The per-GPU driver object kbase_device; almost every function takes it."},{"id":"context","term":"context (kctx)","aka":["kctx","kbase_context"],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>Per-client GPU state <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/272\"><code>kbase_context</code></a>, one per opened file after SET_FLAGS: page table, memory regions, queues/atoms.</p>","plain":"Per-client GPU state kbase_context, one per opened file after SET_FLAGS: page table, memory regions, queues/atoms."},{"id":"kfile","term":"kbase_file","aka":["kfile"],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>Per-open-file object; holds the ABI version and, after setup, the context.</p>","plain":"Per-open-file object; holds the ABI version and, after setup, the context."},{"id":"uk-version","term":"UK version","aka":["API version"],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>The \"user-kernel\" ABI version negotiated by <code>VERSION_CHECK</code>: 11.46 (JM) / 1.30 (CSF) in this release.</p>","plain":"The \"user-kernel\" ABI version negotiated by `VERSION_CHECK`: 11.46 (JM) / 1.30 (CSF) in this release."},{"id":"hwaccess-lock","term":"hwaccess_lock","aka":["hwaccess_lock"],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>The device-wide IRQ-safe spinlock protecting hardware-facing state. The most-asserted lock in the driver.</p>","plain":"The device-wide IRQ-safe spinlock protecting hardware-facing state. The most-asserted lock in the driver."},{"id":"jm","term":"JM (Job Manager)","aka":["Job Manager"],"cat":"jm","def":"<p>The older Mali job submission model: the CPU writes job chains to hardware job slots. Built when <code>CONFIG_MALI_CSF_SUPPORT</code> is not set (<code>MALI_USE_CSF=0</code>).</p>","plain":"The older Mali job submission model: the CPU writes job chains to hardware job slots. Built when `CONFIG_MALI_CSF_SUPPORT` is not set (`MALI_USE_CSF=0`)."},{"id":"csf","term":"CSF (Command Stream Frontend)","aka":["Command Stream Frontend","MALI_USE_CSF"],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>The newer submission model: firmware on an MCU schedules userspace command queues. Built with <code>CONFIG_MALI_CSF_SUPPORT=y</code> (<code>MALI_USE_CSF=1</code>).</p>","plain":"The newer submission model: firmware on an MCU schedules userspace command queues. Built with `CONFIG_MALI_CSF_SUPPORT=y` (`MALI_USE_CSF=1`)."},{"id":"gpuprops","term":"GPU properties","aka":["gpu_props"],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>Values read from GPU ID/feature registers (core count, L2 size, MMU VA bits…), exposed to userspace by <code>GET_GPUPROPS</code>.</p>","plain":"Values read from GPU ID/feature registers (core count, L2 size, MMU VA bits…), exposed to userspace by `GET_GPUPROPS`."},{"id":"hw-issue","term":"HW issue / workaround","aka":["BASE_HW_ISSUE"],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>Known hardware errata (<code>BASE_HW_ISSUE_*</code> in <a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_base_hwconfig_issues.h\"><code>mali_base_hwconfig_issues.h</code></a>); <code>kbase_hw_has_issue()</code> gates workarounds.</p>","plain":"Known hardware errata (`BASE_HW_ISSUE_*` in mali_base_hwconfig_issues.h); `kbase_hw_has_issue()` gates workarounds."},{"id":"ktrace","term":"KTrace","aka":["KBASE_KTRACE_ADD"],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>kbase's own lightweight trace ring buffer of driver events (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/trace\">Tracing, debugfs &amp; debug aids</a>).</p>","plain":"kbase's own lightweight trace ring buffer of driver events (trace)."},{"id":"timeline","term":"timeline stream (TL/MIPE)","aka":["tlstream","MIPE"],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>Binary trace stream of GPU/driver events consumed by Arm profiling tools; acquired via <code>TLSTREAM_ACQUIRE</code>.</p>","plain":"Binary trace stream of GPU/driver events consumed by Arm profiling tools; acquired via `TLSTREAM_ACQUIRE`."},{"id":"mgm","term":"memory group manager (MGM)","aka":["memory group","MGM"],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>Pluggable allocator (separate module) through which kbase allocates physical pages per <em>memory group</em>; lets SoCs route GPU memory to special carve-outs or set PBHA bits.</p>","plain":"Pluggable allocator (separate module) through which kbase allocates physical pages per *memory group*; lets SoCs route GPU memory to special carve-outs or set PBHA bits."},{"id":"pcm","term":"priority control manager","aka":[],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>Optional platform module that limits the scheduling priority a process may request.</p>","plain":"Optional platform module that limits the scheduling priority a process may request."},{"id":"pbha","term":"PBHA","aka":[],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>Page-Based Hardware Attributes: extra bits in PTEs the SoC interconnect can use (e.g. for cache policy); configured from DT.</p>","plain":"Page-Based Hardware Attributes: extra bits in PTEs the SoC interconnect can use (e.g. for cache policy); configured from DT."},{"id":"arbiter","term":"arbiter","aka":[],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>External component that time-shares one GPU between virtual machines (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/arbiter\">Arbiter, virtualization &amp; protected mode</a>).</p>","plain":"External component that time-shares one GPU between virtual machines (arbiter)."},{"id":"kutf","term":"KUTF","aka":[],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p>Kernel Unit Test Framework shipped with the driver (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/tests\">KUTF kernel tests</a>).</p>","plain":"Kernel Unit Test Framework shipped with the driver (tests)."},{"id":"no-mali","term":"NO_MALI","aka":[],"cat":"kbase","def":"<p><code>CONFIG_MALI_NO_MALI</code>: build against a software GPU model instead of real hardware.</p>","plain":"`CONFIG_MALI_NO_MALI`: build against a software GPU model instead of real hardware."},{"id":"region","term":"region (kbase_va_region)","aka":["kbase_va_region","VA region"],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>A contiguous GPU VA range with flags; links to its physical backing (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/319\"><code>kbase_va_region</code></a>).</p>","plain":"A contiguous GPU VA range with flags; links to its physical backing (kbase_va_region)."},{"id":"phy-alloc","term":"physical allocation","aka":["kbase_mem_phy_alloc"],"cat":"mem","def":"<p><a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/315\"><code>kbase_mem_phy_alloc</code></a>: refcounted array of physical pages backing one or more regions.</p>","plain":"kbase_mem_phy_alloc: refcounted array of physical pages backing one or more regions."},{"id":"zone","term":"memory zone","aka":["SAME_VA_ZONE","CUSTOM_VA"],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>A sub-range of a context's GPU VA space with its own rbtree: SAME_VA, CUSTOM_VA, EXEC_VA, and on CSF FIXED_VA, EXEC_FIXED_VA; MCU_SHARED is per-device.</p>","plain":"A sub-range of a context's GPU VA space with its own rbtree: SAME_VA, CUSTOM_VA, EXEC_VA, and on CSF FIXED_VA, EXEC_FIXED_VA; MCU_SHARED is per-device."},{"id":"same-va","term":"SAME_VA","aka":["BASE_MEM_SAME_VA"],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>Allocation whose GPU address equals its CPU address in the process; created at <code>mmap()</code> time.</p>","plain":"Allocation whose GPU address equals its CPU address in the process; created at `mmap()` time."},{"id":"cookie","term":"cookie (mmap handle)","aka":["cookies"],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>A small token returned by MEM_ALLOC (or CS_QUEUE_BIND) that userspace passes as the <code>mmap</code> offset to complete the mapping.</p>","plain":"A small token returned by MEM_ALLOC (or CS_QUEUE_BIND) that userspace passes as the `mmap` offset to complete the mapping."},{"id":"commit","term":"commit pages","aka":[],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>Number of physically backed pages of a region (≤ <code>va_pages</code>); can change with MEM_COMMIT or GPU page faults (growable).</p>","plain":"Number of physically backed pages of a region (≤ `va_pages`); can change with MEM_COMMIT or GPU page faults (growable)."},{"id":"growable","term":"growable region","aka":["BASE_MEM_GROW_ON_GPF","KBASE_REG_GROWABLE"],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>Region with <code>BASE_MEM_GROW_ON_GPF</code>: GPU page faults inside it allocate more pages (<code>extension</code> at a time) instead of killing the context.</p>","plain":"Region with `BASE_MEM_GROW_ON_GPF`: GPU page faults inside it allocate more pages (`extension` at a time) instead of killing the context."},{"id":"mem-pool","term":"memory pool","aka":["kbase_mem_pool"],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>Cache of free, zeroed pages; context pools fall back to device pools, which fall back to the kernel. Small (4 KB) and large (2 MB) variants.</p>","plain":"Cache of free, zeroed pages; context pools fall back to device pools, which fall back to the kernel. Small (4 KB) and large (2 MB) variants."},{"id":"large-page","term":"2 MB large page","aka":[],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>GPU mapping at level 2 of the page table covering 2 MB with one entry; reduces TLB pressure. Controlled by <code>LARGE_PAGE_SUPPORT</code> and the <code>large_page_conf</code> module param.</p>","plain":"GPU mapping at level 2 of the page table covering 2 MB with one entry; reduces TLB pressure. Controlled by `LARGE_PAGE_SUPPORT` and the `large_page_conf` module param."},{"id":"tagged-addr","term":"tagged_addr","aka":[],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>A physical address with flags in the low bits marking parts of large pages.</p>","plain":"A physical address with flags in the low bits marking parts of large pages."},{"id":"jit","term":"JIT memory","aka":[],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>\"Just-in-time\" allocations made by the driver on behalf of GPU work (JM soft jobs / CSF KCPU commands) and reused from a free list.</p>","plain":"\"Just-in-time\" allocations made by the driver on behalf of GPU work (JM soft jobs / CSF KCPU commands) and reused from a free list."},{"id":"evictable","term":"evictable memory","aka":["DONT_NEED"],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>Memory userspace marked <code>BASE_MEM_DONT_NEED</code>; its pages can be reclaimed by a shrinker under memory pressure.</p>","plain":"Memory userspace marked `BASE_MEM_DONT_NEED`; its pages can be reclaimed by a shrinker under memory pressure."},{"id":"alias","term":"alias","aka":[],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>A region composed of slices of other allocations (MEM_ALIAS).</p>","plain":"A region composed of slices of other allocations (MEM_ALIAS)."},{"id":"user-buf","term":"user buffer import","aka":["IMPORTED_USER_BUF"],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>Importing ordinary process memory (<code>KBASE_MEM_TYPE_IMPORTED_USER_BUF</code>): pages are pinned, DMA-mapped and GPU-mapped through a small state machine.</p>","plain":"Importing ordinary process memory (`KBASE_MEM_TYPE_IMPORTED_USER_BUF`): pages are pinned, DMA-mapped and GPU-mapped through a small state machine."},{"id":"sticky","term":"sticky resource","aka":[],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>An external resource (import) kept mapped across jobs until explicitly unmapped (STICKY_RESOURCE_MAP).</p>","plain":"An external resource (import) kept mapped across jobs until explicitly unmapped (STICKY_RESOURCE_MAP)."},{"id":"page-migration","term":"page migration","aka":[],"cat":"mem","def":"<p>Letting the kernel move physical pages used by the GPU (compaction); optional (<code>CONFIG_MALI_PAGE_MIGRATION</code>).</p>","plain":"Letting the kernel move physical pages used by the GPU (compaction); optional (`CONFIG_MALI_PAGE_MIGRATION`)."},{"id":"atom","term":"atom","aka":["katom","kbase_jd_atom"],"cat":"jm","def":"<p>The unit of work submitted on JM GPUs (<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/213\"><code>kbase_jd_atom</code></a>): a job chain address plus requirements, priority and up to two dependencies, identified by an 8-bit number.</p>","plain":"The unit of work submitted on JM GPUs (kbase_jd_atom): a job chain address plus requirements, priority and up to two dependencies, identified by an 8-bit number."},{"id":"jd","term":"JD (job dispatcher)","aka":["job dispatcher"],"cat":"jm","def":"<p>Front half of JM submission: parses atoms, tracks dependencies, completes atoms (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_jd.c\"><code>mali_kbase_jd.c</code></a>).</p>","plain":"Front half of JM submission: parses atoms, tracks dependencies, completes atoms (mali_kbase_jd.c)."},{"id":"js","term":"JS (job scheduler)","aka":["job scheduler"],"cat":"jm","def":"<p>Picks contexts and atoms per job slot by priority (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_js.c\"><code>mali_kbase_js.c</code></a>).</p>","plain":"Picks contexts and atoms per job slot by priority (mali_kbase_js.c)."},{"id":"job-slot","term":"job slot","aka":["JS_HEAD_NEXT"],"cat":"jm","def":"<p>Hardware queue on JM GPUs (typically 0 = fragment, 1 = vertex/compute, 2 = compute) with current and NEXT register sets.</p>","plain":"Hardware queue on JM GPUs (typically 0 = fragment, 1 = vertex/compute, 2 = compute) with current and NEXT register sets."},{"id":"soft-job","term":"soft job","aka":["soft jobs"],"cat":"jm","def":"<p>An atom executed by the kernel on the CPU (<code>BASE_JD_REQ_SOFT_*</code>): fence wait/trigger, event set/wait, JIT alloc/free, external resource map…</p>","plain":"An atom executed by the kernel on the CPU (`BASE_JD_REQ_SOFT_*`): fence wait/trigger, event set/wait, JIT alloc/free, external resource map…"},{"id":"soft-stop","term":"soft-stop / hard-stop","aka":["hard-stop"],"cat":"jm","def":"<p>Stopping a running job: soft-stop lets the GPU stop at a safe point so the job can be resumed later; hard-stop aborts it. Triggered by the JS timer on timeouts.</p>","plain":"Stopping a running job: soft-stop lets the GPU stop at a safe point so the job can be resumed later; hard-stop aborts it. Triggered by the JS timer on timeouts."},{"id":"ringbuffer","term":"slot ringbuffer","aka":[],"cat":"jm","def":"<p>Backend array of up to 2 atoms per job slot (head = running, next = queued in NEXT registers) (<a class=\"fileref\" href=\"#/file/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c\"><code>backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c</code></a>).</p>","plain":"Backend array of up to 2 atoms per job slot (head = running, next = queued in NEXT registers) (backend/gpu/mali_kbase_jm_rb.c)."},{"id":"event","term":"event (JM)","aka":[],"cat":"jm","def":"<p>Completion record <code>base_jd_event_v2</code> that <code>read()</code> returns for each finished atom.</p>","plain":"Completion record `base_jd_event_v2` that `read()` returns for each finished atom."},{"id":"mcu","term":"MCU","aka":["firmware","MCU firmware"],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>The microcontroller inside CSF GPUs that runs the Arm firmware (<code>mali_csffw.bin</code>). It has its own GPU address space (<code>MCU_AS_NR</code>).</p>","plain":"The microcontroller inside CSF GPUs that runs the Arm firmware (`mali_csffw.bin`). It has its own GPU address space (`MCU_AS_NR`)."},{"id":"cs","term":"command stream (CS)","aka":["command stream","CS"],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>One GPU command queue as seen by the firmware: a ring buffer of instructions plus input/output pages.</p>","plain":"One GPU command queue as seen by the firmware: a ring buffer of instructions plus input/output pages."},{"id":"csg","term":"CSG (command stream group)","aka":["queue group","CSG slot"],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>A group of up to N command streams scheduled together on one firmware CSG slot; the kernel object is <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/64\"><code>kbase_queue_group</code></a>.</p>","plain":"A group of up to N command streams scheduled together on one firmware CSG slot; the kernel object is kbase_queue_group."},{"id":"csi","term":"CSI","aka":[],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>Command stream interface: the index of a CS within its group.</p>","plain":"Command stream interface: the index of a CS within its group."},{"id":"req-ack","term":"REQ/ACK protocol","aka":["CSG_REQ","GLB_REQ","CS_REQ"],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>Firmware handshake: the driver toggles bits in <code>*_REQ</code> (input page) and the firmware mirrors them in <code>*_ACK</code> (output page) when done; <code>(REQ ^ ACK) &amp; mask</code> ≠ 0 means pending.</p>","plain":"Firmware handshake: the driver toggles bits in `*_REQ` (input page) and the firmware mirrors them in `*_ACK` (output page) when done; `(REQ ^ ACK) & mask` ≠ 0 means pending."},{"id":"glb-iface","term":"global interface","aka":["GLB"],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>Firmware interface for device-wide requests (<code>GLB_*</code>): idle timer, protected mode, perf counters, halt, ping.</p>","plain":"Firmware interface for device-wide requests (`GLB_*`): idle timer, protected mode, perf counters, halt, ping."},{"id":"user-io","term":"user I/O pages","aka":[],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>Two pages per queue mapped into the process: the input page (<code>CS_INSERT</code>, written by userspace) and output page (<code>CS_EXTRACT</code>, <code>CS_ACTIVE</code>, written by firmware).</p>","plain":"Two pages per queue mapped into the process: the input page (`CS_INSERT`, written by userspace) and output page (`CS_EXTRACT`, `CS_ACTIVE`, written by firmware)."},{"id":"tick","term":"tick / tock","aka":["tock"],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>CSF scheduling passes: a <em>tick</em> is periodic (rotates groups for fairness); a <em>tock</em> is an out-of-cycle pass triggered by events (e.g. a group became idle).</p>","plain":"CSF scheduling passes: a *tick* is periodic (rotates groups for fairness); a *tock* is an out-of-cycle pass triggered by events (e.g. a group became idle)."},{"id":"kcpu","term":"KCPU queue","aka":["KCPU"],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>A command queue executed by the kernel on the CPU (fences, CQS, JIT, imports) (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/kcpu\">KCPU queues, sync objects &amp; tiler heap</a>).</p>","plain":"A command queue executed by the kernel on the CPU (fences, CQS, JIT, imports) (kcpu)."},{"id":"cqs","term":"CQS","aka":[],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>Cross-queue sync object: a value in GPU memory that queues wait on or set.</p>","plain":"Cross-queue sync object: a value in GPU memory that queues wait on or set."},{"id":"tiler-heap","term":"tiler heap","aka":[],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>Growable chunked memory for the tiler's intermediate data; grown by the driver on tiler OOM events.</p>","plain":"Growable chunked memory for the tiler's intermediate data; grown by the driver on tiler OOM events."},{"id":"suspend-buf","term":"suspend buffer","aka":[],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>GPU memory where the firmware saves a group's state when it is taken off a slot.</p>","plain":"GPU memory where the firmware saves a group's state when it is taken off a slot."},{"id":"ipa-control","term":"IPA control","aka":[],"cat":"csf","def":"<p>CSF component that shares firmware performance counters between IPA power models and others.</p>","plain":"CSF component that shares firmware performance counters between IPA power models and others."},{"id":"ipa","term":"IPA","aka":[],"cat":"gpu","def":"<p>Intelligent Power Allocation: the thermal governor's power model for the GPU (<a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/dvfs\">DVFS, devfreq &amp; thermal (IPA)</a>).</p>","plain":"Intelligent Power Allocation: the thermal governor's power model for the GPU (dvfs)."}],"pages":{"overview":"<h3>What this driver is</h3>\n<p>This is <strong><code>mali_kbase</code></strong>, Arm's Linux <strong>kernel-mode driver (KMD)</strong> for Mali GPUs, release <strong>r56p0-19eac0</strong> (<span class=\"inref\">Kbuild</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild@81\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild:81\">Kbuild:81</a>)</span>). It matches device-tree nodes compatible with <code>arm,malit6xx</code>, <code>arm,mali-midgard</code>, <code>arm,mali-bifrost</code> and <code>arm,mali-valhall</code> (<span class=\"inref\">kbase_dt_ids</span> <span class=\"cites\">(<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#/code/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c@6216\" title=\"drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6216\">mali_kbase_core_linux.c:6216</a>)</span>).</p>\n<p>A GPU driver stack has two halves:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>User-mode driver (UMD)</strong>: the big library linked into apps (OpenGL ES / Vulkan / OpenCL). It compiles shaders, builds GPU command buffers and job descriptors, and decides <em>what</em> the GPU should do. It is <strong>not</strong> in this archive.</li><li><strong>Kernel-mode driver (KMD)</strong>: this code. It owns everything that must be shared or protected between processes:<ul><li>powering the GPU and managing its clocks</li><li>giving each process an isolated GPU address space (page tables)</li><li>allocating and mapping memory</li><li>feeding work to the hardware or firmware fairly</li><li>handling interrupts, faults and resets</li><li>exposing counters and traces</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p>The UMD talks to the KMD through <code>/dev/mali0</code> with <code>ioctl</code>, <code>mmap</code>, <code>read</code> and <code>poll</code>.</p>\n<h3>Two back-ends in one tree</h3>\n<p><code>CONFIG_MALI_CSF_SUPPORT</code> selects one of two ways of submitting work:</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th><strong>JM (Job Manager)</strong></th><th><strong>CSF (Command Stream Frontend)</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GPUs</td><td>Midgard, Bifrost, early Valhall</td><td>later Valhall and newer</td></tr><tr><td>Unit of work</td><td><em>atom</em> → job chain in hardware job slots</td><td>userspace <em>command queues</em> in <em>queue groups</em></td></tr><tr><td>Who schedules on the GPU</td><td>the kernel driver (JS)</td><td>firmware on the GPU's MCU; the kernel schedules groups onto firmware slots</td></tr><tr><td>Submit path</td><td><code>KBASE_IOCTL_JOB_SUBMIT</code> every time</td><td>userspace writes ring buffer + doorbell; kernel involved for (re)scheduling</td></tr><tr><td>Completion</td><td>IRQ → kernel → <code>read()</code> events</td><td>sync objects in memory; IRQ only wakes <code>poll()</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>The archive itself does not say which back-end your product uses. Every page here marks content as &lt;span class=\"tag t-JM\"&gt;JM&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=\"tag t-CSF\"&gt;CSF&lt;/span&gt; or common. The header toggle filters it.</p>\n<h3>Where it sits</h3>","howto":"<h3>How to read this site</h3>\n<ul><li>**Start with the <a href=\"#/arch\">architecture diagram</a>** (Overview, below). Click a box to open that subsystem.</li><li><strong>Subsystem pages</strong> explain the purpose and give the key structs and functions. They also list the locks the code asserts or takes (generated from <code>lockdep_assert_held</code> and lock calls), how the subsystem talks to the others, and debugging tips. A short quiz ends each page.</li><li><strong>Flows</strong> are step-by-step sequence diagrams of the real call paths. Use ← / → (or the buttons) to step. Each step shows the function, <code>file:line</code>, a code excerpt, and a <strong>Data</strong> box saying what data is created or moved at that point.</li><li><strong>Data flow</strong> follows each important piece of data, such as a buffer, an atom, a command or an interrupt, through every layer from userspace to hardware and back.</li><li><strong>Code viewer:</strong> every <code>file:line</code> link opens it. Function names in the code are links. Click one to jump to its definition; the side panel lists callers and callees. Struct names link to the struct explorer.</li><li><strong>Search</strong> (press <code>/</code>) covers functions, structs, files, macros, ioctls, Kconfig options, sysfs/debugfs entries and glossary terms.</li><li><strong>Dotted-underlined words</strong> are glossary terms. Hover for a definition, click for the full entry.</li><li><strong>JM / CSF tags:</strong> many functions exist twice, once per back-end, with the same name. Search results and function pages list every definition with its tag.</li></ul>\n<h3>How the content was produced</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Generated by <code>tools/build_index.py</code> and <code>tools/build_site.py</code> from <code>kmd_src/</code>:</strong><ul><li>the file list and the Kbuild condition under which each <code>.c</code> is compiled</li><li>every function and struct with its kernel-doc text</li><li>the call graph and the lock usage</li><li>ioctls and their handlers</li><li>Kconfig options, sysfs/debugfs entries, module parameters, tracepoints, workqueues and registers</li></ul></li><li><strong>Hand-written explanations</strong> live in <code>tools/content/</code>. They refer to code by <em>symbol name and anchor pattern</em>, never by a typed line number, so every line number on the site is computed. A reference that no longer matches the source makes the build fail.</li><li><strong>Limits of the call graph:</strong> calls through function pointers (ops tables such as <code>mmu_mode-&gt;update</code> or <code>policy-&gt;get_core_active</code>) are not resolved automatically. Functions placed in tables are listed as \"referenced by\" the table instead. Macros that expand to calls are not followed.</li><li><strong>Doc text:</strong> where the code has no kernel-doc comment, the site shows none rather than guessing.</li></ul>"},"arch":{"w":1000,"h":760,"layers":[{"y":10,"h":80,"label":"Userspace"},{"y":100,"h":90,"label":"Kernel ABI"},{"y":200,"h":210,"label":"Core services"},{"y":420,"h":110,"label":"Submission back-end"},{"y":540,"h":90,"label":"HW access & platform"},{"y":640,"h":110,"label":"Hardware"}],"boxes":[{"id":"umd","x":120,"y":25,"w":360,"h":50,"label":"UMD: GLES / Vulkan / OpenCL library","note":"not in archive"},{"id":"tools","x":520,"y":25,"w":220,"h":50,"label":"Profilers / tools","note":"hwcnt, timeline"},{"id":"osk","x":780,"y":25,"w":200,"h":50,"label":"Linux PM / devfreq / thermal"},{"id":"uapi","x":120,"y":115,"w":620,"h":60,"label":"/dev/maliN: open · ioctl · mmap · read/poll · sysfs · debugfs","sub":"uapi"},{"id":"init","x":780,"y":115,"w":200,"h":60,"label":"Module init / probe","sub":"init"},{"id":"context","x":120,"y":215,"w":150,"h":55,"label":"Contexts","sub":"context"},{"id":"mem","x":290,"y":215,"w":190,"h":55,"label":"Memory mgmt","sub":"mem"},{"id":"mmu","x":500,"y":215,"w":120,"h":55,"label":"GPU MMU","sub":"mmu"},{"id":"ctxsched","x":640,"y":215,"w":120,"h":55,"label":"AS scheduling","sub":"ctxsched"},{"id":"pm","x":780,"y":215,"w":200,"h":55,"label":"Power management","sub":"pm"},{"id":"hwcnt","x":120,"y":285,"w":190,"h":55,"label":"HW counters","sub":"hwcnt"},{"id":"trace","x":330,"y":285,"w":190,"h":55,"label":"Tracing / debugfs","sub":"trace"},{"id":"reset","x":540,"y":285,"w":220,"h":55,"label":"Reset & recovery","sub":"reset"},{"id":"dvfs","x":780,"y":285,"w":200,"h":55,"label":"DVFS / IPA","sub":"dvfs"},{"id":"arbiter","x":120,"y":350,"w":300,"h":50,"label":"Arbiter / protected mode","sub":"arbiter"},{"id":"build","x":440,"y":350,"w":200,"h":50,"label":"Build & config","sub":"build"},{"id":"tests","x":660,"y":350,"w":100,"h":50,"label":"KUTF","sub":"tests"},{"id":"jm","x":120,"y":435,"w":300,"h":80,"label":"JM: JD → JS → job slots","sub":"jm","tag":"JM"},{"id":"csf","x":440,"y":435,"w":200,"h":80,"label":"CSF queues, groups, scheduler","sub":"csf","tag":"CSF"},{"id":"kcpu","x":660,"y":435,"w":140,"h":80,"label":"KCPU, sync, tiler heap","sub":"kcpu","tag":"CSF"},{"id":"csffw","x":820,"y":435,"w":160,"h":80,"label":"Firmware loader & iface","sub":"csffw","tag":"CSF"},{"id":"hwaccess","x":120,"y":555,"w":420,"h":60,"label":"Register access · IRQ handlers · GPU props","sub":"hwaccess"},{"id":"platform","x":560,"y":555,"w":420,"h":60,"label":"Platform: DT, clocks, regulators, MGM","sub":"platform"},{"id":"gpu_js","x":120,"y":660,"w":200,"h":75,"label":"Job slots (JM)","tag":"JM","sub":"jm"},{"id":"gpu_mcu","x":340,"y":660,"w":200,"h":75,"label":"MCU + firmware (CSF)","tag":"CSF","sub":"csffw"},{"id":"gpu_mmu","x":560,"y":660,"w":170,"h":75,"label":"GPU MMU / AS slots","sub":"mmu"},{"id":"gpu_cores","x":750,"y":660,"w":230,"h":75,"label":"L2 + shader cores, power regs","sub":"pm"}],"arrows":[["umd","uapi"],["tools","uapi"],["osk","init"],["uapi","context"],["uapi","mem"],["uapi","jm"],["uapi","csf"],["mem","mmu"],["ctxsched","mmu"],["jm","ctxsched"],["csf","ctxsched"],["csf","csffw"],["kcpu","csf"],["jm","hwaccess"],["csffw","hwaccess"],["pm","platform"],["dvfs","platform"],["hwaccess","gpu_js"],["hwaccess","gpu_mcu"],["hwaccess","gpu_mmu"],["pm","gpu_cores"],["reset","pm"]]},"dataflow":[{"id":"buffer","title":"A GPU buffer: from MEM_ALLOC to GPU memory accesses","summary":"<p>Follow one allocation through every representation it takes. See also <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/memalloc\">GPU memory allocation and mapping into the GPU address space</a>.</p>","stages":[{"layer":"Userspace","what":"<p><code>va_pages</code>, <code>commit_pages</code>, <code>extension</code>, <code>flags</code> (e.g. <code>BASE_MEM_PROT_GPU_RD|WR</code>, <code>BASE_MEM_SAME_VA</code>).</p>","form":"<code>union kbase_ioctl_mem_alloc</code>"},{"layer":"ioctl layer","what":"<p>Copied in by <code>KBASE_HANDLE_IOCTL_INOUT</code>; SAME_VA forced for 64-bit.</p>","form":"<a class=\"fnref\" href=\"#/fn/1946\"><code>kbase_api_mem_alloc()</code></a>"},{"layer":"Memory mgmt","what":"<p>Virtual range object: <code>start_pfn</code>, <code>nr_pages</code>, <code>flags</code> (<code>KBASE_REG_*</code>), zone bits.</p>","form":"<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/319\"><code>kbase_va_region</code></a>"},{"layer":"Memory mgmt","what":"<p><code>pages[]</code> of <code>tagged_addr</code>, <code>nents</code> = committed pages, <code>type = NATIVE</code>, <code>group_id</code>.</p>","form":"<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/315\"><code>kbase_mem_phy_alloc</code></a>"},{"layer":"Page pools","what":"<p>Pages taken from per-context pool → device pool → kernel (<code>mgm_alloc_page</code>), zeroed, DMA-mapped.</p>","form":"<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/256\"><code>kbase_mem_pool</code></a>"},{"layer":"Userspace (again)","what":"<p>SAME_VA: <code>gpu_va</code> = cookie; process calls <code>mmap(fd, cookie)</code>; kernel picks CPU VA = GPU VA.</p>","form":"cookie"},{"layer":"GPU MMU","what":"<p><code>kbase_mmu_insert_pages</code> writes leaf entries (physical address + attributes) in a 4-level table rooted at <code>kctx-&gt;mmu.pgd</code>.</p>","form":"page-table pages + ATEs"},{"layer":"Hardware","what":"<p>When the context is scheduled, <code>TRANSTAB</code> = pgd, <code>MEMATTR</code>, <code>TRANSCFG</code> are written to its AS; TLB flushes after changes.</p>","form":"AS registers"},{"layer":"GPU","what":"<p>Shaders/firmware use the GPU VA; the MMU translates; a miss in a growable region becomes a page fault → <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/fault\">GPU page fault handling (grow or kill)</a>.</p>","form":"memory access"}]},{"id":"atom","title":"A JM atom: from userspace struct to job slot and back","summary":"<p>See also <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/submit_jm\">Submitting work and completion: Job Manager GPUs</a>.</p>","stages":[{"layer":"Userspace","what":"<p><code>jc</code> (GPU VA of job chain), <code>core_req</code>, <code>atom_number</code>, <code>pre_dep[2]</code>, <code>prio</code>, external resources.</p>","form":"<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/448\"><code>base_jd_atom</code></a>"},{"layer":"JD","what":"<p>Slot <code>kctx-&gt;jctx.atoms[atom_number]</code>; <code>status = QUEUED</code>, dependency lists, <code>event_code</code>.</p>","form":"<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/213\"><code>kbase_jd_atom</code></a>"},{"layer":"JS","what":"<p><code>status = IN_JS</code>; context put on <code>ctx_list_pullable[slot][prio]</code>.</p>","form":"per-slot priority tree"},{"layer":"Backend","what":"<p><code>gpu_rb_state</code> walks NOT_IN_SLOT_RB → … → READY → SUBMITTED.</p>","form":"slot ringbuffer entry"},{"layer":"Registers","what":"<p><code>jc</code>, cache-flush config, <code>START</code>.</p>","form":"<code>JS_HEAD_NEXT</code>, <code>JS_CONFIG_NEXT</code>, <code>JS_COMMAND_NEXT</code>"},{"layer":"Hardware","what":"<p>GPU walks job descriptors in the context's AS.</p>","form":"job chain execution"},{"layer":"IRQ","what":"<p>Done/failed bit per slot, completion code.</p>","form":"<code>JOB_IRQ_STATUS</code> + <code>JS_STATUS</code>"},{"layer":"JD (worker)","what":"<p><code>status = COMPLETED</code>, dependants released.</p>","form":"<code>katom-&gt;event_code</code>"},{"layer":"Userspace","what":"<p><code>event_code</code>, <code>atom_number</code>, <code>udata</code>.</p>","form":"<code>base_jd_event_v2</code> via read()"}]},{"id":"csfcmd","title":"A CSF command: from ring buffer to completion","summary":"<p>See also <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/submit_csf\">Submitting work and completion: CSF GPUs</a>.</p>","stages":[{"layer":"Userspace","what":"<p>UMD writes CS instructions (opaque to the kernel).</p>","form":"ring buffer in GPU memory"},{"layer":"Userspace","what":"<p>Advances <code>CS_INSERT</code>; optionally writes the doorbell page.</p>","form":"user I/O input page"},{"layer":"Kernel (setup)","what":"<p>Queue bound to group/CSI; group runnable.</p>","form":"<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/61\"><code>kbase_queue</code></a> / <a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/64\"><code>kbase_queue_group</code></a>"},{"layer":"CSF scheduler","what":"<p><code>CS_BASE</code>, <code>CS_SIZE</code>, <code>CS_USER_INPUT/OUTPUT</code>, <code>CSG_CONFIG = as_nr</code>, <code>CSG_REQ = START</code>, doorbell.</p>","form":"CSG/CS input pages"},{"layer":"Firmware","what":"<p>Fetches instructions, dispatches compute/tiler/fragment work, updates <code>CS_EXTRACT</code>.</p>","form":"iterators"},{"layer":"Memory","what":"<p>GPU writes a value when work completes.</p>","form":"sync object (CQS)"},{"layer":"IRQ","what":"<p>Firmware interrupt on JOB line → <code>kbase_csf_interrupt</code>.</p>","form":"<code>CSG_ACK.SYNC_UPDATE</code>"},{"layer":"Userspace","what":"<p>UMD rechecks sync objects; KCPU queues waiting on CQS also re-run.</p>","form":"poll() wake-up"}]},{"id":"interrupt","title":"An interrupt: from IRQ line to deferred work","summary":"<p>See also <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/irq\">GPU interrupt handling (top half → bottom half)</a>.</p>","stages":[{"layer":"Hardware","what":"<p>JOB / MMU / GPU (or one combined line).</p>","form":"IRQ line"},{"layer":"Top half","what":"<p>Read under <code>hwaccess_lock</code>; <code>IRQ_NONE</code> if GPU unpowered.</p>","form":"<code>*_IRQ_STATUS</code> register"},{"layer":"Top half","what":"<p>JM: <code>kbase_job_done</code>; CSF: <code>kbase_csf_interrupt</code>; MMU: record fault; GPU: power/cache/reset events.</p>","form":"per-source dispatch"},{"layer":"Bottom half","what":"<p><code>kbase_jd_done_worker</code>, <code>kbase_mmu_page_fault_worker</code>, CSF scheduler kthread, power-off worker.</p>","form":"work item / kthread"},{"layer":"Result","what":"<p>Event posted, pages mapped, group rescheduled, power state advanced.</p>","form":"state change"}]},{"id":"power","title":"A power request: from refcount to power registers","summary":"<p>See also <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/power\">Power up / power down (runtime)</a> and <a class=\"flowref\" href=\"#/flow/suspend\">System suspend and resume</a>.</p>","stages":[{"layer":"Any subsystem","what":"<p><code>pm.active_count++</code>.</p>","form":"<code>kbase_pm_context_active()</code>"},{"layer":"Policy","what":"<p>coarse_demand/always_on decide on/off.</p>","form":"<code>get_core_active()</code>"},{"layer":"Platform","what":"<p>Clocks/regulators on.</p>","form":"<code>power_on_callback</code>"},{"layer":"State machines","what":"<p>Desired vs current; <code>kbase_pm_update_state</code>.</p>","form":"<code>l2_state</code>, <code>shaders_state</code>, <code>mcu_state</code>"},{"layer":"Registers","what":"<p>Core bitmasks.</p>","form":"<code>L2_PWRON</code>, <code>SHADER_PWRON</code> (+ PWROFF)"},{"layer":"IRQ","what":"<p>Advance the state machine to the next state.</p>","form":"<code>POWER_CHANGED_ALL</code>"}]},{"id":"counters","title":"A performance-counter sample","summary":"<p>See <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/hwcnt\">Hardware performance counters</a>.</p>","stages":[{"layer":"Hardware","what":"<p>FE, tiler, memsys (L2), shader cores.</p>","form":"counter blocks"},{"layer":"Backend","what":"<p>JM: <code>PRFCNT_*</code> registers dump to memory; CSF: firmware <code>GLB_PRFCNT_*</code> request writes a ring buffer.</p>","form":"dump buffer"},{"layer":"Accumulator","what":"<p>Accumulates across power cycles / disables.</p>","form":"<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/177\"><code>kbase_hwcnt_context</code></a>"},{"layer":"Virtualizer","what":"<p>Per-client deltas from a shared accumulator.</p>","form":"<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/193\"><code>kbase_hwcnt_virtualizer</code></a>"},{"layer":"kinstr_prfcnt","what":"<p>Userspace <code>GET_SAMPLE</code> / <code>PUT_SAMPLE</code> on its own fd.</p>","form":"sample ring buffer (mmap)"}]},{"id":"firmware","title":"The CSF firmware image","summary":"<p>See <a class=\"subref\" href=\"#/sub/csffw\">CSF firmware &amp; host interface</a>.</p>","stages":[{"layer":"Filesystem","what":"<p>Name from module param <code>fw_name</code> or DT <code>firmware-name</code>.</p>","form":"<code>/lib/firmware/mali_csffw.bin</code>"},{"layer":"Kernel","what":"<p>Retained copy so the image can be reloaded after reset.</p>","form":"<code>kbdev-&gt;csf.fw</code> (vmalloc)"},{"layer":"Kernel","what":"<p>One per section: GPU pages allocated, data copied, mapped into the MCU AS.</p>","form":"<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/86\"><code>kbase_csf_firmware_interface</code></a> list"},{"layer":"MCU","what":"<p>MCU enabled; waits for the boot-complete interrupt.</p>","form":"boot"},{"layer":"Shared memory","what":"<p>Driver parses the interface: number of CSG slots, CS per group, features.</p>","form":"<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/102\"><code>kbase_csf_global_iface</code></a>"}]},{"id":"props","title":"GPU properties","summary":"<p>How userspace learns what GPU it is running on.</p>","stages":[{"layer":"Registers","what":"<p>Read at probe.</p>","form":"<code>GPU_ID</code>, <code>*_FEATURES</code>, <code>*_PRESENT</code>"},{"layer":"Kernel","what":"<p>Decoded: core mask, L2 slices, VA bits, AS count…</p>","form":"<a class=\"stref\" href=\"#/struct/294\"><code>kbase_gpu_props</code></a>"},{"layer":"Kernel","what":"<p>Packed key/value list built once (<code>kbase_gpuprops_populate_user_buffer</code>).</p>","form":"prop buffer"},{"layer":"Userspace","what":"<p>Copied out; key encodes size (u8/u16/u32/u64).</p>","form":"<code>KBASE_IOCTL_GET_GPUPROPS</code>"}]}],"learn":[{"title":"1. The big picture","links":[["","Overview + architecture"],["glossary","Glossary (skim kernel terms)"]],"why":"Know what the KMD owns and the JM vs CSF split before reading code."},{"title":"2. How the driver starts","links":[["sub/init","Init subsystem"],["flow/load","Flow: driver load"],["sub/platform","Platform"]],"why":"Table-driven init is the backbone; every other subsystem plugs in here."},{"title":"3. The userspace contract","links":[["sub/uapi","Userspace interface"],["flow/open","Flow: open + context"],["ioctls","ioctl reference"]],"why":"Everything the driver does is triggered by these entry points."},{"title":"4. Memory (the biggest part)","links":[["sub/context","Contexts"],["sub/mem","Memory"],["sub/mmu","GPU MMU"],["flow/memalloc","Flow: allocation"],["dataflow","Data flow: buffer"]],"why":"Most bugs and most code are here: regions, pages, page tables."},{"title":"5. Work submission (pick your back-end)","links":[["sub/jm","JM"],["flow/submit_jm","Flow: JM submit"],["sub/csf","CSF scheduler"],["sub/csffw","CSF firmware"],["flow/submit_csf","Flow: CSF submit"],["sub/ctxsched","AS scheduling"]],"why":"Read the one your GPU uses first; skim the other."},{"title":"6. Interrupts and power","links":[["sub/hwaccess","Registers & IRQs"],["flow/irq","Flow: interrupts"],["sub/pm","Power"],["flow/power","Flow: power"],["flow/suspend","Flow: suspend/resume"],["sub/dvfs","DVFS"]],"why":"Explains most 'GPU didn't power up / IRQ storm / hang on resume' issues."},{"title":"7. When things go wrong","links":[["flow/fault","Flow: page fault"],["sub/reset","Reset"],["flow/reset","Flow: reset"],["sub/trace","Tracing & debugfs"],["locks","Lock reference"]],"why":"Debugging tools and recovery paths."},{"title":"8. Advanced","links":[["sub/kcpu","KCPU/sync/tiler heap"],["sub/hwcnt","HW counters"],["sub/arbiter","Arbiter/protected"],["config","Kconfig & build"],["registers","Registers"]],"why":"Read when you need them."}]};
